--- An icon editor that permits a user to modify a `SpawnIcon` and re-render it. This is used by the spawn menu and is what is shown when you right-click an icon and select `Edit Icon`.
--- This makes use of the `DAdjustableModelPanel` element.
--- **NOTE**: This panel is only available in Sandbox and Sandbox derived gamemodes!
declare class IconEditor extends DFrame
    --- Applies the top-down view camera settings for the model in the `DAdjustableModelPanel`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `Above` (third) button (See `IconEditor`).
    @side(client)
    function AboveLayout(): nil
    --- Applies the best camera settings for the model in the `DAdjustableModelPanel`, using the values returned by `Global.PositionSpawnIcon`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `wand` button (See the ) and when `IconEditor:Refresh` is called.
    @side(client)
    function BestGuessLayout(): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Fills the `DListView` on the left of the editor with the model entity's animation list. Called by `IconEditor:Refresh`.
    --- @param ent The entity being rendered within the model panel.
    @side(client)
    function FillAnimations(ent: Entity): nil
    --- Applies the front view camera settings for the model in the `DAdjustableModelPanel`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `Front` (second) button (See the ).
    @side(client)
    function FullFrontalLayout(): nil
    --- Places the camera at the origin (0,0,0), relative to the entity, in the `DAdjustableModelPanel`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `Center` (fifth) button (See the ).
    @side(client)
    function OriginLayout(): nil
    --- Updates the internal `DAdjustableModelPanel` and `SpawnIcon`.
    --- This should be called immediately after setting the SpawnIcon with `IconEditor:SetIcon`.
    @side(client)
    override function Refresh(): nil
    --- Re-renders the `SpawnIcon`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `RENDER` button, this retrieves the render data from the internal `DAdjustableModelPanel` and passes it as a table to `Panel:RebuildSpawnIconEx`.
    @side(client)
    function RenderIcon(): nil
    --- Applies the right side view camera settings for the model in the `DAdjustableModelPanel`.
    --- Called when a user clicks the `Right` (fourth) button (See the ). (Note: The icon for this points left.)
    @side(client)
    function RightLayout(): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Sets up the default ambient and directional lighting for the `DAdjustableModelPanel`. Called by `IconEditor:Refresh`.
    @side(client)
    function SetDefaultLighting(): nil
    --- Sets the editor's model and icon from an entity. Alternative to `IconEditor:SetIcon`, with uses a `SpawnIcon`.
    --- You do not need to call `IconEditor:Refresh` after this.
    --- @param ent The entity to retrieve the model and skin from.
    @side(client)
    function SetFromEntity(ent: Entity): nil
    --- Sets the `SpawnIcon` to modify. You should call `Panel:Refresh` immediately after this, as the user will not be able to make changes to the icon beforehand.
    --- @param icon The SpawnIcon object to be modified.
    @side(client)
    override function SetIcon(icon: Panel): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Updates the entity being rendered in the internal `DAdjustableModelPanel`. Called by the model panel's `DModelPanel:LayoutEntity` method.
    --- @param ent The entity being rendered within the model panel.
    @side(client)
    function UpdateEntity(ent: Entity): nil
end

--- A checkbox panel similar to `DCheckBox` and `DImageButton` with customizable checked state image.
--- Uses the `Material` panel internally. Can't have a label.
--- **NOTE**: Will error if no material was set.
declare class ImageCheckBox extends Button
    --- Returns the checked state of the `ImageCheckBox`
    --- @return boolean true for checked, false otherwise
    @side(client)
    function GetChecked(): boolean
    --- Sets the checked state of the checkbox.
    --- Checked state can be obtained by `ImageCheckBox`.State.
    --- @param OnOff true for checked, false otherwise
    @side(client)
    function Set(OnOff: boolean): nil
    --- Sets the checked state of the checkbox.
    --- Checked state can be obtained via `ImageCheckBox:GetChecked`
    --- @param bOn true for checked, false otherwise
    @side(client)
    function SetChecked(bOn: boolean): nil
    --- Sets the material that will be visible when the `ImageCheckBox` is checked.
    --- Internally calls `Material:SetMaterial`.
    --- **NOTE**: Will error if no material was set.
    --- @param mat The file path of the material to set (relative to "garrysmod/materials/").
    @side(client)
    override function SetMaterial(mat: string): nil
end

--- The panel used by Material & Lamp Sandbox tools for texture selection. Despite being only used in Sandbox, it is **not** exclusive to that gamemode.
--- See also `PropSelect` for the prop selecting alternative.
declare class MatSelect extends ContextBase
    --- Adds a new material to the selection list.
    --- @param label Tooltip for the material, for when the player hovers over the material.
    --- @param path Path to the material. Relative to `materials/` folder (do not include it), and do not include the `.vmt` extension.
    @side(client)
    function AddMaterial(label: string, path: string): nil
    --- Adds a new material to the selection list, with some extra options.
    --- @param label Tooltip for the material, for when the player hovers over the material.
    --- @param path Path to the material. Relative to `materials/` folder (do not include it), and do not include the `.vmt` extension.
    --- @param value Overrides the "value" of the material. This will be what MatSelect:OnSelect receives in the first argument. It also affects MatSelect:FindMaterialByValue.
    --- @param convars A list of convar names (as keys) and their values to set when the user selects this material. ContextBase:SetConVar will be ignored.
    @side(client)
    function AddMaterialEx(label: string, path: string, value: any, convars: { [any]: any }): nil
    --- Find a material and selects it, if it exists in this panel.
    --- @param mat The material to find and select within this MatSelect.
    @side(client)
    function FindAndSelectMaterial(mat: string): nil
    --- Find a `DImageButton` panel based on the input material path.
    --- @param mat The material to find within this MatSelect.
    --- @return DImageButton The found material, or nil.
    @side(client)
    function FindMaterialByValue(mat: string): DImageButton
    --- Returns whether the panel would set its own height to fit all materials within its height.
    --- @return boolean `true` = auto size itself.
    @side(client)
    function GetAutoHeight(): boolean
    --- **INTERNAL**: Use `MatSelect:FindAndSelectMaterial` instead.
    --- Selects a given material panel.
    --- @param mat The material to select, found by MatSelect:FindMaterialByValue
    @side(client)
    function SelectMaterial(mat: DImageButton): nil
    --- Sets whether the panel should set its own height to fit all materials within its height.
    --- @param autoSize If `true`, auto size itself.
    @side(client)
    function SetAutoHeight(autoSize: boolean): nil
    --- Sets the height of a single material in pixels.
    --- @param height_ The height of the material, in pixels. Default is `128`.
    @side(client)
    function SetItemHeight(height_: number): nil
    --- Sets the width of a single material in pixels.
    --- @param width The width of the material, in pixels. Default is `128`.
    @side(client)
    function SetItemWidth(width: number): nil
    --- Sets the target height of the panel, in number of rows.
    --- @param rows Amount of rows to target the height to. Default is `2`.
    @side(client)
    function SetNumRows(rows: number): nil
end

--- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
--- Panel used to display models, used by `SpawnIcon`.
declare class ModelImage extends Panel
end

--- A panel list with a custom vertical scroll bar that doesn't have up/down buttons and has a momentum to scrolling.
declare class PanelList extends Panel
end

--- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
--- A preset editor, which can be opened by `ControlPresets`.
--- This control only exists in Sandbox derived gamemodes.
declare class PresetEditor extends DFrame
end

--- Used in Sandbox tools to allow the player to select models out of a list. Despite being only used in Sandbox, it is **not** exclusive to that gamemode.
--- See also `MatSelect` for the material selecting alternative.
declare class PropSelect extends ContextBase
    --- Adds a new model to the selection list.
    --- @param model Model path, **including** `models/` and `.mdl`.
    --- @param convars A list of convar names (as keys) and their values to set when the user selects this model.
    @side(client)
    function AddModel(model: string, convars: { [any]: any }): nil
    --- Adds a new model to the selection list.
    --- @param value The "value" for this model, which is used to set the ContextBase:SetConVar.
    --- @param model Model path, **including** `models/` and `.mdl`.
    --- @param skin The skin number for this model. It will **not** be set to the convar, use the value argument to track skin-model combos.
    @side(client)
    function AddModelEx(value: string, model: string, skin: number): nil
    --- Find and select a `SpawnIcon` panel based on the input model path.
    --- @param mdl The model to find and select within this PropSelect.
    @side(client)
    function FindAndSelectButton(mdl: string): nil
    --- Find a `SpawnIcon` panel based on the input model path.
    --- @param mdl The model to find within this PropSelect.
    --- @return SpawnIcon The found spawnicon, or `nil`.
    @side(client)
    function FindModelByValue(mdl: string): SpawnIcon
end

--- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
--- Currently there are no functions to retrieve checked state of a Radio Button, and their visuals are seemingly broken.
declare class RadioButton extends Panel
end

--- A very versatile text display element that's used to power the default chat and console.
--- Rich Text panels allows multicolored, highlight-able, and interactive text using individual text segment markup (segments are defined by the `Panel:AppendText` method).
--- The **RichText** element has a `64000` character limit.
--- You can hide the RichText scrollbar with the following function: `Panel:SetVerticalScrollbarEnabled`
declare class RichText extends Panel
end

--- Used as scroll bar for `PanelList`
declare class SlideBar extends Panel
end

--- A simple slider featuring an numeric display.
declare class Slider extends Panel
end

--- A "spawn icon" displays an image for the given model path.
--- It is mostly used in the Spawn Menu (Q).
--- It uses `ModelImage` internally.
declare class SpawnIcon extends DButton
    --- Returns the currently active `Sub Model IDs` for each Body Group of the spawn icon.
    --- This is set by `SpawnIcon:SetBodyGroup`.
    --- @return string The Body Groups of the spawnicon, in format `"00010100"` where each position indicates a bodygroup ID, and each value indicates the bodygroup value for that ID/position, 0-9a-z
    @side(client)
    function GetBodyGroup(): string
    --- Returns the currently set model name. This is set by `SpawnIcon:SetModelName`.
    --- @return string The model name
    @side(client)
    function GetModelName(): string
    --- Returns the currently set skin of the spawnicon. This is set by `SpawnIcon:SetSkinID`.
    --- @return number Current skin ID
    @side(client)
    function GetSkinID(): number
    --- Called when right clicked on the SpawnIcon. It will not be called if there is a selection (`Panel:GetSelectionCanvas`), in which case `SANDBOX:SpawnlistOpenGenericMenu` is called.
    @side(client)
    function OpenMenu(): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is done automatically by SpawnIcon. You do not need to call this. Doing so may cause unforeseen consequences.
    --- Sets the active `Sub Model ID` for the given `Body Group   ID`, so it can be retrieved with `SpawnIcon:GetBodyGroup`.
    --- Use `Panel:SetModel` instead.
    --- @param bodyGroupId The Body Group ID to set the active Sub Model ID for. Body Group IDs start at `0`.
    --- @param activeSubModelId The Sub Model ID to set as active. Sub Model IDs start at `0`.
    @side(client)
    function SetBodyGroup(bodyGroupId: number, activeSubModelId: number): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is done automatically by SpawnIcon. You do not need to call this. Doing so may cause unforeseen consequences.
    --- Sets the model name, so it can be retrieved with `SpawnIcon:GetModelName`. Use `Panel:SetModel` instead.
    --- @param mdl The model name to set
    @side(client)
    function SetModelName(mdl: string): nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is done automatically by SpawnIcon. You do not need to call this. Doing so may cause unforeseen consequences.
    --- Sets the skin id of the spawn icon, so it can be retrieved with `SpawnIcon:GetSkinID`. Use `Panel:SetModel` instead.
    --- @param skin Skin ID to set
    @side(client)
    function SetSkinID(skin: number): nil
end

--- The default SpawnmenuContentPanel
--- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
declare class SpawnmenuContentPanel extends DPanel
    --- Changes the Spawnmenu category to search in
    --- @param hookname The Hook name
    @side(client)
    function CallPopulateHook(hookname: string): nil
    --- Allows the modification of the ContentSidebar
    @side(client)
    function EnableModify(): nil
    --- Changes the Spawnmenu category to search in
    --- @param category The category
    --- @param hookname The Hook name
    @side(client)
    function EnableSearch(category: string, hookname: string): nil
    --- Switches the current panel with the given panel
    --- @param panel Panel to switch to
    @side(client)
    function SwitchPanel(panel: Panel): nil
end

--- A panel capable of loading `.tga` images.
declare class TGAImage extends Panel
end

--- A window that is used to publish dupes and saves
declare class UGCPublishWindow extends DFrame
    --- Checks if the Tags and Title are valid and if so it enables the publish button.
    @side(client)
    function CheckInput(): nil
    --- Displays the given error message.
    --- @param err The error message.
    @side(client)
    function DisplayError(err: string): nil
    --- Publishes the Item or throws an error if the Title or Tags are invalid
    --- @param wsid The workshop id
    --- @param err If wsid is nil, this will be the error message
    @side(client)
    function DoPublish(wsid: string, err: string): nil
    --- Rezises the panel to nicely fit all children
    @side(client)
    function FitContents(): nil
    --- Returns the name of the current selected tag.
    --- @return string The choosen tag, or nil if none is selected.
    @side(client)
    function GetChosenTag(): string
    --- Called when the Item was published or if any error occurred while publishing
    --- @param wsid The workshop id
    --- @param err If wsid is nil, this will be the error message
    @side(client)
    function OnPublishFinished(wsid: string, err: string): nil
    --- updated the Workshop items list.
    --- @param ugcType The type / namespace of the WorkshopFileBase that created this panel
    --- @param file The File to publish
    --- @param imageFile The Image
    --- @param handler The WorkshopFileBase that created this panel
    @side(client)
    function Setup(ugcType: string, file: string, imageFile: string, handler: WorkshopFileBase): nil
    --- updated the Workshop items list.
    @side(client)
    function UpdateWorkshopItems(): nil
end

declare class ScriptedEntity extends Entity
    Base: string | nil
    Type: string | nil
    ClassName: string | nil
    ClassNameOverride: string | nil
    Folder: string | nil
    AutomaticFrameAdvance: boolean | nil
    Category: string | nil
    SubCategory: string | nil
    Spawnable: boolean | nil
    Editable: boolean | nil
    AdminOnly: boolean | nil
    PrintName: string | nil
    Author: string | nil
    Contact: string | nil
    Purpose: string | nil
    Instructions: string | nil
    RenderGroup: number | nil
    WantsTranslucency: boolean | nil
    DisableDuplicator: boolean | nil
    ScriptedEntityType: string | nil
    IconOverride: string | nil
    PhysicsSolidMask: number | nil
    PhysicsSounds: boolean | nil
    --- Called when another entity fires an event to this entity.
    --- @param inputName The name of the input that was triggered.
    --- @param activator The initial cause for the input getting triggered. (e.g. the player who pushed a button)
    --- @param caller The entity that directly triggered the input. (e.g. the button that was pushed)
    --- @param param The input parameter.
    --- @return boolean Should we suppress the default action for this input? Returning `true` for unknown inputs will also prevent the game complaining about the unknown input in console with `developer 2`.
    @side(server)
    function AcceptInput(inputName: string, activator: Entity, caller: Entity, param: string): boolean | nil
    --- A helper function for creating `Scripted Entities`.
    --- Similar to `ENTITY:AddOutputFromKeyValue`, call it from `ENTITY:AcceptInput` and it'll return true if it successfully added an output from the passed input data.
    --- @param name The input name from ENTITY:AcceptInput.
    --- @param data The input data from ENTITY:AcceptInput.
    --- @return boolean Whether any outputs were added or not.
    @side(server)
    function AddOutputFromAcceptInput(name: string, data: string): boolean | nil
    --- A helper function for creating `Scripted Entities`.
    --- Call it from `ENTITY:KeyValue` and it'll return true if it successfully added an output from the passed KV pair.
    --- @param key The key-value key.
    --- @param value The key-value value.
    --- @return boolean Whether any outputs were added or not.
    @side(server)
    function AddOutputFromKeyValue(key: string, value: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called whenever the entity's position changes. A callback for when an entity's angle changes is available via `Entity:AddCallback`.
    --- Like `ENTITY:RenderOverride`, this hook works on any entity (scripted or not) it is applied on.
    --- **WARNING**: Defining or clearing this function in the entity table will not do anything, you must define this method in the entity itself
    --- **NOTE**: If EFL_DIRTY_ABSTRANSFORM is set on the entity, this will be called serverside only; otherwise, this will be called clientside only. This means serverside calls of `Entity:SetPos` without the EFL_DIRTY_ABSTRANSFORM flag enabled (most cases) will be called clientside only.
    --- **NOTE**: The give concommand will call this hook serverside only upon entity spawn.
    --- @param pos The entity's actual position. May differ from Entity:GetPos
    --- @param ang The entity's actual angles. May differ from Entity:GetAngles
    --- @return Vector New position
    --- @return Angle New angles
    @side(shared)
    function CalcAbsolutePosition(pos: Vector, ang: Angle): Vector | nil
    --- Called by the Sandbox gamemode from the default implementation of `GM:CanEditVariable`.
    --- @param ply The player is trying to edit a variable on this entity.
    --- @return boolean `true` to allow the edit, `false` to disallow.
    @side(server)
    function CanEditVariables(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Controls if a property can be used on this entity or not.
    --- This hook will only work in Sandbox derived gamemodes that do not have `GM:CanProperty` overridden.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook will work on ALL entities, not just the scripted ones (SENTs)
    --- @param ply Player, that tried to use the property
    --- @param property Class of the property that is tried to use, for example - bonemanipulate
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow using that property, return true to allow. You must return a value. Not returning anything can cause unexpected results.
    @side(shared)
    function CanProperty(ply: Player, property: string): boolean | nil
    --- Controls if a tool can be used on this entity or not.
    --- This hook will only work in Sandbox derived gamemodes that do not have `SANDBOX:CanTool` overridden.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook will work on ALL entities, not just the scripted ones (SENTs)
    --- @param ply Player, that tried to use the tool
    --- @param tr The trace of the tool. Returns only the `world` in the `Entity` key and returns false in the `Hit` key when the 5th argument returns `4`.
    --- @param toolname Class of the tool that is tried to use, for example - `weld`
    --- @param tool The tool mode table the player currently has selected.
    --- @param button The tool button pressed. * `1` - left click * `2` - right click * `3` - reload * `4` - spawn menu (No interaction with the toolgun). **Client-side only**
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to disallow using that tool on this entity, return `true` to allow.
    @side(shared)
    function CanTool(ply: Player, tr: TraceResult, toolname: string, tool: { [any]: any }, button: number): boolean | nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called just before `ENTITY:Initialize` for "ai" type entities only.
    @side(server)
    function CreateSchedulesInternal(): any
    --- Called so the entity can override the bullet impact effects it makes. This is called when the entity itself fires bullets via `Entity:FireBullets`, not when it gets hit.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works for the `anim` type entities.
    --- @param tr A Structures/TraceResult from the bullet's start point to the impact point
    --- @param damageType The damage type of bullet. See Enums/DMG
    --- @return boolean Return true to not do the default thing - which is to call `UTIL_ImpactTrace` in C++
    @side(shared)
    function DoImpactEffect(tr: { [any]: any }, damageType: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called by the default `base_ai` SNPC, checking whether `ENT.bDoingEngineSchedule` is set by `ENTITY:StartEngineSchedule`..
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    @side(server)
    function DoingEngineSchedule(): boolean | nil
    --- Runs a Lua schedule. Runs tasks inside the schedule.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param sched The schedule to run.
    @side(server)
    function DoSchedule(sched: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called if and when the entity should be drawn opaquely, based on the `Entity:GetRenderGroup` of the entity.
    --- See `Structures/ENT` and `Enums/RENDERGROUP` for more information.
    --- See also `ENTITY:DrawTranslucent`.
    --- **NOTE**: This function will not called if the entity's render bounds are not in player's view. See `Entity:SetRenderBounds`.
    --- @param flags The bit flags from Enums/STUDIO
    @side(client)
    function Draw(flags: number): any
    --- Called when the entity should be drawn translucently. If your scripted entity has a translucent model, it will be invisible unless it is drawn here.
    --- See `ENTITY:Draw` for the opaque rendering alternative to this hook.
    --- @param flags The bit flags from Enums/STUDIO
    @side(client)
    function DrawTranslucent(flags: number): any
    --- Called when the entity stops touching another entity.
    --- See `ENTITY:StartTouch` and `ENTITY:Touch` for related hooks.
    --- **WARNING**: This only works for **brush** entities and for entities that have `Entity:SetTrigger` set to true.
    --- @param entity The entity that we no longer touch.
    @side(server)
    function EndTouch(entity: Entity): any
    --- Called whenever an engine schedule is finished; either the last task within the engine schedule has been finished or the schedule has been interrupted by an interrupt condition.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook isn't called when the engine schedule is failed, the schedule is cleared with `NPC:ClearSchedule` or `NPC:SetSchedule` has been called.
    @side(server)
    function EngineScheduleFinish(): any
    --- Called when an NPC's expression has finished.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param strExp The path of the expression.
    @side(server)
    function ExpressionFinished(strExp: string): any
    --- Called before firing clientside animation events, such as muzzle flashes or shell ejections.
    --- See `ENTITY:HandleAnimEvent` for the serverside version.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works on "anim", "nextbot" and "ai" type entities.
    --- @param pos Position of the effect
    --- @param ang Angle of the effect
    --- @param event The event ID of happened even. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events). Only event IDs above 5000 will appear in this hook. (Are considered the "new" system in-engine)
    --- @param name Name of the event
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable the effect
    @side(client)
    function FireAnimationEvent(pos: Vector, ang: Angle, event: number, name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called to determine how good an NPC is at using a particular weapon.
    --- **NOTE**: "ai" base only
    --- @param wep The weapon being used by the NPC.
    --- @param target The target the NPC is attacking
    --- @return number The number of degrees of inaccuracy in the NPC's attack.
    @side(server)
    function GetAttackSpread(wep: Weapon, target: NPC): number | nil
    --- Called when scripted NPC needs to check how it "feels" against another entity, such as when `NPC:Disposition` is called.
    --- **NOTE**: Scripted NPCs will not select other entities using same `Entity:GetModel` as this Scripted NPC's `Entity:GetModel` as enemy, unless `NPC:AddEntityRelationship` is cast.
    --- @param ent The entity in question
    --- @return number How our scripted NPC "feels" towards the entity in question. See Enums/D. Not returning any value will make NPC:Disposition return the default disposition for this SNPC's given `m_iClass` by the engine.
    @side(server)
    function GetRelationship(ent: Entity): number | nil
    --- Specify a mesh that should be rendered instead of this SENT's model.
    --- **NOTE**: You should not be creating or modifying an `IMesh` in this hook. [Reference](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/6411#issuecomment-3070608549)
    --- @return { [any]: any } A table containing the following keys: * IMesh Mesh - (Required) The mesh to render instead of the default model * IMaterial Material - (Required) The material to render the mesh with. * VMatrix Matrix - (Optional) - Render matrix override (mesh position, angles, etc)
    @side(client)
    function GetRenderMesh(): { [any]: any } | nil
    --- Called when the shadow needs to be recomputed. Allows shadow angles to be customized. This only works for `anim` type entities.
    --- @param type Type of the shadow this entity uses. Possible values: * 0 - No shadow * 1 - Simple 'blob' shadow * 2 - Render To Texture shadow (updates only when necessary) * 3 - Dynamic RTT - updates always * 4 - Render to Depth Texture
    --- @return Vector The new shadow direction to use.
    @side(client)
    function GetShadowCastDirection(type: number): Vector | nil
    --- Called every second to poll the sound hint interests of this SNPC. This is used in conjunction with other sound hint functions, such as `sound.EmitHint` and `NPC:GetBestSoundHint`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs
    --- @return number A bitflag representing which sound types this NPC wants to react to.  See Enums/SOUND.
    @side(server)
    function GetSoundInterests(): number | nil
    --- Called by `GM:GravGunPickupAllowed` on ALL entites in Sandbox-derived  gamemodes and acts as an override.
    --- @param ply The player aiming at us
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow the entity to be picked up
    @side(server)
    function GravGunPickupAllowed(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when this entity is about to be punted with the gravity gun (primary fire).
    --- Only works in Sandbox derived gamemodes and only if `GM:GravGunPunt` is not overridden.
    --- @param ply The player pressing left-click with the gravity gun at an entity
    --- @return boolean Return true or false to enable or disable punting respectively.
    @side(shared)
    function GravGunPunt(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called before firing serverside animation events, such as weapon reload, drawing and holstering for NPCs, scripted sequences, etc.
    --- See `ENTITY:FireAnimationEvent` for the clientside version.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works on "anim", "ai" and "nextbot" type entities.
    --- @param event The ID of the event. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events) for a list of default events, and see util.GetAnimEventNameByID for a helper function in handing custom events.
    --- @param eventTime The absolute time this event occurred using Global.CurTime.
    --- @param cycle The frame this event occurred as a number between 0 and 1.
    --- @param type Event type. See [the Source SDK](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/shared/eventlist.h#L14-L23).
    --- @param options Name or options of this event.
    --- @return boolean Return true to mark the event as handled.
    @side(server)
    function HandleAnimEvent(event: number, eventTime: number, cycle: number, type: number, options: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a bullet trace hits this entity and allows you to override the default behavior by returning true.
    --- @param traceResult The trace that hit this entity as a Structures/TraceResult.
    --- @param damageType The damage bits associated with the trace, see Enums/DMG
    --- @param customImpactName The effect name to override the impact effect with. Possible arguments are ImpactJeep, AirboatGunImpact, HelicopterImpact, ImpactGunship.
    --- @return boolean Return true to override the default impact effects.
    @side(client)
    function ImpactTrace(traceResult: { [any]: any }, damageType: number, customImpactName: string | nil): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the entity is created. This is called when you `Entity:Spawn` the custom entity.
    --- This is called **after** `ENTITY:SetupDataTables` and `GM:OnEntityCreated`.
    @side(shared)
    function Initialize(): any
    --- Called when deciding if the Scripted NPC should be able to perform a certain jump or not.
    --- **NOTE**: This is only called for "ai" type entities
    --- @param startPos Start of the jump
    --- @param apex Apex point of the jump
    --- @param endPos The landing position
    --- @return boolean Return true if this jump should be allowed to be performed, false otherwise. Not returning anything, or returning a non boolean will perform the [default action](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc_movement.cpp#L319).
    @side(server)
    function IsJumpLegal(startPos: Vector, apex: Vector, endPos: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the engine sets a value for this scripted entity.
    --- This hook is called **before** `ENTITY:Initialize` when the key-values are set by the map.
    --- Otherwise this hook will be called whenever `Entity:SetKeyValue` is called on the entity.
    --- See `GM:EntityKeyValue` for a hook that works for all entities.
    --- See `WEAPON:KeyValue` for a hook that works for scripted weapons.
    --- @param key The key that was affected.
    --- @param value The new value.
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress this KeyValue or return false or nothing to apply this key value.
    @side(server)
    function KeyValue(key: string, value: string): boolean | nil
    --- Start the next task in specific Lua schedule.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param sched The schedule to start next task in.
    @side(server)
    function NextTask(sched: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called when the currently active weapon of the SNPC changes.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works on `ai` type entities.
    --- @param old The previous active weapon.
    --- @param new_ The new active weapon.
    @side(server)
    function OnChangeActiveWeapon(old: Weapon, new_: Weapon): any
    --- Called when the NPC has changed its activity.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works for `ai` type entities.
    --- @param act The new activity. See Enums/ACT.
    @side(server)
    function OnChangeActivity(act: number): any
    --- Called each time the NPC updates its condition.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param conditionID The ID of condition. See NPC:ConditionName.
    @side(server)
    function OnCondition(conditionID: number): any
    --- Called on any entity after it has been created by the `duplicator` and before any bone/entity modifiers have been applied.
    --- This hook is called after `ENTITY:Initialize` and before `ENTITY:PostEntityPaste`.
    --- @param entTable The stored data about the original entity that was duplicated. This would typically contain the Entity:GetTable fields that are serializable. See Structures/EntityCopyData.
    @side(server)
    function OnDuplicated(entTable: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called after duplicator finishes saving the entity, allowing you to modify the save data.
    --- This is called after `ENTITY:PostEntityCopy`.
    --- @param data The save Structures/EntityCopyData that you can modify.
    @side(server)
    function OnEntityCopyTableFinish(data: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called when the SNPC completes its movement to its destination.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works on `ai` type entities.
    @side(server)
    function OnMovementComplete(): any
    --- Called when the SNPC failed to move to its destination.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works on `ai` type entities.
    @side(server)
    function OnMovementFailed(): any
    --- Called when the entity is reloaded by the lua auto-refresh system, i.e. when the developer edits the lua file for the entity while the game is running.
    @side(shared)
    function OnReloaded(): any
    --- Called when the entity is about to be removed.
    --- See also `Entity:CallOnRemove`, which can even be used on engine (non-Lua) entities.
    --- Create an explosion when the entity will be removed. To create an entity, you can read `ents.Create`.
    --- function ENT:OnRemove()
    --- local explosion = ents.Create( "env_explosion" ) -- The explosion entity
    --- explosion:SetPos( self:GetPos() ) -- Put the position of the explosion at the position of the entity
    --- explosion:Spawn() -- Spawn the explosion
    --- explosion:SetKeyValue( "iMagnitude", "50" ) -- the magnitude of the explosion
    --- explosion:Fire( "Explode", 0, 0 ) -- explode
    --- end
    --- @param fullUpdate Whether the removal is happening due to a full update clientside. The entity may or **may not** be recreated immediately after, depending on whether it is in the local player's [PVS](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). (See Entity:IsDormant)
    @side(shared)
    function OnRemove(fullUpdate: boolean): any
    --- Called when the entity is reloaded from a Source Engine save (not the Sandbox saves or dupes) or on a changelevel (for example Half-Life 2 campaign level transitions).
    --- For the `duplicator` callbacks, see `ENTITY:OnDuplicated`.
    @side(shared)
    function OnRestore(): any
    --- Called by the engine when NPC's state changes.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- @param oldState The old state. See Enums/NPC_STATE.
    --- @param newState The new state. See Enums/NPC_STATE.
    @side(server)
    function OnStateChange(oldState: number, newState: number): any
    --- Called when the entity is taking damage.
    --- **WARNING**: Calling `Entity:TakeDamage`, `Entity:TakeDamageInfo`, `Entity:DispatchTraceAttack`, or `Player:TraceHullAttack` (if the entity is hit) in this hook on the victim entity can cause infinite loops since the hook will be called again. Make sure to setup recursion safeguards like the example below.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is only called for `ai`, `nextbot` and `anim` type entities.
    --- @param damage The damage to be applied to the entity.
    --- @return number How much damage the entity took. Basically `> 0` means took damage, `0` means did not take damage.
    @side(server)
    function OnTakeDamage(damage: CTakeDamageInfo): number | nil
    --- Called from the engine when TaskComplete is called.
    --- This allows us to move onto the next task - even when TaskComplete was called from an engine side task.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    @side(server)
    function OnTaskComplete(): any
    --- Called when a task this NPC was running has failed for whatever reason.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param failCode The fail code for the task. It will be a [FAIL_ enum](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/0d8dceea4310fde5706b3ce1c70609d72a38efdf/sp/src/game/server/ai_task.h#L26) or a generated code for a custom string. (second argument)
    --- @param failReason If set, a custom reason for the failure.
    @side(server)
    function OnTaskFailed(failCode: number, failReason: string): any
    --- Called when a trace attack is done against the entity, allowing override of the damage being dealt by altering the `CTakeDamageInfo`.
    --- This is called before `ENTITY:OnTakeDamage`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is only called for `ai`, `anim` (as of version `2026.07.03`) and `nextbot` type entities.
    --- @param info The damage info
    --- @param dir The direction the damage goes in
    --- @param trace The Structures/TraceResult of the attack, containing the hitgroup.
    @side(server)
    function OnTraceAttack(info: CTakeDamageInfo, dir: Vector, trace: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called to completely override NPC movement. This can be used for example for flying NPCs.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- @param interval Time interval for the movement, in seconds. Usually time since last movement.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to disable the default movement code.
    @side(server)
    function OverrideMove(interval: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called to completely override the direction NPC will be facing during navigation.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called by the default movement hook. Returning `true` inside `ENTITY:OverrideMove` will prevent engine from calling this hook.
    --- @param interval Time interval for the movement, in seconds. Usually time since last movement.
    --- @param AILMG Extra data for the movement. A table containing the following data: * boolean hasTraced - The result if a forward probing trace has been done * number expectedDist = `speed*interval` - The distance expected to move this think * number flags - [AILMG flags](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_movetypes.h#L113) * number maxDist = NPC:GetPathDistanceToGoal - The distance maximum distance intended to travel in path length * number navType - Enums/NAV * number speed - Entity:GetSequenceGroundSpeed Note these need not always agree with `target` * Entity moveTarget = `m_hGoalEnt` - Target entity as goal. * Vector dir - The step direction, towards `target` * Vector facing - The direction NPC's body will turn during movement. * Vector target = NPC:GetCurWaypointPos - Current waypoint in world coordinates.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to disable the default movement facing code.
    @side(server)
    function OverrideMoveFacing(interval: number, AILMG: { [any]: any }): boolean | nil
    --- Polls whenever the entity should trigger the brush.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is broken and will not work without code below
    --- @param ent The entity that is about to trigger.
    --- @return boolean Should trigger or not.
    @side(server)
    function PassesTriggerFilters(ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the entity collides with anything via `physics objects`. The `move type` and `solid mode` must be `VPHYSICS` for the hook to be called.
    --- This hook only works for `anim` type entities.
    --- This is different from `ENTITY:Touch`.
    --- **NOTE**: If you want to use this hook on default/engine/non-Lua entities (like `prop_physics`), use `Entity:AddCallback` instead! This page describes a hook for Lua scripted entities
    --- @param colData Information regarding the collision. See Structures/CollisionData.
    --- @param collider The physics object that collided.
    @side(server)
    function PhysicsCollide(colData: { [any]: any }, collider: PhysObj): any
    --- Called from the Entity's motion controller to simulate physics.
    --- This will only be called after using `Entity:StartMotionController` on a `scripted entity` of `anim` type.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook can work on the CLIENT if you call `Entity:StartMotionController` and use `Entity:AddToMotionController` on the physics objects you want to control
    --- **WARNING**: Do not use functions such as `PhysObj:EnableCollisions` or `PhysObj:EnableGravity` in this hook as they're very likely to crash your game. You may want to use `ENTITY:PhysicsUpdate` instead.
    --- @param phys The physics object of the entity.
    --- @param deltaTime Time since the last call.
    --- @return Vector Angular force. The 3rd argument must be above SIM_NOTHING.
    --- @return Vector Linear force. The 3rd argument must be above SIM_NOTHING.
    --- @return number One of the Enums/SIM.
    @side(shared)
    function PhysicsSimulate(phys: PhysObj, deltaTime: number): Vector | nil
    --- Called whenever a physics object of this entity is updated.
    --- This hook won't be called if the Entity's `PhysObj` goes asleep, or doesn't exist.
    --- @param phys The physics object of the entity.
    @side(shared)
    function PhysicsUpdate(phys: PhysObj): any
    --- Called after the duplicator finished copying the entity, after `ENTITY:PreEntityCopy`.
    --- Use `ENTITY:OnEntityCopyTableFinish` to modify the dupe table for this entity.
    --- See also `ENTITY:PostEntityPaste` for the restore hook.
    @side(server)
    function PostEntityCopy(): any
    --- Called after the `duplicator` pastes the entity, after the bone/entity modifiers have been applied to the entity.
    --- This hook is called after `ENTITY:OnDuplicated`. See also `ENTITY:PreEntityCopy`.
    --- @param ply The player who pasted the entity. This may not be a valid player in some circumstances. For example, when a save is loaded from the main menu, this hook will be called before the player is spawned. This argument will be a NULL entity in that case.
    --- @param ent The entity itself. Same as `self` within the function context.
    --- @param createdEntities All entities that are within the placed dupe. The keys of each value in this table are the original entity indexes when the duplication was created. This can be utilized to restore entity references that don't get saved in duplications.
    @side(server)
    function PostEntityPaste(ply: Player, ent: Entity, createdEntities: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called before the duplicator copies the entity.
    --- If you are looking for a way to make the duplicator spawn another entity when duplicated. (For example, you duplicate a `prop_physics`, but you want the duplicator to spawn `prop_physics_my`), you should add `prop_physics.ClassOverride = "prop_physics_my"`. The duplication table should be also stored on that `prop_physics`, not on `prop_physics_my`.
    --- See also `ENTITY:PostEntityCopy`.
    @side(server)
    function PreEntityCopy(): any
    --- Called instead of the engine drawing function of the entity. This hook works on any entity (scripted or not) it is applied on.
    --- This does not work on "physgun_beam", use `GM:DrawPhysgunBeam` instead.
    --- **WARNING**: Defining or clearing this function in the entity table will not do anything, you must define this method in the entity itself
    --- Drawing a viewmodel in this function will cause `GM:PreDrawViewModel`, `WEAPON:PreDrawViewModel`, `WEAPON:ViewModelDrawn`, `GM:PostDrawViewModel`, and `WEAPON:PostDrawViewModel` to be called twice.
    --- This is called before PrePlayerDraw for players. If this function exists at all on a player, their worldmodel will always be rendered regardless of PrePlayerDraw's return.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    function RenderOverride(flags: number): any
    --- Called during a non-VPhysics collision event for flying entities.
    --- This is best used to make projectiles bounce off from surfaces in their own way. For this to be triggered, this entity must be the one that's colliding, have some velocity, `Entity:GetMoveType` must be either `MOVETYPE_FLY` or `MOVETYPE_FLYGRAVITY`, and `Entity:GetMoveCollide` must be `MOVECOLLIDE_FLY_CUSTOM`.
    --- **NOTE**: This works only on `anim` type entities.
    --- @param traceResult The Structures/TraceResult where the collision occured.
    --- @param vel The calculated velocity after calculations such as bounciness, elasticity, ground sliding etc...
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent default action.
    @side(server)
    function ResolveCustomFlyCollision(traceResult: TraceResult, vel: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Called from the engine every [m_flNextDecisionTime](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc.cpp#L3943C10-L3943C30) in seconds. This interval changes depending on NPC's [Efficiency](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc.cpp#L3093). Returning `true` inside this hook will allow [CAI_BaseNPC::MaintainSchedule](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc_schedule.cpp#L562) to also be called.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @return boolean `true` to run engine schedules
    @side(server)
    function RunAI(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when an engine task is ran on the entity.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param taskID The task ID, see [ai_task.h](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/55ed12f8d1eb6887d348be03aee5573d44177ffb/mp/src/game/server/ai_task.h#L89-L502)
    --- @param taskData The task data.
    --- @return boolean true to prevent default action
    @side(server)
    function RunEngineTask(taskID: number, taskData: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called every think on running task.
    --- The actual task function should tell us when the task is finished.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param task The task to run
    @side(server)
    function RunTask(task: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called whenever a Lua schedule is finished or `ENTITY:StartEngineSchedule` is called. Clears out schedule and task data stored within NPC's table.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    @side(server)
    function ScheduleFinished(): any
    --- Set the schedule we should be playing right now. Allows the NPC to start either a Lua schedule or an engine schedule. Despite sharing the same name as `CAI_BaseNPC::SelectSchedule()`, this isn't hooked to that function; this is called by Lua's `ENTITY:RunAI`, doesn't return an engine function, returning an engine function doesn't help and doesn't make the NPC start an engine schedule. To alter initial engine schedule, it is recommended to use `ENTITY:TranslateSchedule`.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    @side(server)
    function SelectSchedule(): any
    --- Toggles automatic frame advancing for animated sequences on an entity.
    --- This has the same effect as setting the ``ENT.AutomaticFrameAdvance`` property. (See `Structures/ENT`)
    --- @param enable Whether or not to set automatic frame advancing.
    @side(shared)
    function SetAutomaticFrameAdvance(enable: boolean): any
    --- Sets the current task, to be used in a Lua schedule.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param task The task to set.
    @side(server)
    function SetTask(task: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called when the entity should set up its ` Data Tables`.
    --- This is a much better option than using Set/Get Networked Values.
    --- This hook is called after `GM:OnEntityCreated` and `GM:NetworkEntityCreated`.
    @side(shared)
    function SetupDataTables(): any
    --- This is the spawn function. It's called when a player spawns the entity from the spawnmenu.
    --- If you want to make your SENT spawnable you need this function to properly create the entity.
    --- **WARNING**: Unlike other ENTITY functions, the "self" parameter of this function is not an entity but rather the table used to generate the SENT. This table is equivalent to `scripted_ents.GetStored`("ent_name").
    --- @param ply The player that is spawning this SENT
    --- @param tr A Structures/TraceResult from player eyes to their aim position
    --- @param className The classname of your entity
    --- @return Entity The created scripted entity.
    @side(server)
    function SpawnFunction(ply: Player, tr: { [any]: any }, className: string): Entity | nil
    --- Called by the engine only whenever `NPC:SetSchedule` is called.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param scheduleID Schedule ID to start. See Enums/SCHED
    @side(server)
    function StartEngineSchedule(scheduleID: number): any
    --- Called when an engine task has been started on the entity.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @param taskID Task ID to start, see [ai_task.h](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/55ed12f8d1eb6887d348be03aee5573d44177ffb/mp/src/game/server/ai_task.h#L89-L502)
    --- @param TaskData Task data
    --- @return boolean true to stop default action
    @side(server)
    function StartEngineTask(taskID: number, TaskData: number): boolean | nil
    --- Starts a schedule previously created by `ai_schedule.New`.
    --- Not to be confused with `ENTITY:StartEngineSchedule` or `NPC:SetSchedule` which start an Engine-based schedule.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param sched Schedule to start.
    @side(server)
    function StartSchedule(sched: Schedule): any
    --- Called once when a LUA schedule has started a task.
    --- **NOTE**: This is a helper function only available if your SENT is based on `base_ai`
    --- @param task The task to start, created by ai_task.New.
    @side(server)
    function StartTask(task: Task): any
    --- Called when the entity starts touching another entity.
    --- See `ENTITY:Touch` and `ENTITY:EndTouch` for related hooks.
    --- **WARNING**: This only works for **brush** entities and for entities that have `Entity:SetTrigger` set to true.
    --- @param entity The entity that we started touching for the first time.
    @side(server)
    function StartTouch(entity: Entity): any
    --- Used to store an output so it can be triggered with `ENTITY:TriggerOutput`.
    --- Outputs compiled into a map are passed to entities as key/value pairs through `ENTITY:KeyValue`.
    --- TriggerOutput will do nothing if this function has not been called first.
    --- @param name Name of output to store
    --- @param info Output info
    @side(server)
    function StoreOutput(name: string, info: string): any
    --- Returns true if the current running `Task` is finished.
    --- Tasks finish whenever `NPC:TaskComplete` is called, which sets `TASKSTATUS_COMPLETE` for all NPCs, also sets `self.bTaskComplete` for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @return boolean Is the current running Task is finished or not.
    @side(server)
    function TaskFinished(): boolean | nil
    --- Returns how many seconds we've been doing this current task
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type `SENTs`.
    --- @return number How many seconds we've been doing this current task
    @side(server)
    function TaskTime(): number | nil
    --- Allows you to override trace result when a trace hits the entity.
    --- Your entity **must** have `Entity:EnableCustomCollisions` enabled for this hook to work.
    --- Your entity must also be otherwise "hit-able" with a trace, so it should have `SOLID_OBB` or `SOLID_VPHYSICS` be set (as an example), and it must have its `collision bounds` be set accordingly.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called for `anim` type only.
    --- @param startpos Start position of the trace.
    --- @param delta Offset from startpos to the endpos of the trace.
    --- @param isbox Is the trace a hull trace?
    --- @param extents Size of the hull trace, with the center of the Bounding Box being `0, 0, 0`, so mins are `-extents`, and maxs are `extents`.
    --- @param mask The Enums/CONTENTS mask.
    --- @return { [any]: any } Returning a `table` will allow you to override trace results. Table should contain the following keys: (All keys fallback to the original trace value) * Vector `HitPos` - The new hit position of the trace. * number `Fraction` - A number from `0` to `1`, describing how far the trace went from its origin point, `1` = did not hit. * Could be calculated like so : `Fraction = ( startpos + delta ):Length() / myCustomHitPos:Length()` * Vector `Normal` - A unit vector (length=1) describing the direction perpendicular to the hit surface. Returning `true` will allow "normal" collisions to happen for `SOLID_VPHYSICS` and `SOLID_OBB` entities. Returning `nothing` or `false` allows the trace to ignore the entity completely.
    @side(shared)
    function TestCollision(startpos: Vector, delta: Vector, isbox: boolean, extents: Vector, mask: number): { [any]: any } | nil
    --- Called every frame on the client.
    --- Called about 5-6 times per second on the server.
    --- **NOTE**: You may need to call `Entity:Spawn` to get this hook to run server side.
    --- You can force it to run at servers tickrate using the example below.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` if you used Entity:NextThink to override the next execution time. Otherwise it will be reset to `CurTime() + 0.2`.
    @side(shared)
    function Think(): boolean | nil
    --- Called every tick for every entity being "touched". Touching is usually detected via AABB intersection checks using entity's `collision bounds`.
    --- Entities like triggers would be using the touch hooks for their function.
    --- See `Entity:PhysicsCollide` for physics based collision events.
    --- See also `ENTITY:StartTouch` and `ENTITY:EndTouch`.
    --- **NOTE**: For physics enabled entities, this hook will **not** be ran while the entity's physics is asleep. See `PhysObj:Wake`.
    --- @param entity The entity that touched it.
    @side(server)
    function Touch(entity: Entity): any
    --- Called by the engine to alter NPC activities, if desired by the NPC.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- @param oldAct The activity to translate.
    --- @return number The activity that should override the incoming activity. Not returning anything, or returning a non value will perform the [default action](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc.cpp#L5976).
    @side(server)
    function TranslateActivity(oldAct: number): number | nil
    --- Called by the engine to alter NPC's final position to reach its enemy or target. This is called twice for `GOALTYPE_PATHCORNER`; first is for the first path_corner and second for the next connected path_corner.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- @param target The enemy being chased or the path_corner in query.
    --- @param currentGoal The target's origin.
    --- @return Vector The actual point that NPC will move to reach its enemy or target. For the path to get updated, the new move path must be away from the current NPC:GetGoalPos by 120 units. Not returning anything, or returning a non vector will perform the [default action](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_basenpc_schedule.cpp#L4251).
    @side(server)
    function TranslateNavGoal(target: NPC | Entity | nil, currentGoal: Vector | nil): Vector | nil
    --- Called by the engine to alter NPC schedules, if desired by the NPC.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only exists for `ai` type SENTs.
    --- @param schedule The schedule to translate. See Enums/SCHED.
    --- @return number The schedule that should override the incoming schedule. Not returning anything, or returning a non value will perform the [default action](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/server/ai_default.cpp#L253).
    @side(server)
    function TranslateSchedule(schedule: number): number | nil
    --- Triggers all outputs stored using `ENTITY:StoreOutput`.
    --- @param output Name of output to fire
    --- @param activator Activator entity
    --- @param data The data to give to the output.
    @side(server)
    function TriggerOutput(output: string, activator: Entity, data: string | nil): any
    --- Called whenever the transmit state should be updated.
    --- @return number Transmit state to set, see Enums/TRANSMIT.
    @side(server)
    function UpdateTransmitState(): number | nil
    --- Called when an entity "uses" this entity, for example a player pressing their `+use` key (default E) on this entity.
    --- To change how often the hook is called, see `Entity:SetUseType`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only works for `nextbot`, `ai` and `anim` scripted entity types.
    --- @param activator The entity that caused this input. This will usually be the player who pressed their use key.
    --- @param caller The entity responsible for the input. This will typically be the same as `activator` unless some other entity is acting as a proxy.
    --- @param useType Use type, see Enums/USE.
    --- @param value Any passed value.
    @side(server)
    override function Use(activator: Entity, caller: Entity, useType: number, value: number): any
end
declare ENT: ScriptedEntity

declare class ScriptedWeapon extends Weapon
    ClassName: string | nil
    ClassNameOverride: string | nil
    Category: string | nil
    SubCategory: string | nil
    Spawnable: boolean | nil
    AdminOnly: boolean | nil
    PrintName: string | nil
    Base: string | nil
    m_WeaponDeploySpeed: number | nil
    Owner: Entity | nil
    Weapon: Weapon | nil
    Author: string | nil
    Contact: string | nil
    Purpose: string | nil
    Instructions: string | nil
    ViewModel: string | nil
    ViewModelFlip: boolean | nil
    ViewModelFlip1: boolean | nil
    ViewModelFlip2: boolean | nil
    ViewModelFOV: number | nil
    WorldModel: string | nil
    AutoSwitchFrom: boolean | nil
    AutoSwitchTo: boolean | nil
    Weight: number | nil
    BobScale: number | nil
    SwayScale: number | nil
    BounceWeaponIcon: boolean | nil
    DrawWeaponInfoBox: boolean | nil
    DrawAmmo: boolean | nil
    DrawCrosshair: boolean | nil
    RenderGroup: number | nil
    WantsTranslucency: boolean | nil
    Slot: number | nil
    SlotPos: number | nil
    SpeechBubbleLid: number | nil
    WepSelectIcon: number | nil
    CSMuzzleFlashes: boolean | nil
    CSMuzzleX: boolean | nil
    Primary: { [any]: any } | nil
    Secondary: { [any]: any } | nil
    UseHands: boolean | nil
    Folder: string | nil
    AccurateCrosshair: boolean | nil
    DisableDuplicator: boolean | nil
    ScriptedEntityType: string | nil
    m_bPlayPickupSound: boolean | nil
    IconOverride: string | nil
    --- Called when another entity fires an event to this entity.
    --- @param inputName The name of the input that was triggered.
    --- @param activator The initial cause for the input getting triggered.
    --- @param called The entity that directly trigger the input.
    --- @param data The data passed.
    --- @return boolean Should we suppress the default action for this input?
    @side(server)
    function AcceptInput(inputName: string, activator: Entity, called: Entity, data: string): boolean | nil
    --- Allows you to adjust the weapon's mouse sensitivity. This hook only works if you haven't overridden `GM:AdjustMouseSensitivity`.
    --- @param defaultSensitivity The old sensitivity In general this will be 0, which is equivalent to a sensitivity of 1.
    --- @param localFOV The player's current FOV.
    --- @param defaultFOV The player's default FOV.
    --- @return number A multiplier of the player's normal sensitivity (0.5 would be half as sensitive, 2 would be twice as sensitive).
    @side(client)
    function AdjustMouseSensitivity(defaultSensitivity: number, localFOV: number, defaultFOV: number): number | nil
    --- Returns how much of primary ammo the player has.
    --- @return number The amount of primary ammo player has
    @side(shared)
    function Ammo1(): number | nil
    --- Returns how much of secondary ammo the player has.
    --- @return number The amount of secondary ammo player has
    @side(shared)
    function Ammo2(): number | nil
    --- Allows you to adjust player view while this weapon in use.
    --- This hook is called from the default implementation of `GM:CalcView` which is [here](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/gamemodes/base/gamemode/cl_init.lua#L387-L395). Therefore, it will not be called if any other hook added to `CalcView` returns any value, or if the current gamemode overrides the default hook and does not call the SWEP function.
    --- @param ply The owner of weapon
    --- @param pos Current position of players view
    --- @param ang Current angles of players view
    --- @param fov Current FOV of players view
    --- @return Vector New position of players view
    --- @return Angle New angle of players view
    --- @return number New FOV of players view
    @side(client)
    function CalcView(ply: Player, pos: Vector, ang: Angle, fov: number): Vector | nil
    --- Allows overriding the position and angle of the viewmodel. This hook only works if you haven't overridden `GM:CalcViewModelView`.
    --- @param ViewModel The viewmodel entity
    --- @param OldEyePos Original position (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param OldEyeAng Original angle (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param EyePos Current position
    --- @param EyeAng Current angle
    --- @return Vector New position
    --- @return Angle New angle
    @side(client)
    function CalcViewModelView(ViewModel: Entity, OldEyePos: Vector, OldEyeAng: Angle, EyePos: Vector, EyeAng: Angle): Vector | nil
    --- Called when a Citizen NPC is looking around to a (better) weapon to pickup.
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow this weapon to be picked up by NPCs.
    @side(server)
    function CanBePickedUpByNPCs(): boolean | nil
    --- Helper function for checking for no ammo.
    --- @return boolean Can use primary attack
    @side(shared)
    function CanPrimaryAttack(): boolean | nil
    --- Helper function for checking for no ammo.
    --- @return boolean Can use secondary attack
    @side(shared)
    function CanSecondaryAttack(): boolean | nil
    --- Allows you to use any numbers you want for the ammo display on the HUD.
    --- Can be useful for weapons that don't use standard ammo.
    --- @return { [any]: any } The new ammo display settings. A table with 4 possible keys: (All default to -1) * boolean Draw - Whether to draw the ammo display or not * number PrimaryClip - Amount of primary ammo in the clip * number PrimaryAmmo - Amount of primary ammo in the reserves * number SecondaryAmmo - Amount of secondary ammo. It is shown like alt-fire for SMG1 and AR2 are shown. * number SecondaryClip - Amount of secondary ammo in the clip. If set, the secondary ammo display will have clips and reserve ammo dispalyed.
    @side(client)
    function CustomAmmoDisplay(): { [any]: any } | nil
    --- Called when player has just switched to this weapon.
    --- **NOTE**: Due to this hook being predicted, it is not called clientside in singleplayer at all, and in multiplayer it will not be called clientside if the weapon is switched with `Player:SelectWeapon` or the "use" console command, however it will be called clientside with the default weapon selection menu and when using `CUserCmd:SelectWeapon`
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow switching away from this weapon using `lastinv` command
    @side(shared)
    function Deploy(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the crosshair is about to get drawn, and allows you to override it.
    --- This function will **not** be called if `SWEP.DrawCrosshair` is set to false or if player is affected by `Player:CrosshairDisable`.
    --- @param x X coordinate of the crosshair.
    --- @param y Y coordinate of the crosshair.
    --- @return boolean Return true to override the default crosshair.
    @side(client)
    function DoDrawCrosshair(x: number, y: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called so the weapon can override the impact effects it makes.
    --- **NOTE**: If the bullet was fired in a predicted environment, the hook will not be called on the `CLIENT` realm.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook will also be called when `WEAPON:GetOwner():FireBullets` is called. While in `MULTIPLAYER`, this hook will be called on the respective state, but in `SINGLEPLAYER`, this hook will always be called on the `CLIENT` realm even if `FireBullets` was called on the `SERVER`.
    --- @param tr A Structures/TraceResult from player's eyes to the impact point
    --- @param damageType The damage type of bullet. See Enums/DMG
    --- @return boolean Return true to not do the default thing - which is to call `UTIL_ImpactTrace` in C++
    @side(shared)
    function DoImpactEffect(tr: { [any]: any }, damageType: number): boolean | nil
    --- This hook allows you to draw on screen while this weapon is in use.
    --- If you want to draw a custom crosshair, consider using `WEAPON:DoDrawCrosshair` instead.
    @side(client)
    function DrawHUD(): any
    --- This hook allows you to draw on screen while this weapon is in use. This hook is called **before** `WEAPON:DrawHUD` and is equivalent of `GM:HUDPaintBackground`.
    @side(client)
    function DrawHUDBackground(): any
    --- This hook draws the selection icon in the weapon selection menu.
    --- @param x X coordinate of the selection panel
    --- @param y Y coordinate of the selection panel
    --- @param width Width of the selection panel
    --- @param height Height of the selection panel
    --- @param alpha Alpha value of the selection panel
    @side(client)
    function DrawWeaponSelection(x: number, y: number, width: number, height: number, alpha: number): any
    --- Called when we are about to draw the opaque parts of the weapon's world model.
    --- See `WEAPON:DrawWorldModelTranslucent` for translucent pass callback.
    --- See `WEAPON:ViewModelDrawn` for view model rendering.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    function DrawWorldModel(flags: number): any
    --- Called when we are about to draw the translucent parts of the weapon's world model.
    --- See `WEAPON:DrawWorldModel` for opaque pass callback.
    --- See `WEAPON:ViewModelDrawn` for view model rendering.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    function DrawWorldModelTranslucent(flags: number): any
    --- Called when a player or NPC has picked the weapon up.
    --- @param NewOwner The one who picked the weapon up. Can be Player or NPC.
    @side(server)
    function Equip(NewOwner: Entity): any
    --- The player has picked up the weapon and has taken the ammo from it.
    --- The weapon will be removed immediately after this call.
    --- @param ply The player who picked up the weapon
    @side(server)
    function EquipAmmo(ply: Player): any
    --- Called before executing an animation event, such as a muzzle flash appearing or a shell ejecting.
    --- This will only be called serverside for 3000-range events, and clientside for 5000-range and other events.
    --- @param pos Position of the effect.
    --- @param ang Angle of the effect.
    --- @param event The event ID of the happened event. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events).
    --- @param options Name or options of the event.
    --- @param source The source entity. This will be a viewmodel on the client and the weapon itself on the server
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable the effect.
    @side(shared)
    function FireAnimationEvent(pos: Vector, ang: Angle, event: number, options: string, source: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- This hook allows you to freeze players screen.
    --- **NOTE**: Player will still be able to move or shoot
    --- @return boolean Return true to freeze moving the view
    @side(client)
    function FreezeMovement(): boolean | nil
    --- This hook is for NPCs, you return what they should try to do with it.
    --- **WARNING**: Calling `NPC:CapabilitiesGet` in this hook on the same entity can cause infinite loops since that function adds the result of `WEAPON:GetCapabilities` on top of the return value.
    --- @return number A number defining what NPC should do with the weapon. Use the Enums/CAP.
    @side(server)
    function GetCapabilities(): number | nil
    --- Called when the weapon is used by NPCs to determine how accurate the bullets fired should be.
    --- The inaccuracy is simulated by changing the `NPC:GetAimVector` based on the value returned from this hook.
    --- @param proficiency How proficient the NPC is with this gun. See Enums/WEAPON_PROFICIENCY
    --- @return number An amount of degrees the bullets should deviate from the NPC's NPC:GetAimVector. Default is 15.
    @side(server)
    function GetNPCBulletSpread(proficiency: number): number | nil
    --- Called when the weapon is used by NPCs to tell the NPC how to use this weapon. Controls how long the NPC can or should shoot continuously.
    --- @return number Minimum amount of bullets per burst. Default is 1.
    --- @return number Maximum amount of bullets per burst. Default is 1.
    --- @return number Delay between each shot, aka firerate. Default is 1.
    @side(server)
    function GetNPCBurstSettings(): number | nil
    --- Called when the weapon is used by NPCs to tell the NPC how to use this weapon. Controls amount of time the NPC can rest (not shoot) between bursts.
    --- @return number Minimum amount of time the NPC can rest (not shoot) between bursts in seconds. Default is `0.3` seconds.
    --- @return number Maximum amount of time the NPC can rest (not shoot) between bursts in seconds. Default is `0.6` seconds.
    @side(server)
    function GetNPCRestTimes(): number | nil
    --- Allows you to override where the tracer effect comes from. ( Visual bullets )
    --- @return Vector The new position to start tracer effect from
    @side(client)
    function GetTracerOrigin(): Vector | nil
    --- This hook allows you to adjust view model position and angles.
    --- @param EyePos Current position
    --- @param EyeAng Current angle
    --- @return Vector New position
    --- @return Angle New angle
    @side(client)
    function GetViewModelPosition(EyePos: Vector, EyeAng: Angle): Vector | nil
    --- Called when weapon tries to holster.
    --- **NOTE**: This will only be called serverside when using `Player:SelectWeapon` as that function immediately switches the weapon out of prediction.
    --- This is called twice for every holster clientside, one in `Prediction` and one not.
    --- Before `WEAPON:OnRemove` is called, this function is only called serverside.
    --- @param weapon The weapon we are trying switch to.
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow weapon to holster. This will not have an effect if weapon was switched away from using Player:SetActiveWeapon
    @side(shared)
    function Holster(weapon: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- This hook determines which parts of the HUD to draw.
    --- @param element The HUD element in question
    --- @return boolean Return false to hide this HUD element
    @side(client)
    function HUDShouldDraw(element: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the weapon entity is created.
    --- **NOTE**: `Entity:GetOwner` will return NULL at this point because the weapon is not equpped by a player or NPC yet. Use `WEAPON:Equip` or `WEAPON:Deploy` if you need the owner to be valid.
    --- This is not called serverside after a quicksave.
    @side(shared)
    function Initialize(): any
    --- Called when the engine sets a value for this scripted weapon.
    --- See `GM:EntityKeyValue` for a hook that works for all entities.
    --- See `ENTITY:KeyValue` for an  hook that works for scripted entities.
    --- @param key The key that was affected.
    --- @param value The new value.
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress this KeyValue or return false or nothing to apply this key value.
    @side(server)
    function KeyValue(key: string, value: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called internally during `TASK_RANGE_ATTACK1 --> OnRangeAttack1`. This allows you to separate your SWEPs primary firing function from players and NPCs.
    --- To get the delay the NPC will fire again, you can call `self:GetOwner():GetInternalVariable("m_flNextAttack")`
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called internally only for NPCs that has `CAP_USE_SHOT_REGULATOR` set.
    --- @param shootPos The world position the NPC will use as attack starting position. You can create your projectiles here.
    --- @param shootDir The direction the NPC wants to shoot at.
    @side(server)
    function NPCShoot_Primary(shootPos: Vector | nil, shootDir: Vector | nil): any
    --- A utility function to seperate your SWEPs secondary firing from players.
    --- Unlike `WEAPON:NPCShoot_Primary`, this won't be called by the engine for `TASK_RANGE_ATTACK2`.
    --- @param shootPos The world position the NPC will use as attack starting position. You can create your projectiles here.
    --- @param shootDir The direction the NPC wants to shoot at.
    @side(server)
    function NPCShoot_Secondary(shootPos: Vector | nil, shootDir: Vector | nil): any
    --- Called when weapon is dropped by `Player:DropWeapon`.
    --- See also `WEAPON:OwnerChanged`.
    --- @param owner The entity that dropped the weapon.
    @side(server)
    function OnDrop(owner: Entity): any
    --- Called whenever the weapons Lua script is reloaded.
    @side(shared)
    function OnReloaded(): any
    --- Called when the `Scripted Weapon` is about to be removed.
    --- `Entity:GetOwner` may be unset at this point, see `WEAPON:OnDrop` and `WEAPON:OwnerChanged`.
    @side(shared)
    function OnRemove(): any
    --- Called when the weapon entity is reloaded from a Source Engine save (not the Sandbox saves or dupes) or on a changelevel (for example Half-Life 2 campaign level transitions).
    --- For the `duplicator` callbacks, see `ENTITY:OnDuplicated`.
    --- See also `saverestore` for relevant functions.
    @side(shared)
    function OnRestore(): any
    --- Called when weapon is dropped or picked up by a new player. This can be called clientside for all players on the server if the weapon has no owner and is picked up.
    --- See also `WEAPON:OnDrop`.
    @side(shared)
    function OwnerChanged(): any
    --- Called after the view model has been drawn while the weapon in use.
    --- This hook relies on default implementation of `GM:PostDrawViewModel`. If it appears to not work, it may have been overwritten/broken by the currently active gamemode or other addons.
    --- `WEAPON:ViewModelDrawn` is an alternative hook which is always called before `GM:PostDrawViewModel`.
    --- See also `WEAPON:PreDrawViewModel`.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity after it is drawn
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model (same as self)
    --- @param ply The owner of the view model
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    function PostDrawViewModel(vm: Entity, weapon: Weapon, ply: Player, flags: number): any
    --- Allows you to modify viewmodel while the weapon in use before it is drawn.
    --- This hook relies on default implementation of `GM:PreDrawViewModel`. If it appears to not work, it may have been overwritten/broken by the currently active gamemode or other addons.
    --- See also `WEAPON:ViewModelDrawn` and `WEAPON:PostDrawViewModel`.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity before it is drawn.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param ply The the owner of the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent the default action of rendering the view model. `PostDrawViewModel` will NOT be called in this scenario.
    @side(client)
    function PreDrawViewModel(vm: Entity, weapon: Weapon, ply: Player, flags: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called when primary attack button ( +attack ) is pressed.
    --- When in singleplayer, this function is only called in the server realm. When in multiplayer, the hook will be called on both the server and the client in order to allow for `Prediction`.
    --- You can force the hook to always be called on client like this:
    --- ```
    --- if ( game.SinglePlayer() ) then self:CallOnClient( "PrimaryAttack" ) end
    --- ```
    --- Note that due to prediction, in multiplayer SWEP:PrimaryAttack is called multiple times per one "shot" with the gun. To work around that, use `Global.IsFirstTimePredicted`.
    @side(shared)
    function PrimaryAttack(): any
    --- A convenience function that draws the weapon info box, used in `WEAPON:DrawWeaponSelection`.
    --- @param x The x co-ordinate of box position
    --- @param y The y co-ordinate of box position
    --- @param alpha Alpha value for the box
    @side(client)
    function PrintWeaponInfo(x: number, y: number, alpha: number): any
    --- Called when the reload key ( +reload ) is pressed.
    @side(shared)
    function Reload(): any
    --- Called every frame just before `GM:RenderScene`.
    --- Used by the Tool Gun to render view model screens (`TOOL:DrawToolScreen`).
    --- **NOTE**: Materials rendered in this hook require $ignorez parameter to draw properly.
    @side(client)
    function RenderScreen(): any
    --- Called when secondary attack button ( +attack2 ) is pressed.
    --- For issues with this hook being called rapidly on the client side, see the global function `Global.IsFirstTimePredicted`.
    @side(shared)
    function SecondaryAttack(): any
    --- Called when the SWEP should set up its ` Data Tables`.
    @side(shared)
    function SetupDataTables(): any
    --- Sets the hold type of the weapon. This must be called on **both** the server and the client to work properly.
    --- **NOTE**: You should avoid calling this function and call `Weapon:SetHoldType` now.
    --- @param name Name of the hold type. You can find all default hold types Hold_Types
    @side(shared)
    function SetWeaponHoldType(name: string): any
    --- A convenient function to shoot bullets.
    --- @param damage The damage of the bullet
    --- @param num_bullets Amount of bullets to shoot
    --- @param aimcone Spread of bullets
    --- @param ammo_type Ammo type of the bullets
    --- @param force Force of the bullets
    --- @param tracer Show a tracer on every x bullets
    @side(shared)
    function ShootBullet(damage: number, num_bullets: number, aimcone: number, ammo_type: string | nil, force: number | nil, tracer: number | nil): any
    --- A convenience function to create shoot effects.
    @side(shared)
    function ShootEffects(): any
    --- Called to determine if the view model should be drawn or not.
    --- @return boolean Return true to draw the view model, false otherwise.
    @side(client)
    function ShouldDrawViewModel(): boolean | nil
    --- Should this weapon be dropped when its owner dies?
    --- This only works if the player has `Player:ShouldDropWeapon` set to true.
    --- @return boolean Return true to drop the weapon, false otherwise. Default ( if you don't return anything ) is false.
    @side(server)
    function ShouldDropOnDie(): boolean | nil
    --- A convenience function to remove primary ammo from clip.
    --- @param amount Amount of primary ammo to remove
    @side(shared)
    function TakePrimaryAmmo(amount: number): any
    --- A convenience function to remove secondary ammo from clip.
    --- @param amount How much of secondary ammo to remove
    @side(shared)
    function TakeSecondaryAmmo(amount: number): any
    --- Called when the weapon thinks.
    --- This hook won't be called during the deploy animation and when using `Weapon:DefaultReload`.
    --- **NOTE**: If you wish for this hook to be called during the deploy animation, add the following to the model's **ACT_VM_DRAW** sequence: `node "Ready"`
    --- Despite being a predicted hook, this hook is called clientside in single player (for your convenience), however it will not be recognized as a predicted hook via `Player:GetCurrentCommand`, and will run more often in this case.
    --- This hook will be called before Player movement is processed on the client, and after on the server.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook only runs while the weapon is in players hands. It does not run while it is carried by an NPC.
    --- This will not be run during deploy animations after a serverside-only deploy. This usually happens after picking up and dropping an object with +use.
    @side(shared)
    function Think(): any
    --- Alias of `Weapon:Think`.
    --- @deprecated Use Weapon:Think instead.
    @side(shared)
    function Tick(): any
    --- Translate a generic activity into a more specific activity, such as holdtype-specific activities.
    --- The translated activity is then used to request animations from the owner's model via `Entity:SelectWeightedSequence` and similar functions.
    --- For example, `ACT_MP_RUN` becomes `ACT_HL2MP_RUN_PISTOL`.
    --- @param act The activity to translate
    --- @return number The translated activity
    @side(shared)
    function TranslateActivity(act: number): number | nil
    --- Allows to change players field of view while player holds the weapon.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook must be defined shared and return same value on both to properly affect Area Portals.
    --- @param fov The current/default FOV.
    --- @return number The target FOV.
    @side(shared)
    function TranslateFOV(fov: number): number | nil
    --- Called straight after the view model has been drawn. This is called before `GM:PostDrawViewModel` and `WEAPON:PostDrawViewModel`.
    --- See `WEAPON:DrawWorldModel` for world model rendering.
    --- See also `WEAPON:PreDrawViewModel` and `WEAPON:PostDrawViewModel`.
    --- @param ViewModel Players view model
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    function ViewModelDrawn(ViewModel: Entity, flags: number): any
end
declare SWEP: ScriptedWeapon

--- The hooks of the gamemode, by event name, as `hook.Add` registers them.
declare interface GMHooks
    --- Called when a map I/O event occurs.
    --- See also `Entity:Fire` and `Entity:Input` for functions to fire Inputs on entities.
    --- @param ent Entity that receives the input
    --- @param input The input name. Is not guaranteed to be a valid input on the entity.
    --- @param activator Activator of the input
    --- @param caller Caller of the input
    --- @param value Data provided with the input. Will be either a string, a number, a boolean or a nil.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent this input from being processed. Do not return otherwise.
    @side(server)
    AcceptInput: ((Entity, string, Entity, Entity, any) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Adds a death notice entry.
    --- @param attacker The name of the attacker
    --- @param attackerTeam The team of the attacker
    --- @param inflictor Class name of the entity inflicting the damage
    --- @param victim Name of the victim
    --- @param victimTeam Team of the victim
    --- @return any `true/false` to prevent the notice from being shown. Do not return otherwise.
    @side(client)
    AddDeathNotice: ((string, number, string, string, number) -> any | nil)?
    --- Allows you to adjust the mouse sensitivity.
    --- @param defaultSensitivity The old sensitivity In general it will be 0, which is equivalent to a sensitivity of 1.
    --- @param localFOV Player's current FOV.
    --- @param defaultFOV Default FOV.
    --- @return number A fraction of the normal sensitivity (0.5 would be half as sensitive). Return -1 to not override and prevent subsequent hooks and WEAPON:AdjustMouseSensitivity from running. Return nil to not override and allow subsequent hooks and WEAPON:AdjustMouseSensitivity to run.
    @side(client)
    AdjustMouseSensitivity: ((number, number, number) -> number | nil)?
    --- Called when a player tries to pick up something using the "use" key, return to override.
    --- This hook will not be called if `sv_playerpickupallowed` is set to 0.
    --- See `GM:GravGunPickupAllowed` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player trying to pick up something.
    --- @param ent The Entity the player attempted to pick up.
    --- @return boolean Allow the player to pick up the entity or not.
    @side(server)
    AllowPlayerPickup: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- This hook is used to calculate animations for a player.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook must return the same values at the same time on both, client **and** server. On client for players to see the animations, on server for hit detection to work properly.
    --- @param ply The player to apply the animation.
    --- @param vel The velocity of the player.
    --- @return number Enums/ACT for the activity the player should use. A nil return will be treated as ACT_INVALID.
    --- @return number Sequence for the player to use. This takes precedence over the activity (the activity is still used for layering). Return -1 or nil to let the activity determine the sequence.
    @side(shared)
    CalcMainActivity: ((Player, Vector) -> number | nil)?
    --- Called from `GM:CalcView` when player is in driving a vehicle.
    --- This hook may not be called in gamemodes that override `GM:CalcView`.
    --- @param veh The vehicle the player is driving
    --- @param ply The vehicle driver
    --- @param view The view data containing players FOV, view position and angles, see Structures/CamData
    --- @return { [any]: any } The modified view table containing new values, see Structures/CamData
    @side(client)
    CalcVehicleView: ((Vehicle, Player, { [any]: any }) -> { [any]: any } | nil)?
    --- Allows override of the default view.
    --- **NOTE**: To avoid breaking compatibility with other addons, it is recommended to add onto the origin and angle values using `Vector:Add` or `Angle:Add` instead of overriding them completely.
    --- @param ply The local player.
    --- @param origin The player's view position.
    --- @param angles The player's view angles.
    --- @param fov Field of view.
    --- @param znear Distance to near clipping plane.
    --- @param zfar Distance to far clipping plane.
    --- @return CamData View data table. See Structures/CamData.
    @side(client)
    CalcView: ((Player, Vector, Angle, number, number, number) -> CamData | nil)?
    --- Allows overriding the position and angle of the viewmodel.
    --- @param wep The weapon entity
    --- @param vm The viewmodel entity
    --- @param oldPos Original position (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param oldAng Original angle (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param pos Current position
    --- @param ang Current angle
    --- @return Vector New position
    --- @return Angle New angle
    @side(client)
    CalcViewModelView: ((Weapon, Entity, Vector, Angle, Vector, Angle) -> Vector | nil)?
    --- Called whenever a players tries to create an undo.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to create something.
    --- @param undo The undo table as a Structures/Undo.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow creation of the undo.
    @side(server)
    CanCreateUndo: ((Player, { [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a variable is about to be edited on an Entity (called by `Edit Properties...` menu), to determine if the edit should be permitted.
    --- See `Editable entities` for more details about the system.
    --- By default, Sandbox will also call `ENTITY:CanEditVariables` if no hook returns a value.
    --- @param ent The entity being edited.
    --- @param ply The player doing the editing.
    --- @param key The name of the variable.
    --- @param value The new value, as a string which will later be converted to its appropriate type.
    --- @param editor The edit table defined in Entity:NetworkVar.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to disallow editing.
    @side(server)
    CanEditVariable: ((Entity, Player, string, string, { [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Determines if the player can exit the vehicle on their own. `Player:ExitVehicle` will bypass this hook.
    --- See `GM:CanPlayerEnterVehicle` for the opposite hook.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerLeaveVehicle` for a hook that will be called whenever a player exits any vehicle for any reason.
    --- @param veh The vehicle entity
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return boolean True if the player can exit the vehicle.
    @side(server)
    CanExitVehicle: ((Vehicle, Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Determines whether or not a given player player can enter the given vehicle. `Player:EnterVehicle` will still call this hook.
    --- Called just before `GM:PlayerEnteredVehicle`. See also `GM:CanExitVehicle`.
    --- @param player The player that wants to enter a vehicle.
    --- @param vehicle The vehicle in question.
    --- @param role The seat number.
    --- @return boolean `false` if the player is not allowed to enter the vehicle.
    @side(server)
    CanPlayerEnterVehicle: ((Player, Vehicle, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Determines if the player can kill themselves using the `kill` or `explode` console commands.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @return boolean `true` if the player should be allowed to suicide, `false` if not.
    @side(server)
    CanPlayerSuicide: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Determines if the player can unfreeze the entity.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @param entity The entity
    --- @param phys The physics object of the entity
    --- @return boolean True if they can unfreeze.
    @side(server)
    CanPlayerUnfreeze: ((Player, Entity, PhysObj) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Controls if a `property` can be used or not.
    --- @param ply Player, that tried to use the property
    --- @param property Class of the property that is tried to use, for example - bonemanipulate This is not guaranteed to be the internal property name used in `properties.Add`!
    --- @param ent The entity, on which property is tried to be used on
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow using that property
    @side(shared)
    CanProperty: ((Player, string, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called whenever a players tries to undo.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to undo something.
    --- @param undo The undo table as a Structures/Undo.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow the undo.
    @side(server)
    CanUndo: ((Player, Undo) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called each frame to record demos to video using `IVideoWriter`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called every frame regardless of whether or not a demo is being recorded
    @side(client)
    CaptureVideo: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a message is printed to the chat box. Note, that this isn't working with player messages even though there are arguments for it.
    --- For player messages see `GM:PlayerSay` and `GM:OnPlayerChat`
    --- @param index The index of the player.
    --- @param name The name of the player.
    --- @param text The text that is being sent.
    --- @param type Chat filter type. Possible values are: * `joinleave` - Player join and leave messages * `namechange` - Player name change messages * `servermsg` - Server messages such as convar changes * `teamchange` - Team changes? * `chat` - (Obsolete?) Player chat? Seems to trigger when server console uses the `say` command * `none` - A fallback value
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress the chat message.
    @side(client)
    ChatText: ((number, string, string, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called whenever the content of the user's chat input box is changed.
    --- @param text The new contents of the input box
    @side(client)
    ChatTextChanged: ((string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a **non local player** connects to allow the Lua system to check the password.
    --- The default behaviour in the base gamemodes emulates what would normally happen. If `sv_password` is set and its value matches the password passed in by the client (via `password` concommand) - then they are allowed to join. If `sv_password` isn't set it lets them in too.
    --- @param steamID64 The 64bit Steam ID of the joining player, use util.SteamIDFrom64 to convert it to a `STEAM_0:` one.
    --- @param ipAddress The IP of the connecting client
    --- @param svPassword The current value of sv_password (the password set by the server)
    --- @param clPassword The password provided by the client
    --- @param name The name of the joining player
    --- @return boolean If the hook returns `false` then the player is disconnected
    --- @return string If returning false in the first argument, then this should be the disconnect message. This will default to `#GameUI_ServerRejectBadPassword`, which is `Bad Password.` translated to the client's language.
    @side(server)
    CheckPassword: ((string, string, string, string, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player's sign on state changes.
    --- You cannot get a valid player object from the userID at any point during this hook.
    --- @param userID The userID of the player whose sign on state has changed.
    --- @param oldState The previous sign on state. See Enums/SIGNONSTATE enums.
    --- @param newState The new/current sign on state. See Enums/SIGNONSTATE enums.
    @side(shared)
    ClientSignOnStateChanged: ((number, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when derma menus are closed with `Global.CloseDermaMenus`.
    @side(client)
    CloseDermaMenus: (() -> any)?
    --- Called whenever an entity becomes a clientside ragdoll.
    --- See `GM:CreateEntityRagdoll` for serverside ragdolls.
    --- @param entity The Entity that created the ragdoll
    --- @param ragdoll The ragdoll being created.
    @side(client)
    CreateClientsideRagdoll: ((Entity, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when a serverside ragdoll of an entity has been created.
    --- See `GM:CreateClientsideRagdoll` for clientside ragdolls.
    --- @param owner Entity that owns the ragdoll
    --- @param ragdoll The ragdoll entity
    @side(server)
    CreateEntityRagdoll: ((Entity, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Allows you to change the players movements before they're sent to the server.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- **NOTE**: Due to this hook being clientside only, it could be overridden by the user allowing them to completely skip your logic, it is recommended to use `GM:StartCommand` in a shared file instead.
    --- @param cmd The User Command data
    --- @return boolean Return true to: * Disable Sandbox C menu "screen clicking" * Disable Teammate nocollide (verification required) * Prevent calling of C_BaseHLPlayer::CreateMove & subsequently C_BasePlayer::CreateMove
    @side(client)
    CreateMove: ((CUserCmd) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Teams are created within this hook using `team.SetUp`.
    --- This hook is called before `GM:PreGamemodeLoaded`.
    @side(shared)
    CreateTeams: (() -> any)?
    --- Called upon an animation event, this is the ideal place to call player animation functions such as `Player:AddVCDSequenceToGestureSlot`, `Player:AnimRestartGesture` and so on.
    --- @param ply Player who is being animated
    --- @param event Animation event. See Enums/PLAYERANIMEVENT
    --- @param data The data for the event. This is interpreted as an Enums/ACT by `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM` and `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM_GESTURE`, or a sequence by `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM_SEQUENCE`.
    --- @return number The translated activity to send to the weapon. See Enums/ACT. Return `ACT_INVALID` if you don't want to send an activity.
    @side(shared)
    DoAnimationEvent: ((Player, number, number) -> number | nil)?
    --- Handles the player's death.
    --- This hook is **not** called if the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`. See `GM:PlayerSilentDeath` for that.
    --- * `GM:PlayerDeath` is called after this hook
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called after that
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param attacker The entity that killed the player
    --- @param dmg Damage info
    @side(server)
    DoPlayerDeath: ((Player, Entity, CTakeDamageInfo) -> any)?
    --- This hook is called every frame to draw all of the current death notices.
    --- @param x X position to draw death notices as a ratio
    --- @param y Y position to draw death notices as a ratio
    @side(client)
    DrawDeathNotice: ((number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called every frame before drawing the in-game monitors ( Breencast, in-game TVs, etc ), but doesn't seem to be doing anything, trying to render 2D or 3D elements fail.
    @side(client)
    DrawMonitors: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after all other 2D draw hooks are called. Draws over all VGUI Panels and HUDs.
    --- Unlike `GM:HUDPaint`, this hook is called with the game paused and while the Camera SWEP is equipped.
    --- Does not get called when `r_drawvgui` is disabled.
    @side(client)
    DrawOverlay: (() -> any)?
    --- Allows you to override physgun effects rendering.
    --- **NOTE**: This is still called when `physgun_drawbeams` is set to `0`, because this hook is also capable of overriding physgun sprite effects, while the convar does not.
    --- @param ply Physgun owner
    --- @param physgun The physgun
    --- @param enabled Is the beam enabled
    --- @param target Entity we are grabbing. This will be NULL if nothing is being held
    --- @param physBone ID of the physics bone (PhysObj) we are grabbing at. Use Entity:TranslatePhysBoneToBone to translate to an actual bone.
    --- @param hitPos Beam hit position relative to the physics bone (PhysObj) we are grabbing.
    --- @return boolean Return false to hide default effects
    @side(client)
    DrawPhysgunBeam: ((Player, Weapon, boolean, Entity, number, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called right before an entity stops driving. Overriding this hook will cause it to not call `drive.End` and the player will not stop driving.
    --- @param ent The entity being driven
    --- @param ply The player driving the entity
    @side(shared)
    EndEntityDriving: ((Entity, Player) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a sound has been played. This will not be called clientside if the server played the sound without the client also calling `Entity:EmitSound`.
    --- @param data Information about the played sound. Changes done to this table can be applied by returning `true` from this hook. See Structures/EmitSoundInfo.
    --- @return boolean * Return `true` to apply all changes done to the data table. * Return `false` to prevent the sound from playing. * Return `nil` or nothing to play the sound without altering it.
    @side(shared)
    EntityEmitSound: (({ [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called every time a bullet is about to be fired from an entity, which allows to completely modify the bullet structure before the bullet is actually fired.
    --- See `GM:PostEntityFireBullets` if you wish to hook the final bullet values, such as the aim direction post spread calculations.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called directly from `Entity:FireBullets`. Due to this, you cannot call `Entity:FireBullets` inside this hook or an infinite loop will occur crashing the game.
    --- @param entity The entity that fired the bullet
    --- @param data The bullet data. See Structures/Bullet.
    --- @return boolean * Return `true` to apply all changes done to the bullet table. * Return `false` to suppress the bullet.
    @side(shared)
    EntityFireBullets: ((Entity, Bullet) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a key-value pair is set on an entity on map spawn. Is **not** called by `Entity:SetKeyValue`.
    --- See `ENTITY:KeyValue` for a `scripted entities` hook, and its scripted weapon alternative: `WEAPON:KeyValue`.
    --- @param ent Entity that the keyvalue is being set on
    --- @param key Key of the key/value pair
    --- @param value Value of the key/value pair
    --- @return string If set, the value of the key-value pair will be overridden by this string.
    @side(shared)
    EntityKeyValue: ((Entity, string, string) -> string | nil)?
    --- Called when an NW2Var is changed.
    --- If a NW2Var is set on an entity that is based on a Lua Entity could result in the NW2Var being mixed up with other ones and being updated multiple times.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is fired before the client value is actually changed. Calling the GetNW2 function for the specified variable name within this hook will return the old value, not the current/updated one.
    --- This hook gets called for all NW2Vars on all Entities in a full update. The old value will be nil in this case.
    --- If this hook seems to be called for no apparent reason, check if it's caused by a full update.
    --- @param ent The owner entity of the changed NW2Var
    --- @param name The name of the changed NW2Var
    --- @param oldval The old value of the NW2Var
    --- @param newval The new value of the NW2Var
    @side(shared)
    EntityNetworkedVarChanged: ((Entity, string, any, any) -> any)?
    --- Called right before removal of an entity.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called clientside during full updates due to how networking works in the Source Engine.
    --- This can happen when the client briefly loses connection to the server, and can be simulated via `cl_fullupdate` for testing purposes.
    --- @param ent Entity being removed
    --- @param fullUpdate Whether the removal is happening due to a full update clientside. The entity may or **may not** be recreated immediately after, depending on whether it is in the local player's [PVS](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). (See Entity:IsDormant)
    @side(shared)
    EntityRemoved: ((Entity, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called when an entity is about to take damage. You can modify all parts of the damage info in this hook or completely block the damage event.
    --- See `GM:PostEntityTakeDamage` if you wish to hook the final damage event.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the entity taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param target The entity taking damage
    --- @param dmg Detailed information about the damage event. When you retrieve "the attacker" the player's angle and position will be incorrect.
    --- @return boolean Return true to completely block the damage event
    @side(server)
    EntityTakeDamage: ((Entity, CTakeDamageInfo) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- This hook polls the entity the player use action should be applied to.
    --- **NOTE**: The default behavior of this hook is in [CBasePlayer::FindUseEntity](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/0d8dceea4310fde5706b3ce1c70609d72a38efdf/mp/src/game/shared/baseplayer_shared.cpp#L1068-L1270). Despite CBasePlayer::FindUseEntity being defined shared, it is only called serverside in practice, so this hook will be only called serverside, as well. It is possible for modules to call it clientside, so the Lua code should still be treated as shared.
    --- @param ply The player who initiated the use action.
    --- @param defaultEnt The entity that was chosen by the engine.
    --- @return Entity The entity to use instead of default entity
    @side(shared)
    FindUseEntity: ((Player, Entity) -> Entity | nil)?
    --- Runs when user cancels/finishes typing.
    @side(client)
    FinishChat: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after `GM:Move`, applies all the changes from the `CMoveData` to the player.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply Player
    --- @param mv Movement data
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default engine behavior, i.e. declare that you have already moved the player according to the move data in a custom way.
    @side(shared)
    FinishMove: ((Player, CMoveData) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to allow override of the default Derma skin for all panels.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is only called on Lua start up, changing its value (or adding new hooks) after it has been already called will not have any effect.
    --- **NOTE**: You can `Panel:SetSkin` "Default" (or other skins) on the frame/base panel and they will still take priority
    --- @return string A **case sensitive** Derma skin name to be used as default, registered previously via derma.DefineSkin. Returning nothing, nil or invalid name will make it fallback to the "Default" skin.
    @side(client)
    ForceDermaSkin: (() -> string | nil)?
    --- Called when game content has been changed, for example an addon or a mountable game was (un)mounted.
    @side(shared)
    GameContentChanged: (() -> any)?
    --- An internal function used to get an untranslated string to show in the kill feed as the entity's name. See `GM:SendDeathNotice`
    --- @param name The name of the entity.
    --- @return string The untranslated name for given NPC. The translation/localization would happen on the client.
    @side(server)
    GetDeathNoticeEntityName: ((string | Entity) -> string | nil)?
    --- Called when a player takes damage from falling, allows to override the damage.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param speed The fall speed
    --- @return number New fall damage
    @side(server)
    GetFallDamage: ((Player, number) -> number | nil)?
    --- Called when the game(server) needs to update the text shown in the server browser as the gamemode. Runs at a ~2s interval, runs even when the server is hibernating. This hook doesn't run when `hide_server 1` is set.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook (and the `sv_gamename_override` command) may not work on some popular gamemodes like DarkRP or Trouble Terrorist Town. This is not a bug, it's just how it works. See [here](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/4637#issuecomment-677884989) for more information.
    --- Also, it **only** works on dedicated servers and is called at regular intervals (about one second) **even** if the server has no players and the hibernation function is enabled.
    --- @return string The text to be shown in the server browser as the gamemode.
    @side(shared)
    GetGameDescription: (() -> string | nil)?
    --- Allows you to modify the Source Engine's motion blur shaders.
    --- @param horizontal The amount of horizontal blur.
    --- @param vertical The amount of vertical  blur.
    --- @param forward The amount of forward/radial blur.
    --- @param rotational The amount of rotational blur.
    --- @return number New amount of horizontal blur.
    --- @return number New amount of vertical blur.
    --- @return number New amount of forward/radial blur.
    --- @return number New amount of rotational blur.
    @side(client)
    GetMotionBlurValues: ((number, number, number, number) -> number | nil)?
    --- Called to determine preferred carry angles for the entity. It works for both, +use pickup and gravity gun pickup.
    --- **WARNING**: Due to nature of the gravity gun coding in multiplayer, this hook **MAY** seem to not work ( but rest assured it does ), due to clientside prediction not knowing the carry angles. The +use pickup doesn't present this issue as it doesn't predict the player carrying the object clientside ( as you may notice by the prop lagging behind in multiplayer )
    --- **NOTE**: This hook can **not** override preferred carry angles of props such as the sawblade and the harpoon.
    --- @param ent The entity to generate carry angles for
    --- @param ply The player who is holding the object
    --- @return Angle The preferred carry angles for the entity.
    @side(server)
    GetPreferredCarryAngles: ((Entity, Player) -> Angle | nil)?
    --- Returns the color for the given entity's team. This is used in chat and deathnotice text.
    --- @param ent Entity
    --- @return Color Team Color
    @side(client)
    GetTeamColor: ((Entity) -> Color | nil)?
    --- Returns the team color for the given team index.
    --- @param team Team index
    --- @return Color Team Color
    @side(client)
    GetTeamNumColor: ((number) -> Color | nil)?
    --- Override this hook to disable/change ear-grabbing in your gamemode. By default, it is not called anywhere on the server.
    --- @param ply Player
    @side(shared)
    GrabEarAnimation: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when an entity is released by a gravity gun.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunDrop` for the Physics Gun drop variant.
    --- @param ply Player who is wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity that has been dropped
    @side(server)
    GravGunOnDropped: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when an entity is picked up by a gravity gun.
    --- See `GM:OnPlayerPhysicsPickup` for the player `+use` pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity that has been picked up by the gravity gun
    @side(server)
    GravGunOnPickedUp: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called every tick to poll whether a player is allowed to pick up an entity with the gravity gun or not.
    --- See `GM:AllowPlayerPickup` for the +USE pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- Calls `ENTITY:GravGunPickupAllowed` on the entity being hovered every frame in Sandbox-derived gamemodes.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity the player is attempting to pick up
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow entity pick up
    @side(server)
    GravGunPickupAllowed: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when an entity is about to be punted with the gravity gun (primary fire).
    --- By default this function makes `ENTITY:GravGunPunt` work in Sandbox derived gamemodes.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity the player is attempting to punt
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow and false to disallow.
    @side(shared)
    GravGunPunt: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the mouse has been double clicked on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- By default this hook calls `GM:GUIMousePressed`.
    --- @param mouseCode The code of the mouse button pressed, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @param aimVector A normalized vector pointing in the direction the client has clicked
    @side(client)
    GUIMouseDoublePressed: ((number, Vector) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a players presses a mouse key on the context menu in Sandbox or on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- See `GM:VGUIMousePressed` for a hook that is called on all VGUI elements.
    --- @param mouseCode The key that the player pressed using Enums/MOUSE.
    --- @param aimVector A normalized direction vector local to the camera. Internally, this is  gui.ScreenToVector( gui.MousePos() ).
    @side(client)
    GUIMousePressed: ((number, Vector) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a players releases a mouse key on the context menu in Sandbox or on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- @param mouseCode The key the player released, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @param aimVector A normalized direction vector local to the camera. Internally this is  gui.ScreenToVector( gui.MousePos() ).
    @side(client)
    GUIMouseReleased: ((number, Vector) -> any)?
    --- Called to handle player armor reduction, when player receives damage.
    --- Clarify hook order with other damage hooks.
    --- @param ply The player that took damage.
    --- @param dmginfo The taken damage.
    @side(server)
    HandlePlayerArmorReduction: ((Player, CTakeDamageInfo) -> any)?
    --- Allows to override player driving animations.
    --- @param ply Player to process
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerDriving: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows to override player crouch animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerDucking: ((Player, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called every frame by the player model animation system. Allows to override player jumping animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerJumping: ((Player, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called every frame by the player model animation system. Allows to override player landing animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @param onGround Was the player on ground?
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerLanding: ((Player, Vector, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows to override player noclip animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerNoClipping: ((Player, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows to override player swimming animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerSwimming: ((Player, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows to override player flying ( in mid-air, not noclipping ) animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    HandlePlayerVaulting: ((Player, Vector) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Hides the team selection panel.
    @side(client)
    HideTeam: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the client has picked up ammo. Override to disable default HUD notification.
    --- @param itemName Name of the item (ammo) picked up
    --- @param amount Amount of the item (ammo) picked up
    @side(client)
    HUDAmmoPickedUp: ((string, number) -> any)?
    --- Renders the HUD pick-up history. Override to hide default or draw your own HUD.
    @side(client)
    HUDDrawPickupHistory: (() -> any)?
    --- Called every frame to render the scoreboard.
    --- It is recommended to use Derma and VGUI for this job instead of this hook. Called right after `GM:HUDPaint`.
    @side(client)
    HUDDrawScoreBoard: (() -> any)?
    --- Called from `GM:HUDPaint` to draw player info when you hover over a player with your crosshair or mouse.
    --- @return boolean Should the player info be drawn.
    @side(client)
    HUDDrawTargetID: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when an item has been picked up. Override to disable the default HUD notification.
    --- @param itemName Name of the picked up item
    @side(client)
    HUDItemPickedUp: ((string) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever the HUD should be drawn.
    --- This is the ideal place to draw custom HUD elements.
    --- To prevent the default game HUD from drawing, use `GM:HUDShouldDraw`.
    --- This hook does **not** get called when the Camera SWEP is held, or when the esc menu is open.
    --- If you need to draw in those situations, use `GM:DrawOverlay` instead.
    @side(client)
    HUDPaint: (() -> any)?
    --- Called before `GM:HUDPaint` when the HUD background is being drawn.
    --- Just like `GM:HUDPaint`, this hook will not be called when the main menu is visible. `GM:PostDrawHUD` does not have this behavior.
    --- Things rendered in this hook will **always** appear behind things rendered in `GM:HUDPaint`.
    @side(client)
    HUDPaintBackground: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the Gamemode is about to draw a given element on the client's HUD (heads-up display).
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called HUNDREDS of times per second (more than 5 times per frame on average). You shouldn't be performing any computationally intensive operations. For Weapons you SHOULD use `WEAPON:HUDShouldDraw` instead.
    --- @param name The name of the HUD element. You can find a full list of HUD elements for this hook HUD_Element_List.
    --- @return boolean Return false to prevent the given element from being drawn on the client's screen.
    @side(client)
    HUDShouldDraw: ((string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a weapon has been picked up. Override to disable the default HUD notification.
    --- @param weapon The picked up weapon
    @side(client)
    HUDWeaponPickedUp: ((Weapon) -> any)?
    --- Called after the gamemode loads and starts.
    --- No entities would be present at the time this hook is called, please see `GM:InitPostEntity` for a one time fire hook after all map entities have been initialized.
    @side(shared)
    Initialize: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after all the entities are initialized. Starting from this hook `Global.LocalPlayer` will return valid object.
    --- **NOTE**: At this point the client only knows about the entities that are within the spawnpoints' [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). For instance, if the server sends an entity that is not within this PVS, the client will receive it as NULL entity.
    @side(shared)
    InitPostEntity: (() -> any)?
    --- Allows you to modify the supplied User Command with mouse input. This could be used to make moving the mouse do funky things to view angles.
    --- @param cmd User command.
    --- @param x The amount of mouse movement across the X axis this frame.
    --- @param y The amount of mouse movement across the Y axis this frame.
    --- @param ang The current view angle.
    --- @return boolean Return true if we modified something.
    @side(client)
    InputMouseApply: ((CUserCmd, number, number, Angle) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Check if a player can spawn at a certain spawnpoint.
    --- @param ply The player who is spawned
    --- @param spawnpoint The spawnpoint entity (on the map).
    --- @param makeSuitable If this is true, it'll kill any players blocking the spawnpoint.
    --- @return boolean Return true to indicate that the spawnpoint is suitable (Allow for the player to spawn here), false to prevent spawning.
    @side(server)
    IsSpawnpointSuitable: ((Player, Entity, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called whenever a player pressed a key included within the IN keys.
    --- For a more general purpose function that handles all kinds of input, see `GM:PlayerButtonDown`.
    --- See `GM:KeyRelease` for the key release event.
    --- Despite being a predicted hook, it will still be called in singleplayer for your convenience.
    --- **WARNING**: Due to this being a predicted hook, `Global.ParticleEffect`s created only serverside from this hook will not be networked to the client, so make sure to do that on both realms.
    --- @param ply The player pressing the key. If running client-side, this will always be Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param key The key that the player pressed using Enums/IN.
    @side(shared)
    KeyPress: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Runs when a IN key was released by a player.
    --- For a more general purpose function that handles all kinds of input, see `GM:PlayerButtonUp`.
    --- See `GM:KeyPress` for the key press event.
    --- Despite being a predicted hook, it will still be called in singleplayer for your convenience.
    --- @param ply The player releasing the key. If running client-side, this will always be Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param key The key that the player released using Enums/IN.
    @side(shared)
    KeyRelease: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called from `gm_load` when the game should load a map.
    --- @param data Compressed save data
    --- @param map The name of the map the save was created on
    --- @param timestamp The time the save was created on. Will always be 0.
    @side(server)
    LoadGModSave: ((string, string, number) -> any)?
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is downloading. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param reason Failure Reason.
    --- @param workshopid the workshop ID of the missing map (if found). Can be an empty string
    @side(client)
    LoadGModSaveFailed: ((string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when `menu.lua` has finished loading.
    @side(client)
    MenuStart: (() -> any)?
    --- Override this gamemode function to disable mouth movement when talking on voice chat. By default, it is not called anywhere on the server.
    --- @param ply Player in question
    @side(shared)
    MouthMoveAnimation: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- The Move hook is called for you to manipulate the player's MoveData.
    --- You shouldn't adjust the player's position in any way in the move hook. This is because due to prediction errors, the netcode might run the move hook multiple times as packets arrive late. Therefore you should only adjust the movedata construct in this hook.
    --- Generally you shouldn't have to use this hook - if you want to make a custom move type you should look at the drive system.
    --- This hook is called after `GM:PlayerTick`.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply Player
    --- @param mv Movement information
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default engine action.
    @side(shared)
    Move: ((Player, CMoveData) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Returning true in this hook will cause it to render depth buffers defined with `render.GetResolvedFullFrameDepth`.
    --- @return boolean Render depth buffer
    @side(client)
    NeedsDepthPass: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when an entity has been created over the network.
    --- @param ent Created entity
    @side(client)
    NetworkEntityCreated: ((Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player's SteamID has been validated by Steam.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerAuthed` and `Player:IsFullyAuthenticated`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook doesn't work intentionally in singleplayer [because the SteamID is not validated](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/4906#issuecomment-819337130) in that case. This also applies to `sv_lan 1` servers for every duplicate `-multirun` client.
    --- @param name Player name
    --- @param steamID Player SteamID
    --- @param ownerID SteamID64 of the game license owner, in case Family Sharing is used. See also Player:OwnerSteamID64
    @side(server)
    NetworkIDValidated: ((string, string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever this entity changes its transmission state for this `Global.LocalPlayer`, such as exiting or re entering the [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community").
    --- **NOTE**: This is the best place to handle the reset of `Entity:SetPredictable`, as this would be usually called when the player lags and requests a full packet update.
    --- When the entity stops transmitting, `Entity:IsDormant` will only return true **after** this hook.
    --- @param entity The entity that changed its transmission state.
    --- @param shouldtransmit `True` if we started transmitting to this client and `false` if we stopped.
    @side(client)
    NotifyShouldTransmit: ((Entity, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player has achieved an achievement. You can get the name and other information from an achievement ID with the `achievements` library.
    --- @param ply The player that earned the achievement
    --- @param achievement The index of the achievement
    @side(client)
    OnAchievementAchieved: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when the local player presses TAB while having their chatbox opened.
    --- **WARNING**: This function now uses `player.Iterator`. This means it can't run all the time, as an error in the `GM:OnEntityCreated` or `GM:EntityRemoved` hooks is likely to interrupt it. Make sure that no addon causes an error in these hooks.
    --- @param text The currently typed into chatbox text
    --- @return string What should be placed into the chatbox instead of what currently is when player presses tab
    @side(client)
    OnChatTab: ((string) -> string | nil)?
    --- Called when the player cleans up something.
    --- @param name The name of the cleanup type
    --- @return boolean Return false to suppress the cleanup notification.
    @side(client)
    OnCleanup: ((string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called on the server when a Lua error occurs on a client and is sent to the server.
    --- This hook allows server-side code to detect and log client-side errors.
    --- See `GM:OnLuaError` for a hook that captures Lua errors directly within its `realm`.
    --- **WARNING**: Note that the stack argument can contain a table with 0 values.
    --- **NOTE**: Warning: the hook "protects" against lua error spam. If it has 5 errors in less than 1 second, the hook will not receive any of these 4 errors.
    --- @param error The error that occurred. As well as the path and line of the error. Example: `addons/test/lua/autorun/client/test_error.lua:4: 'then' expected near ''`
    --- @param ply The player whose client caused the error.
    --- @param stack The Lua error stack trace
    --- @param name Title of the addon that is creating the Lua errors, or "ERROR" if addon is not found.
    @side(server)
    OnClientLuaError: ((string, Player, { [any]: any }, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a caption/subtitle has been emitted to the closed caption box.
    --- @param soundScript The name of the soundscript, or `customLuaToken` if it's from gui.AddCaption
    --- @param duration How long the caption should stay for
    --- @param fromPlayer Is this caption coming from the player?
    --- @param fullText The caption. Can be nil if its token is not registered
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent the caption from appearing
    @side(client)
    OnCloseCaptionEmit: ((string, number, boolean, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the context menu keybind (+menu_context) is released, which by default is C.
    --- This hook will not run if `input.IsKeyTrapping` returns true.
    --- See also `GM:OnContextMenuOpen`.
    @side(client)
    OnContextMenuClose: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the context menu keybind (`+menu_context`) is pressed, which by default is C.
    --- See also `GM:OnContextMenuClose`.
    @side(client)
    OnContextMenuOpen: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the crazy physics detection detects an entity with crazy physics, i.e. position being far outside of the map, velocities being near or at infinity, etc. The primary reason for this system is to prevent program crashes in physics engine.
    --- @param ent The entity that was detected as crazy
    --- @param physobj The physics object that is going crazy
    @side(shared)
    OnCrazyPhysics: ((Entity, PhysObj) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player has been hurt by an explosion. Override to disable default sound effect.
    --- @param ply Player who has been hurt
    --- @param dmginfo Damage info from explosion
    @side(server)
    OnDamagedByExplosion: ((Player, CTakeDamageInfo) -> any)?
    --- Called as soon as the entity is created. Very little of the entity's properties will be initialized at this stage. (keyvalues, classname, flags, anything), especially on the serverside.
    --- **WARNING**: Removing the created entity during this event can lead to unexpected problems. Use `Global.SafeRemoveEntityDelayed`( entity, 0 ) to safely remove the entity.
    --- @param entity The entity
    @side(shared)
    OnEntityCreated: ((Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when the `Entity:WaterLevel` of an entity is changed.
    --- 0 - The entity isn't in water.
    --- 1 - Slightly submerged (at least to the feet).
    --- 2 - The majority of the entity is submerged (at least to the waist).
    --- 3 - Completely submerged.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook can be considered a physics callback, so changing collision rules (`Entity:SetSolidFlags`) in it may lead to a crash!
    --- @param entity The entity.
    --- @param old Previous water level.
    --- @param new_ The new water level.
    @side(server)
    OnEntityWaterLevelChanged: ((Entity, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when the gamemode is loaded. `gmod.GetGamemode` will be functional at this point.
    --- `Global.LocalPlayer`() returns NULL at the time this is run.
    @side(shared)
    OnGamemodeLoaded: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a Lua error occurs.
    --- If you want to retrieve client errors on the server side, you can use this hook: `GM:OnClientLuaError`
    --- **NOTE**: On the `server realm`, this hook will only account for server-side errors, not client-side ones.
    --- @param error The error that occurred.
    --- @param realm Where the Lua error took place, "client", or "server"
    --- @param stack The Lua error stack trace
    --- @param name Title of the addon that is creating the Lua errors, or nil if addon is not found.
    --- @param id Steam Workshop ID of the addon creating Lua errors, if it is an addon.
    @side(shared)
    OnLuaError: ((string, string, { [any]: any }, string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a Addon Conflict occurs, only works in the Menu realm.
    --- @param addon1 The first Addon
    --- @param addon2 The second Addon
    --- @param fileName The File the Conflict occurred in.
    @side(client)
    OnNotifyAddonConflict: ((string, string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever an NPC drops an item upon its death, such as health kits, armor batteries, etc.
    --- It will NOT be called for dropped weapons, with exception of Half-Life: Source NPCs, since they don't use actual weapon entities and create a weapon entity on death.
    --- `GM:PlayerDroppedWeapon` works for NPC weapon drops already. (Yes, it's not a typo)
    --- It will also not be called for live grenades spawned by Zombine.
    --- @param npc The killed NPC
    --- @param item The item that got dropped by the NPC.
    @side(server)
    OnNPCDropItem: ((NPC, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever an NPC is killed.
    --- @param npc The killed NPC
    --- @param attacker The NPCs attacker, the entity that gets the kill credit, for example a player or an NPC.
    --- @param inflictor Death inflictor. The entity that did the killing. Not necessarily a weapon.
    @side(server)
    OnNPCKilled: ((NPC, Entity, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when the main menu has been blocked by `GM:OnPauseMenuShow` four times in a small interval. This is used internally to explain to the user that they can hold SHIFT to force open the main menu.
    @side(client)
    OnPauseMenuBlockedTooManyTimes: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the pause menu is attempting to be opened. Allows you to prevent the main menu from being opened that time.
    --- The user can hold SHIFT to not call this hook. If the main menu is blocked multiple times in short succession, a warning will be displayed to the end user on how to bypass the hook.
    --- @return boolean Should the menu be allowed to open?
    @side(client)
    OnPauseMenuShow: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a permission gets Granted or Revoked.
    @side(client)
    OnPermissionsChanged: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a player freezes an entity with the physgun.
    --- @param weapon The weapon that was used to freeze the entity.
    --- @param physobj Physics object of the entity.
    --- @param ent The target entity.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to freeze the entity.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to block the unfreeze. The unfreezing is handled by the base gamemode hook. This hook has no return value, returning any value will prevent the gamemode hook from running, which is true for every hook.
    @side(server)
    OnPhysgunFreeze: ((Entity, PhysObj, Entity, Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to when a player has successfully picked up an entity with their Physics Gun.
    --- Not to be confused with `GM:PhysgunPickup` which is called to ask if the player should be able to pick up an entity.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnPickedUp` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPlayerPhysicsPickup` for the player `+use` pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player that has picked up something using the physics gun.
    --- @param ent The entity that was picked up.
    @side(server)
    OnPhysgunPickup: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player reloads with the physgun. Override this to disable default unfreezing behavior.
    --- Regardless of whether or not you return true or false, it will disable reloading. Only returning nil/nothing will allow reloading. The intended behavior should be that returning false disables reloading.
    --- @param physgun The physgun in question.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the physgun.
    --- @return boolean Whether the player can reload with the physgun or not/
    @side(server)
    OnPhysgunReload: ((Weapon, Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player has changed team using `GM:PlayerJoinTeam`.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not work with `hook.Add` and it is only called manually from `GM:PlayerJoinTeam` by the base gamemode
    --- @param ply Player who has changed team
    --- @param oldTeam Index of the team the player was originally in
    --- @param newTeam Index of the team the player has changed to
    --- @deprecated Use GM:PlayerChangedTeam instead, which works for every Player:SetTeam call.
    @side(server)
    OnPlayerChangedTeam: ((Player, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a player sends a chat message. For the serverside equivalent, see `GM:PlayerSay`.
    --- **NOTE**: The input (or suppression) of this hook is based on the output from `GM:PlayerSay`. Chat events suppressed serverside do not call this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param text The message's text
    --- @param teamChat Is the player typing in team chat?
    --- @param isDead Is the player dead?
    --- @return boolean Should the message be suppressed?
    @side(client)
    OnPlayerChat: ((Player, string, boolean, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player makes contact with the ground after a jump or a fall.
    --- @param player Player
    --- @param inWater Did the player land in water?
    --- @param onFloater Did the player land on an object floating in the water?
    --- @param speed The speed at which the player hit the ground
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default action
    @side(shared)
    OnPlayerHitGround: ((Entity, boolean, boolean, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player jumps.
    --- @param player Player
    --- @param speed The velocity/impulse of the jump
    @side(shared)
    OnPlayerJump: ((Entity, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player +use drops an entity.
    --- @param ply The player that dropped the object
    --- @param ent The object that was dropped.
    --- @param thrown Whether the object was throw or simply let go of.
    @side(server)
    OnPlayerPhysicsDrop: ((Player, Entity, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player +use pickups up an entity. This will be called after the entity passes though `GM:AllowPlayerPickup`.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnPickedUp` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player that picked up the object
    --- @param ent The object that was picked up.
    @side(server)
    OnPlayerPhysicsPickup: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when gamemode has been reloaded by auto refresh.
    --- **NOTE**: It seems that this event can be triggered more than once for a single refresh event.
    @side(shared)
    OnReloaded: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the player's screen resolution of the game changes. This also called when changing MSAA settings.
    --- `Global.ScrW` and `Global.ScrH` will return the new values when this hook is called.
    --- @param oldWidth The previous width of the game's window.
    --- @param oldHeight The previous height of the game's window.
    --- @param newWidth The new/current width of the game's window.
    --- @param newHeight The new/current height of the game's window.
    @side(client)
    OnScreenSizeChanged: ((number, number, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player releases the `+menu` bind on their keyboard, which is bound to Q by default.
    @side(client)
    OnSpawnMenuClose: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a player presses the `+menu` bind on their keyboard, which is bound to Q by default.
    @side(client)
    OnSpawnMenuOpen: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a `DTextEntry` gets focus.
    --- This hook is run from `DTextEntry:OnGetFocus` and `PANEL:OnMousePressed` of `DTextEntry`.
    --- @param panel The panel that got focus
    @side(client)
    OnTextEntryGetFocus: ((Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called when a `DTextEntry` loses focus.
    --- @param panel The panel that lost focus
    @side(client)
    OnTextEntryLoseFocus: ((Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called when the player undoes something.
    --- @param name The name of the undo action
    --- @param customText The custom text for the undo, set by undo.SetCustomUndoText
    --- @return boolean Return false to suppress the undo notification.
    @side(client)
    OnUndo: ((string, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the player changes their weapon to another one - and their viewmodel model changes.
    --- This is not always called clientside.
    --- @param viewmodel The viewmodel that is changing
    --- @param oldModel The old model
    --- @param newModel The new model
    @side(shared)
    OnViewModelChanged: ((Entity, string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player drops an entity with the Physgun.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnDropped` for the Gravity Gun drop variant.
    --- @param player The player who dropped an entity
    --- @param entity The dropped entity
    @side(shared)
    PhysgunDrop: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called to determine if a player should be able to pick up an entity with the Physics Gun.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for a hook which is called when a player has successfully picked up an entity.
    --- See `GM:GravGunPickupAllowed` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:AllowPlayerPickup` for the `+USE` pickup variant.
    --- @param player The player that is picking up using the Physics Gun.
    --- @param entity The entity that is being picked up.
    --- @return boolean Returns whether the player can pick up the entity or not.
    @side(shared)
    PhysgunPickup: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called after player's reserve ammo count changes.
    --- @param ply The player whose ammo is being affected.
    --- @param ammoID The ammo type ID.
    --- @param oldCount The old ammo count.
    --- @param newCount The new ammo count.
    @side(shared)
    PlayerAmmoChanged: ((Player, number, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player gets their `Player:UniqueID` set for the first time. This hook will also be called in singleplayer.
    --- See `GM:NetworkIDValidated` for a hook that is called with the player's SteamID is validated by Steam.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param steamid The player's SteamID. This will always be an empty string `""` in singleplayer.
    --- @param uniqueid The player's UniqueID. This will always be `"1"` in singleplayer.
    @side(server)
    PlayerAuthed: ((Player, string, string) -> any)?
    --- Runs when a bind has been pressed. Allows to block commands.
    --- **NOTE**: By using the "alias" console command, this hook can be effectively circumvented. To prevent this use `input.TranslateAlias`.
    --- To stop the user from using `+attack`, `+left` and any other movement commands of the sort, please look into using `GM:StartCommand` instead.
    --- The third argument will always be true.
    --- This does not run for function keys binds (F1-F12).
    --- @param ply The player who used the command; this will always be equal to Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param bind The bind command.
    --- @param pressed If the bind was activated or deactivated.
    --- @param code The button code. See Enums/BUTTON_CODE Enums.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent the bind.
    @side(client)
    PlayerBindPress: ((Player, string, boolean, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player presses a button.
    --- This will not be called if player has a panel opened with keyboard input enabled, use `PANEL:OnKeyCodePressed` instead.
    --- See `GM:KeyPress` for an alternative that uses `Enums/IN`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerButtonUp` for the "key release" event.
    --- @param ply Player who pressed the button
    --- @param button The button, see Enums/BUTTON_CODE
    @side(shared)
    PlayerButtonDown: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player releases a button.
    --- This will not be called if player has a panel opened with keyboard input enabled, use `PANEL:OnKeyCodeReleased` instead.
    --- See `GM:KeyRelease` for an alternative that uses `Enums/IN`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerButtonDown` for the "key press" event.
    --- @param ply Player who released the button
    --- @param button The button, see Enums/BUTTON_CODE
    @side(shared)
    PlayerButtonUp: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Decides whether a player can hear another player using voice chat.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called **players count * speaking players count** times every 0.3 seconds if at least 1 player is talking or every 5 seconds if no one is talking.
    --- You should ensure that your code is efficient, or this will definitely influence performance.
    --- @param listener The listening player.
    --- @param talker The talking player.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` if the listener should hear the talker, `false` if they shouldn't.
    --- @return boolean 3D sound. If set to `true`, will fade out the sound the further away listener is from the  talker, the voice will also be in stereo, and not mono.
    @side(server)
    PlayerCanHearPlayersVoice: ((Player, Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to join a team
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not work with `hook.Add` and it is only called manually from `GM:PlayerJoinTeam` by the base gamemode
    --- @param ply Player attempting to switch teams
    --- @param team Index of the team
    --- @return boolean Allowed to switch
    @side(server)
    PlayerCanJoinTeam: ((Player, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to pick an item up. (ammo, health, armor)
    --- This will typically only work for base game entities, unless mod authors that implement similar entities also manually call this hook.
    --- See `GM:PlayerCanPickupWeapon` for a hook that controls weapon pickups.
    --- @param ply Player attempting to pick up
    --- @param item The item the player is attempting to pick up
    --- @return boolean Allow pick up
    @side(server)
    PlayerCanPickupItem: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to pick up a weapon.
    --- If this returns `false`, `Player:Give` won't work.
    --- See `GM:PlayerCanPickupItem` for a hook that affects things like health kits, armor batteries and ammo entities.
    --- See `GM:WeaponEquip` for a hook that is called when a player successfully picks up a weapon after passing this hook.
    --- @param ply The player attempting to pick up the weapon.
    --- @param weapon The weapon entity in question.
    --- @return boolean `false` to disallow pickup.
    @side(server)
    PlayerCanPickupWeapon: ((Player, Weapon) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Returns whether or not the player can see the other player's chat.
    --- **NOTE**: The **speaker** parameter does not have to be a valid `Player` object which happens when console messages are displayed for example.
    --- @param text The chat text
    --- @param teamOnly If the message is team-only
    --- @param listener The player receiving the message
    --- @param speaker The player sending the message.
    --- @return boolean Can see other player's chat
    @side(server)
    PlayerCanSeePlayersChat: ((string, boolean, Player, Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player has changed team using `Player:SetTeam`.
    --- **WARNING**: Avoid calling `Player:SetTeam` in this hook as it may cause an infinite loop!
    --- **WARNING**: `Player:Team` inside this hook will return `oldTeam`.
    --- @param ply Player whose team has changed.
    --- @param oldTeam Index of the team the player was originally in. See team.GetName and the team library.
    --- @param newTeam Index of the team the player has changed to.
    @side(server)
    PlayerChangedTeam: ((Player, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a player is about to spawn something to see if they hit a limit for whatever they are spawning.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook will not be called in singleplayer, as singleplayer does not have limits.
    --- @param ply The player who is trying to spawn something.
    --- @param limitName The limit's name.
    --- @param current The amount of whatever player is trying to spawn that the player already has spawned.
    --- @param defaultMax The default maximum count, as dictated by the `sbox_max` convar on the server. This is the amount that will be used if nothing is returned from this hook.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to indicate the limit was hit, or nothing otherwise
    @side(shared)
    PlayerCheckLimit: ((Player, string, number, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called whenever a player's class is changed on the server-side with `player_manager.SetPlayerClass`.
    --- @param ply The player whose class has been changed.
    --- @param newID The network ID of the player class's name string, or `0` if we are clearing a player class from the player. Pass this into util.NetworkIDToString to retrieve the proper name of the player class.
    @side(client)
    PlayerClassChanged: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Executes when a player connects to the server. Called before the player has been assigned a `UserID` and entity. See the `player_connect` gameevent for a version of this hook called after the player entity has been created.
    --- **NOTE**: This is only called clientside for listen server hosts.
    --- **NOTE**: This is not called clientside for the local player.
    --- @param name The player's name.
    --- @param ip The player's IP address. Will be "none" for bots. This argument will only be passed serverside.
    @side(shared)
    PlayerConnect: ((string, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player is killed by `Player:Kill` or any other normal means.
    --- This hook is **not** called if the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`. See `GM:PlayerSilentDeath` for that.
    --- * `GM:DoPlayerDeath` is called **before** this hook.
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called **after** this hook.
    --- See `Player:LastHitGroup` if you need to get the last hit hitgroup of the player.
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param victim The player who died
    --- @param inflictor Item used to kill the victim
    --- @param attacker Player or entity that killed the victim
    @side(server)
    PlayerDeath: ((Player, Entity, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Returns whether or not the default death sound should be muted.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return boolean Mute death sound
    @side(server)
    PlayerDeathSound: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called every think while the player is dead. The return value will determine if the player respawns.
    --- Overwriting this function will prevent players from respawning by pressing space or clicking.
    --- This hook is not called for players with the `FL_FROZEN` flag applied.
    --- @param ply The player affected in the hook.
    --- @return boolean This hook does not define a return value. The description below just describes how the hook library works in general. Return a non-nil value to prevent the current gamemode from handling this event. In the `base` gamemode, the gamemode handles player respawning in this hook. So blocking the gamemode hook will prevent player from respawning, in this specific case.
    @side(server)
    PlayerDeathThink: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player leaves the server. See the `player_disconnect gameevent` for a shared version of this hook that includes the disconnect reason too.
    --- This is not called in single-player or listen servers for the host.
    --- @param ply the player
    @side(server)
    PlayerDisconnected: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called to update the player's animation during a drive.
    --- @param ply The driving player
    @side(shared)
    PlayerDriveAnimate: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when a weapon is dropped by a player via `Player:DropWeapon`. Despite its name, this hook is also called for NPC weapon drops.
    --- Also called when a weapon is removed from a player via `Player:StripWeapon`.
    --- See also `GM:WeaponEquip` for a hook when a player picks up a weapon.
    --- The weapon's `Entity:GetOwner` will be NULL at the time this hook is called.
    --- `WEAPON:OnDrop` will be called before this hook is.
    --- @param owner The player or NPC who owned this weapon before it was dropped.
    --- @param wep The weapon that was dropped.
    @side(server)
    PlayerDroppedWeapon: ((Player | NPC, Weapon) -> any)?
    --- Called when player stops using voice chat.
    --- See `GM:PlayerStartVoice` for the opposite hook.
    --- @param ply Player who stopped talking. Can be NULL when player entity is outside of the PVS. Use the player index.
    --- @param plyIndex The Entity:EntIndex of the talking player.
    @side(client)
    PlayerEndVoice: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player enters a vehicle.
    --- Called just after `GM:CanPlayerEnterVehicle`.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerLeaveVehicle`.
    --- @param ply Player who entered vehicle.
    --- @param veh Vehicle the player entered.
    --- @param role The seat number.
    @side(server)
    PlayerEnteredVehicle: ((Player, Vehicle, number) -> any)?
    --- Called before firing clientside animation events on a player model.
    --- See `GM:PlayerHandleAnimEvent` for the serverside version.
    --- @param ply The player who has triggered the event.
    --- @param pos Position of the effect
    --- @param ang Angle of the effect
    --- @param event The event ID of happened even. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events).
    --- @param name Name of the event
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable the effect
    @side(client)
    PlayerFireAnimationEvent: ((Player, Vector, Angle, number, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called whenever a player steps. Return true to mute the normal sound.
    --- See `GM:PlayerStepSoundTime` for a related hook about footstep frequency.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called on all clients.
    --- @param ply The stepping player
    --- @param pos The position of the step
    --- @param foot Foot that is stepped. 0 for left, 1 for right
    --- @param sound Sound that is going to play
    --- @param volume Volume of the footstep
    --- @param filter The Recipient filter of players who can hear the footstep
    --- @return boolean Prevent default step sound
    @side(shared)
    PlayerFootstep: ((Player, Vector, number, string, number, CRecipientFilter) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player freezes an object.
    --- @param ply Player who has frozen an object
    --- @param ent The frozen object
    --- @param physobj The frozen physics object of the frozen entity ( For ragdolls )
    @side(server)
    PlayerFrozeObject: ((Player, Entity, PhysObj) -> any)?
    --- Called before firing serverside animation events on the player models.
    --- See `GM:PlayerFireAnimationEvent` for the clientside version.
    --- @param ply The player who has triggered the event.
    --- @param event The event ID of happened even. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events).
    --- @param eventTime The absolute time this event occurred using Global.CurTime.
    --- @param cycle The frame this event occurred as a number between 0 and 1.
    --- @param type Event type. See [the Source SDK](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/shared/eventlist.h#L14-L23).
    --- @param options Name or options of this event.
    @side(server)
    PlayerHandleAnimEvent: ((Player, number, number, number, number, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player gets hurt.
    --- @param victim Victim
    --- @param attacker Attacker Entity
    --- @param healthRemaining Remaining Health
    --- @param damageTaken Damage Taken
    @side(server)
    PlayerHurt: ((Player, Entity, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when the player spawns for the first time.
    --- See `GM:PlayerSpawn` for a hook called every player spawn.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called before the player has fully loaded, when the player is still in seeing the `Starting Lua` screen. For example, trying to use the `Entity:GetModel` function will return the default model (`models/player.mdl`).
    --- **WARNING**: Sending `net` messages to the spawned player in this hook may cause them to be received before the player finishes loading, for example `Global.LocalPlayer` might return NULL since `GM:InitPostEntity` may have not been called yet clientside though the net message **won't** be lost and the client still should receive it (more information here: https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-requests/issues/718).
    --- Workaround without networking:
    --- ```
    --- local load_queue = {}
    --- hook.Add( "PlayerInitialSpawn", "myAddonName/Load", function( ply )
    --- load_queue[ ply ] = true
    --- end )
    --- hook.Add( "StartCommand", "myAddonName/Load", function( ply, cmd )
    --- if load_queue[ ply ] and not cmd:IsForced() then
    --- load_queue[ ply ] = nil
    --- -- Send what you need here if it requires the client to be fully loaded!
    --- end
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- With networking:
    --- ```
    --- -- CLIENT
    --- hook.Add( "InitPostEntity", "Ready", function()
    --- net.Start( "cool_addon_client_ready" )
    --- net.SendToServer()
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- ```
    --- -- SERVER
    --- util.AddNetworkString( "cool_addon_client_ready" )
    --- net.Receive( "cool_addon_client_ready", function( len, ply )
    --- -- Send what you need here!
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- @param player The player who spawned.
    --- @param transition If `true`, the player just spawned from a map transition.
    @side(server)
    PlayerInitialSpawn: ((Player, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Makes the player join a specified team. This is a convenience function that calls `Player:SetTeam` and runs the `GM:OnPlayerChangedTeam` hook.
    --- @param ply Player to force
    --- @param team The team to put player into
    @side(server)
    PlayerJoinTeam: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player leaves a vehicle for any reason, including `Player:ExitVehicle`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerEnteredVehicle` for the opposite hook.
    --- **NOTE**: For vehicles with exit animations, this will be called **at the end** of the animation, **not at the start**!
    --- @param ply Player who left a vehicle.
    --- @param veh Vehicle the player left.
    @side(server)
    PlayerLeaveVehicle: ((Player, Vehicle) -> any)?
    --- Called to give players the default set of weapons.
    --- **NOTE**: This function may not work in your custom gamemode if you have overridden your `GM:PlayerSpawn` and you do not use self.BaseClass.PlayerSpawn or `hook.Call`.
    --- @param ply Player to give weapons to.
    @side(server)
    PlayerLoadout: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player tries to switch noclip mode.
    --- `MOVETYPE_NOCLIP` can be used to determine if a player is currently in noclip mode.
    --- @param ply The person who entered/exited noclip
    --- @param desiredState Represents the noclip state (on/off) the user will enter if this hook allows them to.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow the switch.
    @side(shared)
    PlayerNoClip: ((Player, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called after the player's think, just after `GM:FinishMove`.
    --- **NOTE**: On the client side, it is only called for the local player.
    --- @param ply The player
    @side(shared)
    PlayerPostThink: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Request a player to join the team. This function will check if the team is available to join or not.
    --- This hook is called when the player runs "changeteam" in the console.
    --- To prevent the player from changing teams, see `GM:PlayerCanJoinTeam`
    --- @param ply The player to try to put into a team
    --- @param team Team to put the player into if the checks succeeded
    @side(server)
    PlayerRequestTeam: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player dispatched a chat message. For the clientside equivalent, see `GM:OnPlayerChat`.
    --- **NOTE**: It may be more reliable to use `gameevent/player_say` to read messages serverside because addons commonly return values in this hook to change chat messages.
    --- @param sender The player which sent the message.
    --- @param text The message's content.
    --- @param teamChat Return false when the message is for everyone, true when the message is for the sender's team.
    --- @return string What to show instead of original text. Set to `""` to stop the message from displaying.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSay: ((Player, string, boolean) -> string | nil)?
    --- Called to determine a spawn point for a player to spawn at.
    --- **NOTE**: The spawn point entity will also impact the player's eye angle. For example, if the entity is upside down, the player's view will be as well.
    --- @param ply The player who needs a spawn point
    --- @param transition If true, the player just spawned from a map transition (`trigger_changelevel`). You probably want to not return an entity for that case to not override player's position.
    --- @return Entity The spawn point entity to spawn the player at
    @side(server)
    PlayerSelectSpawn: ((Player, boolean) -> Entity | nil)?
    --- Find a team spawn point entity for this player.
    --- @param team Players team
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return Entity The entity to use as a spawn point.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSelectTeamSpawn: ((number, Player) -> Entity | nil)?
    --- Called whenever view model hands needs setting a model. By default this calls `PLAYER:GetHandsModel` and if that fails, sets the hands model according to his player model.
    --- @param ply The player whose hands needs a model set
    --- @param ent The hands to set model of
    @side(server)
    PlayerSetHandsModel: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a player spawns and must choose a model. A good place to assign a model to a player.
    --- **NOTE**: This function may not work in your custom gamemode if you have overridden your `GM:PlayerSpawn` and you do not use `self.BaseClass.PlayerSpawn` in it, or `hook.Call` this hook from `GM:PlayerSpawn`.
    --- @param ply The player being chosen
    @side(server)
    PlayerSetModel: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Returns true if the player should take damage from the given attacker.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the player taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param attacker The attacker
    --- @return boolean Allow damage
    @side(server)
    PlayerShouldTakeDamage: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows to suppress player taunts.
    --- @param ply Player who tried to taunt
    --- @param act Act ID of the taunt player tries to do, see Enums/ACT
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow player taunting
    @side(server)
    PlayerShouldTaunt: ((Player, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`.
    --- The player is already considered dead when this hook is called.
    --- * See `GM:PlayerDeath` for a hook which handles all other death causes.
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called **after** this hook.
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return true in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player who was killed
    @side(server)
    PlayerSilentDeath: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever a player spawns, including respawns.
    --- See `GM:PlayerInitialSpawn` for a hook called only the first time a player spawns.
    --- See the `player_spawn gameevent` for a shared version of this hook.
    --- **WARNING**: By default, in "base" derived gamemodes, this hook will also call `GM:PlayerLoadout` and `GM:PlayerSetModel`, which may override your `Entity:SetModel` and `Player:Give` calls. Consider using the other hooks or a 0-second timer.
    --- @param player The player who spawned.
    --- @param transition If true, the player just spawned from a map transition. You probably want to not touch player's weapons or position if this is set to `true`.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawn: ((Player, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called to spawn the player as a spectator.
    --- @param ply The player to spawn as a spectator
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnAsSpectator: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Determines if the player can spray using the `impulse 201` console command.
    --- @param sprayer The player.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to allow spraying, return `true` to prevent spraying.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpray: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when player starts taunting.
    --- @param ply The player who is taunting
    --- @param act The sequence ID of the taunt
    --- @param length Length of the taunt
    @side(server)
    PlayerStartTaunt: ((Player, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player starts using voice chat.
    --- See `GM:PlayerEndVoice` for the hook when the player stops talking.
    --- **NOTE**: Set `mp_show_voice_icons` to 0, if you want disable voice chat icons above player heads.
    --- @param ply Player who started using voice chat. Can be NULL when player entity is outside of the PVS. Use the player index.
    --- @param plyIndex The Entity:EntIndex. Only appears when non-local player speaks for the first time. After August 2026 - always provided.
    @side(client)
    PlayerStartVoice: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Allows you to override the time between footsteps.
    --- See `GM:PlayerFootstep` for a related hook about footstep sounds themselves.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called on all clients.
    --- @param ply Player who is walking
    --- @param type The type of footsteps, see Enums/STEPSOUNDTIME
    --- @param walking Is the player walking or not ( +walk? )
    --- @return number Time between footsteps, in ms
    @side(shared)
    PlayerStepSoundTime: ((Player, number, boolean) -> number | nil)?
    --- Called whenever a player attempts to either turn on or off their flashlight, returning false will deny the change.
    --- **NOTE**: Also gets called when using `Player:Flashlight`.
    --- @param ply The player who attempts to change their flashlight state.
    --- @param enabled The new state the player requested, true for on, false for off.
    --- @return boolean Can toggle the flashlight or not
    @side(server)
    PlayerSwitchFlashlight: ((Player, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to switch their weapon.
    --- Primary usage of this hook is to prevent/allow weapon switching, **not** to detect weapon switching. It will not be called for `Player:SetActiveWeapon`.
    --- @param player The player switching weapons.
    --- @param oldWeapon The previous weapon. Will be `NULL` if the previous weapon was removed or the player is switching from nothing.
    --- @param newWeapon The weapon the player switched to. Will be `NULL` if the player is switching to nothing. This can be `NULL` on the client if the weapon hasn't been created over the network yet.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent weapon switch.
    @side(shared)
    PlayerSwitchWeapon: ((Player, Weapon, Weapon) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- The Move hook is called for you to manipulate the player's `CMoveData`. This hook is called moments before `GM:Move` and `GM:PlayerNoClip`.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not run when inside a vehicle. `GM:VehicleMove` will be called instead.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @param mv The current movedata for the player.
    @side(shared)
    PlayerTick: ((Player, CMoveData) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player has been hit by a trace and damaged (such as from a bullet). Returning true overrides the damage handling and prevents `GM:ScalePlayerDamage` from being called.
    --- @param ply The player that has been hit
    --- @param dmginfo The damage info of the bullet
    --- @param dir Normalized vector direction of the bullet's path
    --- @param trace The trace of the bullet's path, see Structures/TraceResult
    --- @return boolean Override engine handling
    @side(shared)
    PlayerTraceAttack: ((Player, CTakeDamageInfo, Vector, TraceResult) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player unfreezes an object.
    --- @param ply Player who has unfrozen an object
    --- @param ent The unfrozen object
    --- @param physobj The frozen physics object of the unfrozen entity ( For ragdolls )
    @side(server)
    PlayerUnfrozeObject: ((Player, Entity, PhysObj) -> any)?
    --- Triggered when the player presses use on an object. Continuously runs until USE is released but will not activate other Entities until the USE key is released; dependent on activation type of the Entity.
    --- @param ply The player pressing the "use" key.
    --- @param ent The entity which the player is looking at / activating USE on.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` if the player is not allowed to USE the entity. Do not return `true` if using a hook, otherwise other mods may not get a chance to block a player's use.
    @side(server)
    PlayerUse: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when it's time to populate the context menu menu bar at the top.
    --- @param menubar The DMenuBar itself.
    @side(client)
    PopulateMenuBar: ((Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called right after the map has cleaned up (usually because `game.CleanUpMap` was called)
    --- See also `GM:PreCleanupMap`.
    @side(shared)
    PostCleanupMap: (() -> any)?
    --- Called right after the 2D skybox has been drawn - allowing you to draw over it.
    @side(client)
    PostDraw2DSkyBox: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after rendering effects. This is where halos are drawn. Called just before `GM:PreDrawHUD` (The two hooks are basically identical).
    --- See `GM:PreDrawEffects` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawEffects: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after `GM:PreDrawHUD`,  `GM:HUDPaintBackground` and `GM:HUDPaint` but before  `GM:DrawOverlay`.
    --- Unlike `GM:HUDPaint`(`Background`) hooks, this will still be called when the main menu is visible. And so will be `GM:PreDrawHUD`
    @side(client)
    PostDrawHUD: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after drawing opaque entities.
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawTranslucentRenderables` and `GM:PreDrawOpaqueRenderables`.
    --- @param bDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param bDrawingSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawOpaqueRenderables: ((boolean, boolean, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player hands are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for the view model alternative.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawPlayerHands` for a hook that is called just before view model hands are drawn.
    --- @param hands This is the gmod_hands entity.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity.
    --- @param ply The the owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawPlayerHands: ((Entity, Entity, Player, Weapon, number) -> any)?
    --- Called after drawing the 3D skybox. This will not be called if skybox rendering was prevented via the `GM:PreDrawSkyBox` hook.
    --- See also `GM:PostDraw2DSkyBox`.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawSkyBox: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after all translucent entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawOpaqueRenderables` and  `GM:PreDrawTranslucentRenderables`.
    --- This is still called when r_drawentities or r_drawopaquerenderables is disabled.
    --- This is not called when r_drawtranslucentworld is disabled.
    --- @param bDrawingDepth Whether the current call is writing depth.
    --- @param bDrawingSkybox Whether the current call is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current call is drawing the 3D skybox.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawTranslucentRenderables: ((boolean, boolean, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called after view model is drawn.
    --- The render FOV in this hook is different from the main view, as view models are usually rendered with a different FOV. Every render operation will only be accurate with the view model entity.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` for a hook that is called just before a view model is drawn.
    --- For view model hands alternative, see `GM:PostDrawPlayerHands`.
    --- @param viewmodel Players view model
    --- @param player The owner of the weapon/view model
    --- @param weapon The weapon the player is currently holding
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    PostDrawViewModel: ((Entity, Player, Weapon, number) -> any)?
    --- Called every time a bullet pellet (i.e. this hook is called multiple times for a shotgun shot) is fired from an entity. Notably this hook will have the final damage and aim direction for the bullet pellet.
    --- See `GM:EntityFireBullets` if you wish to modify the bullets before they are fired.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called directly from `Entity:FireBullets`. Due to this, you cannot call `Entity:FireBullets` inside this hook or an infinite loop will occur crashing the game.
    --- @param entity The entity that fired the bullet
    --- @param data A table of data about the bullet that was fired. See Structures/FiredBullet.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to suppress the bullet.
    @side(shared)
    PostEntityFireBullets: ((Entity, FiredBullet) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when an entity receives a damage event, after passing damage filters, etc.
    --- See `GM:EntityTakeDamage` if you wish to prevent damage events, or otherwise alter them.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the entity taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param ent The entity that took the damage.
    --- @param dmginfo Detailed information about the damage event. When you retrieve "the attacker" the player's angle and position will be incorrect.
    --- @param wasDamageTaken Whether the entity actually took the damage. (For example, shooting a Strider will generate this event, but it won't take bullet damage).
    @side(server)
    PostEntityTakeDamage: ((Entity, CTakeDamageInfo, boolean) -> any)?
    --- Called after the gamemode has loaded.
    @side(shared)
    PostGamemodeLoaded: (() -> any)?
    --- Called right after `GM:DoPlayerDeath`, `GM:PlayerDeath` and `GM:PlayerSilentDeath`.
    --- This hook will be called for all deaths, including `Player:KillSilent`
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    @side(server)
    PostPlayerDeath: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called after a given player in your [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community") was drawn.
    --- This hook will not be called if player was prevented from being drawn via `GM:PrePlayerDraw`.
    --- @param ply The player that was drawn.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    PostPlayerDraw: ((Player, number) -> any)?
    --- Allows you to suppress post processing effect drawing.
    --- @param effect_name The classname of Post Processing effect
    --- @return boolean Return true/false depending on whether this post process should be allowed
    @side(client)
    PostProcessPermitted: ((string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called after the frame has been rendered. Will not be called if `GM:PreRender` returned `true`, disabling all further rendering operations for the current frame.
    @side(client)
    PostRender: (() -> any)?
    --- Called after the VGUI has been drawn.
    @side(client)
    PostRenderVGUI: (() -> any)?
    --- Called just after performing an undo.
    --- @param undo The undo table. See Structures/Undo struct.
    --- @param count The amount of props/actions undone. This will be `0` for undos that are skipped in cases where for example the entity that is meant to be undone is already deleted.
    @side(server)
    PostUndo: (({ [any]: any }, number) -> any)?
    --- Called right before the map cleans up (usually because `game.CleanUpMap` was called)
    --- See also `GM:PostCleanupMap`.
    @side(shared)
    PreCleanupMap: (() -> any)?
    --- Called just after `GM:PreDrawViewModel` and can technically be considered as a "PostDrawAllViewModels".
    --- See `GM:PostDrawEffects` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawEffects: (() -> any)?
    --- Called before rendering the halos. This is the place to call `halo.Add`. This hook is actually running inside of `GM:PostDrawEffects`.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawHalos: (() -> any)?
    --- Called just after `GM:PostDrawEffects` (duplicate of it). Drawing anything in it seems to work incorrectly.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawHUD` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawHUD: (() -> any)?
    --- Called before all opaque entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PreDrawTranslucentRenderables` and  `GM:PostDrawOpaqueRenderables`.
    --- @param isDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param isDrawSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent opaque renderables from drawing.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawOpaqueRenderables: ((boolean, boolean, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called before the player hands are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` for the view model alternative.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawPlayerHands` for a hook that is called just before view model hands are drawn.
    --- @param hands This is the gmod_hands entity before it is drawn.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity before it is drawn.
    --- @param ply The the owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent the viewmodel hands from rendering
    @side(client)
    PreDrawPlayerHands: ((Entity, Entity, Player, Weapon, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called before the 3D sky box is drawn. This will not be called for maps with no 3D skybox, or when the 3d skybox is disabled. (`r_3dsky 0`)
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawSkyBox`
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable skybox drawing (both 2D and 3D skybox)
    @side(client)
    PreDrawSkyBox: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called before all the translucent entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PreDrawOpaqueRenderables` and  `GM:PostDrawTranslucentRenderables`.
    --- This is still called when r_drawentities or r_drawopaquerenderables is disabled.
    --- This is not called when r_drawtranslucentworld is disabled.
    --- @param isDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param isDrawSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent translucent renderables from drawing.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawTranslucentRenderables: ((boolean, boolean, boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called before the view model has been drawn.
    --- By default this hook also calls `WEAPON:PreDrawViewModel`, so you can use that if developing a scripted weapon.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for a hook that runs immediately after rendering a view model.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModels` for a hook that runs before **all** view models are drawn within a frame.
    --- For view model hands, see `GM:PreDrawPlayerHands`.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity before it is drawn. On server-side, this entity is the predicted view model.
    --- @param ply The owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent the default view model rendering. This also affects GM:PostDrawViewModel.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawViewModel: ((Entity, Player, Weapon, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called just before all view models (there are 3 per player, see `Player:GetViewModel`) and entities with `RENDERGROUP_VIEWMODEL` are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` and `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for hooks that run for specific view models.
    --- You can use `GM:PreDrawEffects` as a "`PostDrawViewModels`" hook as it is called just after the all the view model(s) are drawn.
    @side(client)
    PreDrawViewModels: (() -> any)?
    --- Called before the gamemode is loaded.
    @side(shared)
    PreGamemodeLoaded: (() -> any)?
    --- Called before the player is drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PostPlayerDraw`.
    --- @param player The player that is about to be drawn.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent default player rendering, which hides the player.
    @side(client)
    PrePlayerDraw: ((Player, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called by `scripted_ents.Register`.
    --- @param ent The entity table to be registered.
    --- @param class_ The class name to be assigned.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the entity from being registered. Returning any other value has no effect.
    @side(shared)
    PreRegisterSENT: (({ [any]: any }, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a Scripted Weapon (SWEP) is about to be registered, allowing addons to alter the weapon's SWEP table with custom data for later usage. Called internally from `weapons.Register`.
    --- @param swep The SWEP table to be registered.
    --- @param class_ The class name to be assigned.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the weapon from being registered. Returning any other value has no effect.
    @side(shared)
    PreRegisterSWEP: (({ [any]: any }, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called before the renderer is about to start rendering the next frame.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent all rendering. This can make the whole game stop rendering anything.
    @side(client)
    PreRender: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called just before performing an undo.
    --- @param undo The undo table. See Structures/Undo struct.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to disallow the undo.
    @side(server)
    PreUndo: (({ [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- This will prevent IN_ATTACK from sending to server when player tries to shoot from C menu.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent screen clicks.
    @side(client)
    PreventScreenClicks: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a prop has been destroyed.
    --- @param attacker The person who broke the prop. This can be a NULL entity for cases where the prop was not broken by a player.
    --- @param prop The entity that has been broken by the attacker.
    @side(shared)
    PropBreak: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Render the scene. Used by the `Stereoscopy` post-processing effect.
    --- **NOTE**: Materials rendered in this hook require `$ignorez` parameter to draw properly.
    --- @param origin View origin
    --- @param angles View angles
    --- @param fov View FOV
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to override drawing the scene.
    @side(client)
    RenderScene: ((Vector, Angle, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Used to render post processing effects.
    @side(client)
    RenderScreenspaceEffects: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the game is reloaded from a Source Engine save system ( not the Sandbox saves or dupes ).
    --- See `GM:Saved` for a hook that is called when such a save file is created.
    @side(shared)
    Restored: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the game is saved using the Source Engine save system (not the Sandbox saves or dupes).
    --- See `GM:Restored` for a hook that is called when such a save file is loaded.
    --- See also the `saverestore` for relevant functions.
    @side(shared)
    Saved: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when an NPC takes damage.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called only when a specific hit group of the NPC is hit. In cases where the hitgroup doesn't matter, you should use `GM:EntityTakeDamage` instead!
    --- @param npc The NPC that takes damage
    --- @param hitgroup The hitgroup (hitbox) enum where the NPC took damage. See Enums/HITGROUP
    --- @param dmginfo Damage info
    @side(server)
    ScaleNPCDamage: ((NPC, number, CTakeDamageInfo) -> any)?
    --- This hook allows you to change how much damage a player receives when one takes damage to a specific body part.
    --- **NOTE**: This is called only for bullet damage a player receives, you should use `GM:EntityTakeDamage` instead if you need to detect **ALL** damage.
    --- @param ply The player taking damage.
    --- @param hitgroup The hitgroup where the player took damage. See Enums/HITGROUP
    --- @param dmginfo The damage info.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent damage that this hook is called for, stop blood particle effects and blood decals. It is possible to return true only on client ( This will work **only in multiplayer** ) to stop the effects but still take damage.
    @side(shared)
    ScalePlayerDamage: ((Player, number, CTakeDamageInfo) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when player released the scoreboard button (TAB by default).
    @side(client)
    ScoreboardHide: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when player presses the scoreboard button (TAB by default).
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent default scoreboard from showing.
    @side(client)
    ScoreboardShow: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- An internal function used to send a death notice event to all clients.
    --- @param attacker The entity that caused the death.
    --- @param inflictor The attacker's weapon class name or the attacker itself if no weapon was equipped.
    --- @param victim The entity that died.
    --- @param flags Death notice flags. 1 = Friendly victim (to the player), 2 = friendly attacker (to the player)
    @side(server)
    SendDeathNotice: ((Entity | string | nil, string, Entity | string, number) -> any)?
    --- Sets player run and sprint speeds.
    --- Using a speed of `0` can lead to prediction errors, and can cause players to move at `sv_maxvelocity`
    --- **WARNING**: This is not a hook. Treat this as a utility function to set the player's speed.
    --- @param ply The player to set the speed of.
    --- @param walkSpeed The walk speed.
    --- @param runSpeed The run speed.
    @side(shared)
    SetPlayerSpeed: ((Player, number, number) -> any)?
    --- SetupMove is called before the engine process movements. This allows us to override the players movement.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply The player whose movement we are about to process
    --- @param mv The move data to override/use
    --- @param cmd The command data
    @side(shared)
    SetupMove: ((Player, CMoveData, CUserCmd) -> any)?
    --- Allows you to add extra positions to the player's [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). This is the place to call `Global.AddOriginToPVS`.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param viewEntity Players Player:GetViewEntity
    @side(server)
    SetupPlayerVisibility: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Allows you to use render.Fog* functions to manipulate skybox fog.
    --- This will not be called for maps with no 3D skybox, or when the 3d skybox is disabled. (`r_3dsky 0`)
    --- @param scale The scale of 3D skybox
    --- @return boolean Return true to tell the engine that fog is set up
    @side(client)
    SetupSkyboxFog: ((number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows you to use render.Fog* functions to manipulate world fog.
    --- @return boolean Return true to tell the engine that fog is set up
    @side(client)
    SetupWorldFog: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to decide whether a pair of entities should collide with each other. This is only called if `Entity:SetCustomCollisionCheck` was used on one or both entities.
    --- Where applicable, consider using `constraint.NoCollide` or a [logic_collision_pair](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Logic_collision_pair) entity instead - they are considerably easier to use and may be more appropriate in some situations.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook **must** return the same value consistently for the same pair of entities.
    --- If an entity changed in such a way that its collision rules change, you **must** call `Entity:CollisionRulesChanged` on that entity immediately - **not in this hook and not in physics callbacks.**
    --- As long as you religiously follow the rules set by the examples this hook will work reliably without breaking, even a small mistake might break physics.
    --- This hook can cause all physics to break under certain conditions.
    --- @param ent1 The first entity in the collision poll.
    --- @param ent2 The second entity in the collision poll.
    --- @return boolean Whether the entities should collide.
    @side(shared)
    ShouldCollide: ((Entity, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to determine if the `Global.LocalPlayer` should be drawn.
    --- If you're using this hook to draw a player for a `GM:CalcView` hook, then you may want to consider using the `drawviewer` variable you can use in your `Structures/CamData` table instead.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook has an internal cache that is reset at the start of every frame. This will prevent this hook from running in certain cases. This cache is reset in `cam.Start` and in a future update in `render.RenderView` when rendering extra views.
    --- @param ply The player.
    --- @return boolean `true` to draw the player, `false` to hide.
    @side(client)
    ShouldDrawLocalPlayer: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showhelp` console command. (Default bind is F1)
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command
    @side(server)
    ShowHelp: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showspare1` console command ( Default bind is F3 ).
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command.
    @side(server)
    ShowSpare1: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showspare2` console command ( Default bind is F4 ).
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command.
    @side(server)
    ShowSpare2: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showteam` console command. ( Default bind is F2 )
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command
    @side(server)
    ShowTeam: ((Player) -> any)?
    --- Called whenever the Lua environment is about to be shut down, for example on map change, or when the server is going to shut down.
    @side(shared)
    ShutDown: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when spawn icon is generated.
    --- @param lastmodel File path of previously generated model.
    --- @param imagename File path of the generated icon.
    --- @param modelsleft Amount of models left to generate.
    @side(client)
    SpawniconGenerated: ((string, string, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when the Spawnmenu is Created.
    @side(client)
    SpawnMenuCreated: (() -> any)?
    --- Runs when the user tries to open the chat box.
    --- **WARNING**: Returning `true` won't stop the chatbox from taking VGUI focus. `chat.Close` may be of use to mitigate that, or usage of `GM:PlayerBindPress`.
    --- @param isTeamChat Whether the message was sent through team chat.
    --- @return boolean Return true to hide the default chat box.
    @side(client)
    StartChat: ((boolean) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Allows you to change the players inputs before they are processed by the server. This function is also called for bots, making it the best solution to control them.
    --- This is basically a shared version of `GM:CreateMove`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is predicted, but not by usual means, it is called when a `CUserCmd` is generated on the client, and on the server when it is received, so it is necessary for this hook to be called clientside even on singleplayer
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param ucmd The usercommand
    @side(shared)
    StartCommand: ((Player, CUserCmd) -> any)?
    --- Called right before an entity starts driving. Overriding this hook will cause it to not call `drive.Start` and the player will not begin driving the entity.
    --- @param ent The entity that is going to be driven
    --- @param ply The player that is going to drive the entity
    @side(shared)
    StartEntityDriving: ((Entity, Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when you start a new game via the menu.
    @side(client)
    StartGame: (() -> any)?
    --- Called every rendered frame on client, except when the game is paused.
    --- Called every game tick on the server. This will be the same as `GM:Tick` on the server when there is no lag, but will only be called once every processed server frame during lag.
    --- `Global.CurTime` is guaranteed to be different with each call to this hook on the server.
    --- See `GM:Tick` for a hook that runs every tick on both the client and server.
    --- **NOTE**: On server, this hook **WILL NOT** run if the server is empty, unless you set the `ConVar` `sv_hibernate_think` to `1`.
    @side(shared)
    Think: (() -> any)?
    --- Called every game tick. `engine.TickCount` is guaranteed to be different between each call.
    --- Server side, this is similar to `GM:Think` (See that page for details).
    --- The default tickrate is `66.6666` (15 millisecond intervals). It can be changed via the `-tickrate` `command line option`.
    --- See `engine.TickInterval` for a function to retrieve this data at runtime.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook **WILL NOT** run if the server is empty, unless you set the `ConVar` `sv_hibernate_think` to 1
    @side(shared)
    Tick: (() -> any)?
    --- **NOTE**: Isn't called when CalcMainActivity returns a valid override sequence id
    --- Allows you to translate player activities.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param act The activity. See Enums/ACT
    --- @return number The new, translated activity
    @side(shared)
    TranslateActivity: ((Player, number) -> number | nil)?
    --- Animation updates (pose params etc) should be done here.
    --- @param ply The player to update the animation info for.
    --- @param velocity The player's velocity.
    --- @param maxSeqGroundSpeed Speed of the animation - used for playback rate scaling.
    @side(shared)
    UpdateAnimation: ((Player, Vector, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when a variable is edited on an Entity (called by Edit Properties... menu). See `Editable Entities` for more information.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called to change a variable and not after a variable was changed
    --- @param ent The entity being edited
    --- @param ply The player doing the editing
    --- @param key The name of the variable
    --- @param val The new value, as a string which will later be converted to its appropriate type
    --- @param editor The edit table defined in Entity:NetworkVar
    @side(server)
    VariableEdited: ((Entity, Player, string, string, { [any]: any }) -> any)?
    --- Called when you are driving a vehicle. This hook works just like `GM:Move`.
    --- This hook is called before `GM:Move` and will be called when `GM:PlayerTick` is not.
    --- @param ply Player who is driving the vehicle
    --- @param veh The vehicle being driven
    --- @param mv Move data
    @side(shared)
    VehicleMove: ((Player, Vehicle, CMoveData) -> any)?
    --- Called when user clicks on a VGUI panel.
    --- @param button The button that was pressed, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @return boolean Return true if the mouse click should be ignored or not.
    @side(client)
    VGUIMousePressAllowed: ((number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a mouse button is pressed on a VGUI element or menu.
    --- @param pnl Panel that currently has focus.
    --- @param mouseCode The key that the player pressed using Enums/MOUSE.
    @side(client)
    VGUIMousePressed: ((Panel, number) -> any)?
    --- Called as a weapon entity is picked up by a player. (Including `Player:Give`)
    --- Contrary to the name of the hook, it is **not called** when the player switches their active weapon to another.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerDroppedWeapon` and `GM:PlayerCanPickupWeapon`.
    --- **NOTE**: At the time when this hook is called `Entity:GetOwner` will return `NULL`. The owner is set on the next frame.
    --- **NOTE**: This will not be called when picking up a weapon you already have as the weapon will be removed and `WEAPON:EquipAmmo` will be called instead.
    --- @param weapon The equipped weapon.
    --- @param owner The player that is picking up the weapon.
    @side(server)
    WeaponEquip: ((Weapon, Player) -> any)?
    --- Called when an addon from the Steam workshop finishes downloading. Used by default to update details on the workshop downloading panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopDownloadedFile: ((number, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when an addon from the Steam workshop begins downloading. Used by default to place details on the workshop downloading panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param imageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param size File size of addon in bytes.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopDownloadFile: ((number, number, string, number) -> any)?
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is downloading. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param imageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param downloaded Current bytes of addon downloaded.
    --- @param expected Expected file size of addon in bytes.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopDownloadProgress: ((number, number, string, number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called after `GM:WorkshopStart`.
    --- @param remain Remaining addons to download
    --- @param total Total addons needing to be downloaded
    @side(client)
    WorkshopDownloadTotals: ((number, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when downloading content from Steam workshop ends. Used by default to hide fancy workshop downloading panel.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopEnd: (() -> any)?
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is extracting. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param ImageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param percent Current bytes of addon extracted.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopExtractProgress: ((number, number, string, number) -> any)?
    --- Called when downloading content from Steam workshop begins. Used by default to show fancy workshop downloading panel.
    --- The order of Workshop hooks is this:
    --- * WorkshopStart
    --- * WorkshopDownloadTotals
    --- * * These are called for each new item:
    --- * WorkshopDownloadFile
    --- * WorkshopDownloadProgress - This is called until the file is finished
    --- * WorkshopDownloadedFile
    --- * WorkshopEnd (this ones called once)
    @side(client)
    WorkshopStart: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when UGC subscription status changes.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopSubscriptionsChanged: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a Workshop Message is received?. Currently, it seems like the message will be **#ugc.mounting** every time.
    --- When does this exactly get called?. If an addon is subscribed, unsubscribed, error occurs or on any event?
    --- @param message The Message from the Workshop. Will be a phrase that needs to be translated.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopSubscriptionsMessage: ((string) -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called by the engine when the game initially fetches subscriptions to be displayed on the bottom of the main menu screen.
    --- @param num Amount of subscribed addons that have info retrieved.
    --- @param max Total amount of subscribed addons that need their info retrieved.
    @side(client)
    WorkshopSubscriptionsProgress: ((number, number) -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- This hook is used to add default categories to spawnmenu tool tabs.
    --- Do not override or hook this function, use `SANDBOX:AddToolMenuCategories`!
    @side(client)
    AddGamemodeToolMenuCategories: (() -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- This hook is used to add default tool tabs to spawnmenu.
    --- Do not override or hook this function, use `SANDBOX:AddToolMenuTabs`!
    @side(client)
    AddGamemodeToolMenuTabs: (() -> any)?
    --- This hook is used to add new categories to spawnmenu tool tabs.
    @side(client)
    AddToolMenuCategories: (() -> any)?
    --- This hook is used to add new tool tabs to spawnmenu.
    @side(client)
    AddToolMenuTabs: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to "arm" a duplication with the Duplicator tool. Return false to prevent the player from sending data to server, and to ignore data if it was somehow sent anyway.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to arm a dupe.
    --- @return boolean Can the player arm a dupe or not.
    --- @return string If given and the return value above is `false`, overrides the error message displayed to the player.
    @side(shared)
    CanArmDupe: ((Player) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to drive a prop via Prop Drive
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to use Prop Drive.
    --- @param ent The entity the player is attempting to drive
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow driving, false to disallow
    @side(shared)
    CanDrive: ((Player, Entity) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to fire their tool gun. Return true to specifically allow the attempt, false to block it.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to use their toolgun.
    --- @param tr A trace from the players eye to where in the world their crosshair/cursor is pointing. Returns only the `world` in the `Entity` key and returns false in the `Hit` key when the 5th argument returns `4`.
    --- @param toolname The tool mode the player currently has selected.
    --- @param tool The tool mode table the player currently has selected.
    --- @param button The tool button pressed. * `1` - left click * `2` - right click * `3` - reload * `4` - spawn menu (No interaction with the toolgun). **Client-side only**
    --- @return boolean Can use toolgun or not.
    @side(shared)
    CanTool: ((Player, TraceResult, string, { [any]: any }, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when player selects an item on the spawnmenu sidebar at the left.
    --- @param parent The panel that holds spawnicons and the sidebar of spawnmenu
    --- @param node The item player selected
    @side(client)
    ContentSidebarSelection: ((Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called when the context menu is supposedly closed.
    --- This is simply an alias of `GM:OnContextMenuClose`.
    --- This hook **will** be called even if the Sandbox's context menu doesn't actually exist, i.e. `SANDBOX:ContextMenuEnabled` blocked its creation.
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuClosed: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when the context menu is created.
    --- @param g_ContextMenu The created context menu panel
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuCreated: ((Panel) -> any)?
    --- Allows to prevent the creation of the context menu. If the context menu is already created, this will have no effect.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the context menu from being created.
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuEnabled: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the context menu is trying to be opened.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to block the opening.
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuOpen: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the context menu is supposedly opened.
    --- This is simply an alias of `GM:OnContextMenuOpen` but will **not** be called if `SANDBOX:ContextMenuOpen` prevents the context menu from opening.
    --- This hook **will** be called even if the context menu doesn't actually exist, i.e. `SANDBOX:ContextMenuEnabled` blocked its creation.
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuOpened: (() -> any)?
    --- Called to poll if active tool settings should appear in the context menu. Please note that this is only called on initial opening of the context menu, not every frame the context menu is in use.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent active tool settings from displaying in the context menu.
    @side(client)
    ContextMenuShowTool: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the Client reverts spawnlist changes
    @side(client)
    OnRevertSpawnlist: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when a player saves his changes made to the spawnmenu
    @side(client)
    OnSaveSpawnlist: (() -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- This hook is called when the player edits a category in the Spawnmenu
    @side(client)
    OpenToolbox: (() -> any)?
    --- Called from `GM:HUDPaint`; does nothing by default.
    --- **NOTE**: This cannot be used with `hook.Add`
    @side(client)
    PaintNotes: (() -> any)?
    --- Called from `GM:HUDPaint` to draw world tips. By default, enabling cl_drawworldtooltips will stop world tips from being drawn here.
    --- See `Global.AddWorldTip` for more information.
    --- **NOTE**: This cannot be used with `hook.Add`
    @side(client)
    PaintWorldTips: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when persistent props are loaded.
    --- @param name Save from which to load.
    @side(server)
    PersistenceLoad: ((string) -> any)?
    --- Called when persistent props are saved.
    --- @param name Where to save. By default is convar "sbox_persist".
    @side(server)
    PersistenceSave: ((string) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to give themselves a weapon from the Q menu. (Left mouse clicks on an icon)
    --- Not to be confused with `SANDBOX:PlayerSpawnSWEP`, which is called when the weapon is spawned as entity on the ground.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to give themselves a weapon.
    --- @param weapon Class name of the weapon the player tried to give themselves.
    --- @param spawninfo The weapon list table of this weapon, see [CCGiveSWEP](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/c3801c10e1aacc4c114d81331f301c57bdcf5a52/garrysmod/gamemodes/sandbox/gamemode/commands.lua#L893) and [weapons.Register](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/c3801c10e1aacc4c114d81331f301c57bdcf5a52/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/weapons.lua#L58)
    --- @return boolean Can the SWEP be given to the player
    @side(server)
    PlayerGiveSWEP: ((Player, string, { [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called after the player spawned an effect.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the effect
    --- @param model The model of spawned effect
    --- @param ent The spawned effect itself
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedEffect: ((Player, string, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player spawned an NPC.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the NPC
    --- @param ent The spawned NPC itself
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedNPC: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called when a player has successfully spawned a prop from the Q menu.
    --- @param ply The player who spawned a prop.
    --- @param model Path to the model of the prop the player is attempting to spawn.
    --- @param entity The entity that was spawned.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedProp: ((Player, string, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player spawned a ragdoll.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the ragdoll
    --- @param model The ragdoll model that player wants to spawn
    --- @param ent The spawned ragdoll itself
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedRagdoll: ((Player, string, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player has spawned a scripted entity.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the SENT
    --- @param ent The spawned SENT
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedSENT: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player has spawned a weapon from the spawnmenu with a middle mouse click (mouse wheel click).
    --- For a hook capable of preventing such spawns, see `SANDBOX:PlayerSpawnSWEP`.
    --- For left mouse click spawns, see `SANDBOX:PlayerGiveSWEP`.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the SWEP
    --- @param ent The SWEP itself
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedSWEP: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called after the player spawned a vehicle.
    --- @param ply The player that spawned the vehicle
    --- @param ent The vehicle itself
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnedVehicle: ((Player, Entity) -> any)?
    --- Called to ask if player allowed to spawn a particular effect or not.
    --- @param ply The player that wants to spawn an effect
    --- @param model The effect model that player wants to spawn
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow spawning that effect
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnEffect: ((Player, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to ask if player allowed to spawn a particular NPC or not.
    --- @param ply The player that wants to spawn that NPC
    --- @param npc_type The npc type that player is trying to spawn
    --- @param weapon The weapon of that NPC
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow spawning that NPC
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnNPC: ((Player, string, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to ask whether player is allowed to spawn a given model. This includes props, effects, and ragdolls and is called before the respective PlayerSpawn* hook.
    --- @param ply The player in question
    --- @param model Model path
    --- @param skin Skin number
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow the player to spawn the given model.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnObject: ((Player, string, number) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to spawn a prop from the Q menu.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to spawn a prop.
    --- @param model Path to the model of the prop the player is attempting to spawn.
    --- @return boolean Should the player be able to spawn the prop or not.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnProp: ((Player, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to spawn a ragdoll from the Q menu.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to spawn a ragdoll.
    --- @param model Path to the model of the ragdoll the player is attempting to spawn.
    --- @return boolean Should the player be able to spawn the ragdoll or not.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnRagdoll: ((Player, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to spawn an Entity from the Q menu.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to spawn the entity.
    --- @param class_ Class name of the entity the player tried to spawn.
    --- @return boolean Should the player be able to spawn the entity or not.
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnSENT: ((Player, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when a player attempts to spawn a weapon from the spawnmenu as an entity on the ground, by middle mouse clicking (mouse wheel clicking) on a weapon icon.
    --- Not to be confused with `SANDBOX:PlayerGiveSWEP`, which is called only when the weapon is given to the player directly, if they don't already have it.
    --- See `SANDBOX:PlayerSpawnedSWEP` for post entity creation event.
    --- @param ply The player who attempted to spawn a weapon.
    --- @param weapon Class name of the weapon the player tried to spawn.
    --- @param swep Information about the weapon the player is trying to spawn, see Structures/SWEP
    --- @return boolean Can the SWEP be spawned
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnSWEP: ((Player, string, { [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called to ask if player allowed to spawn a particular vehicle or not.
    --- @param ply The player that wants to spawn that vehicle
    --- @param model The vehicle model that player wants to spawn
    --- @param name Vehicle name
    --- @param table Table of that vehicle, containing info about it See Structures/VehicleTable.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow spawning that vehicle
    @side(server)
    PlayerSpawnVehicle: ((Player, string, string, { [any]: any }) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called by the spawnmenu when the content tab is generated
    --- **WARNING**: Creating an error in this Hook will result in a completely broken Content Tab
    --- @param pnlContent The SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param tree The ContentNavBar tree from the SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param node The old Spawnlists
    @side(client)
    PopulateContent: ((Panel, Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called by the spawnmenu when the Entities tab is generated
    --- **WARNING**: Creating an error in this Hook will result in a completely broken Entites Tab
    --- @param pnlContent The SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param tree The ContentNavBar tree from the SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param node The old Spawnlists
    @side(client)
    PopulateEntities: ((Panel, Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called by the spawnmenu when the NPCs tab is generated
    --- **WARNING**: Creating an error in this Hook will result in a completely broken NPCs Tab
    --- @param pnlContent The SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param tree The ContentNavBar tree from the SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param node The old Spawnlists
    @side(client)
    PopulateNPCs: ((Panel, Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- This hook makes the engine load the spawnlist text files.
    --- It calls `spawnmenu.PopulateFromEngineTextFiles` by default.
    @side(client)
    PopulatePropMenu: (() -> any)?
    --- Add the `Scripted TOOLs` to the tool menu. You want to call `spawnmenu.AddToolMenuOption` in this hook.
    @side(client)
    PopulateToolMenu: (() -> any)?
    --- Called by the spawnmenu when the Vehicles tab is generated
    --- **WARNING**: Creating an error in this Hook will result in a completely broken vehicles Tab
    --- @param pnlContent The SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param tree The ContentNavBar tree from the SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param node The old Spawnlists
    @side(client)
    PopulateVehicles: ((Panel, Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called by the spawnmenu when the Weapons tab is generated
    --- **WARNING**: Creating an error in this Hook will result in a completely broken Weapons Tab
    --- @param pnlContent The SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param tree The ContentNavBar tree from the SpawnmenuContentPanel
    --- @param node The old Spawnlists
    @side(client)
    PopulateWeapons: ((Panel, Panel, Panel) -> any)?
    --- Called right after the Lua Loaded tool menus are reloaded. This is a good place to set up any `ControlPanel`s.
    @side(client)
    PostReloadToolsMenu: (() -> any)?
    --- Called just before registering a Sandbox scripted tool.
    --- @param tool The TOOL table to be registered. See Structures/TOOL.
    --- @param class_ The class name to be assigned.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the TOOL from being registered.
    @side(shared)
    PreRegisterTOOL: (({ [any]: any }, string) -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called right before the Lua Loaded tool menus are reloaded.
    @side(client)
    PreReloadToolsMenu: (() -> any)?
    --- Called when changes were made to the spawnmenu like creating a new category.
    @side(client)
    SpawnlistContentChanged: (() -> any)?
    --- **INTERNAL**: Use `SANDBOX:SpawnmenuIconMenuOpen` if you wish to add new options to spawnmenu icon right click menus.
    --- Called when there's one or more items selected in the spawnmenu by the player, to open the multi selection right click menu (`DMenu`)
    --- @param canvas The canvas that has the selection. (Panel:GetSelectionCanvas)
    @side(client)
    SpawnlistOpenGenericMenu: ((Panel) -> any)?
    --- If false is returned then the spawn menu is never created. This saves load times if your mod doesn't actually use the spawn menu for any reason.
    --- @return boolean Whether to create spawnmenu or not.
    @side(client)
    SpawnMenuEnabled: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the player opens a context menu by right clicking one of the spawnmenu icons. Either `ContentIcon` or `SpawnIcon`.
    --- This hook can be used to add new custom menu options to the context menu.
    --- @param menu The DMenu to add options to.
    --- @param icon The ContentIcon or SpawnIcon that was right clicked. It will be a `SpawnIcon` for `model` content type, and a `ContentIcon` for all others.
    --- @param contentType The content type, such as: * `weapon` * `entity` * `vehicle` * `npc` * `model` * `tool` * `postprocess` Addon related icons may have different types.
    @side(client)
    SpawnmenuIconMenuOpen: ((Panel, Panel, string) -> any)?
    --- Called when spawnmenu is trying to be opened.
    --- **NOTE**: Hiding the spawnmenu will not stop people from being able to use the various console commands to spawn in items, etc. See GM:PlayerSpawn* hooks for blocking actual spawning.
    --- @return boolean Return false to dissallow opening the spawnmenu
    @side(client)
    SpawnMenuOpen: (() -> boolean | nil)?
    --- Called when the spawnmenu is opened.
    --- This is an alias of `GM:OnSpawnMenuOpen` but will **not** be called if `SANDBOX:SpawnMenuOpen` prevents the spawnmenu from opening.
    --- This hook **will** be called even if the spawnmenu doesn't actually exist, i.e. `SANDBOX:SpawnMenuEnabled` blocked its creation.
    @side(client)
    SpawnMenuOpened: (() -> any)?
end

--- A gamemode table: its settings and the hooks it implements.
declare interface Gamemode
    --- The fancy name of your gamemode.
    Name: string
    --- The name/contact info of the gamemode author.
    Author: string
    --- The contact email associated with the gamemode.
    Email: string
    --- The website associated with the gamemode.
    Website: string
    --- The name of the gamemode folder, automatically set.
    FolderName: string
    --- The name of the gamemode folder prepended with "gamemodes/" (such as "gamemodes/sandbox"), automatically set.
    Folder: string
    --- Set this to true if your gamemode is team-based. Used to enable/disable the base gamemode team system.
    TeamBased: boolean
    --- The name of the gamemode folder prepended with "gamemode_" (such as "gamemode_sandbox"), automatically set.
    ThisClass: string
    --- The table of the base gamemode to derive from, set automatically by Global.DeriveGamemode. It is recommended to use `Global.DEFINE_BASECLASS` when referencing the gamemode's BaseClass to prevent unintended behavior `Global.DeriveGamemode` modifies the main gamemode's BaseClass, which is shared with parent gamemodes. Because of this, in parent gamemodes the BaseClass can be incorrect, so for instance you need to use `self.BaseClass.BaseClass` in the 1st parent instead
    --- Whether the gamemode is Sandbox, or derived from Sandbox. This is not really part of the `GM` structure, and listed here only for convenience.
    IsSandboxDerived: boolean
    --- Set by GMod - The folder name of the derived gamemode (always `GM.BaseClass.FolderName` unless the `BaseClass` is the `base` gamemode) Will be `nil` if it's not derived from any gamemode / uses the `base` gamemode
    DerivedFrom: string
    --- Called when a map I/O event occurs.
    --- See also `Entity:Fire` and `Entity:Input` for functions to fire Inputs on entities.
    --- @param ent Entity that receives the input
    --- @param input The input name. Is not guaranteed to be a valid input on the entity.
    --- @param activator Activator of the input
    --- @param caller Caller of the input
    --- @param value Data provided with the input. Will be either a string, a number, a boolean or a nil.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent this input from being processed. Do not return otherwise.
    @side(server)
    method AcceptInput(ent: Entity, input: string, activator: Entity, caller: Entity, value: any): boolean | nil
    --- Adds a death notice entry.
    --- @param attacker The name of the attacker
    --- @param attackerTeam The team of the attacker
    --- @param inflictor Class name of the entity inflicting the damage
    --- @param victim Name of the victim
    --- @param victimTeam Team of the victim
    --- @return any `true/false` to prevent the notice from being shown. Do not return otherwise.
    @side(client)
    method AddDeathNotice(attacker: string, attackerTeam: number, inflictor: string, victim: string, victimTeam: number): any | nil
    --- Allows you to adjust the mouse sensitivity.
    --- @param defaultSensitivity The old sensitivity In general it will be 0, which is equivalent to a sensitivity of 1.
    --- @param localFOV Player's current FOV.
    --- @param defaultFOV Default FOV.
    --- @return number A fraction of the normal sensitivity (0.5 would be half as sensitive). Return -1 to not override and prevent subsequent hooks and WEAPON:AdjustMouseSensitivity from running. Return nil to not override and allow subsequent hooks and WEAPON:AdjustMouseSensitivity to run.
    @side(client)
    method AdjustMouseSensitivity(defaultSensitivity: number, localFOV: number, defaultFOV: number): number | nil
    --- Called when a player tries to pick up something using the "use" key, return to override.
    --- This hook will not be called if `sv_playerpickupallowed` is set to 0.
    --- See `GM:GravGunPickupAllowed` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player trying to pick up something.
    --- @param ent The Entity the player attempted to pick up.
    --- @return boolean Allow the player to pick up the entity or not.
    @side(server)
    method AllowPlayerPickup(ply: Player, ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- This hook is used to calculate animations for a player.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook must return the same values at the same time on both, client **and** server. On client for players to see the animations, on server for hit detection to work properly.
    --- @param ply The player to apply the animation.
    --- @param vel The velocity of the player.
    --- @return number Enums/ACT for the activity the player should use. A nil return will be treated as ACT_INVALID.
    --- @return number Sequence for the player to use. This takes precedence over the activity (the activity is still used for layering). Return -1 or nil to let the activity determine the sequence.
    @side(shared)
    method CalcMainActivity(ply: Player, vel: Vector): number | nil
    --- Called from `GM:CalcView` when player is in driving a vehicle.
    --- This hook may not be called in gamemodes that override `GM:CalcView`.
    --- @param veh The vehicle the player is driving
    --- @param ply The vehicle driver
    --- @param view The view data containing players FOV, view position and angles, see Structures/CamData
    --- @return { [any]: any } The modified view table containing new values, see Structures/CamData
    @side(client)
    method CalcVehicleView(veh: Vehicle, ply: Player, view: { [any]: any }): { [any]: any } | nil
    --- Allows override of the default view.
    --- **NOTE**: To avoid breaking compatibility with other addons, it is recommended to add onto the origin and angle values using `Vector:Add` or `Angle:Add` instead of overriding them completely.
    --- @param ply The local player.
    --- @param origin The player's view position.
    --- @param angles The player's view angles.
    --- @param fov Field of view.
    --- @param znear Distance to near clipping plane.
    --- @param zfar Distance to far clipping plane.
    --- @return CamData View data table. See Structures/CamData.
    @side(client)
    method CalcView(ply: Player, origin: Vector, angles: Angle, fov: number, znear: number, zfar: number): CamData | nil
    --- Allows overriding the position and angle of the viewmodel.
    --- @param wep The weapon entity
    --- @param vm The viewmodel entity
    --- @param oldPos Original position (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param oldAng Original angle (before viewmodel bobbing and swaying)
    --- @param pos Current position
    --- @param ang Current angle
    --- @return Vector New position
    --- @return Angle New angle
    @side(client)
    method CalcViewModelView(wep: Weapon, vm: Entity, oldPos: Vector, oldAng: Angle, pos: Vector, ang: Angle): Vector | nil
    --- Called whenever a players tries to create an undo.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to create something.
    --- @param undo The undo table as a Structures/Undo.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow creation of the undo.
    @side(server)
    method CanCreateUndo(ply: Player, undo: { [any]: any }): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a variable is about to be edited on an Entity (called by `Edit Properties...` menu), to determine if the edit should be permitted.
    --- See `Editable entities` for more details about the system.
    --- By default, Sandbox will also call `ENTITY:CanEditVariables` if no hook returns a value.
    --- @param ent The entity being edited.
    --- @param ply The player doing the editing.
    --- @param key The name of the variable.
    --- @param value The new value, as a string which will later be converted to its appropriate type.
    --- @param editor The edit table defined in Entity:NetworkVar.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to disallow editing.
    @side(server)
    method CanEditVariable(ent: Entity, ply: Player, key: string, value: string, editor: { [any]: any }): boolean | nil
    --- Determines if the player can exit the vehicle on their own. `Player:ExitVehicle` will bypass this hook.
    --- See `GM:CanPlayerEnterVehicle` for the opposite hook.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerLeaveVehicle` for a hook that will be called whenever a player exits any vehicle for any reason.
    --- @param veh The vehicle entity
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return boolean True if the player can exit the vehicle.
    @side(server)
    method CanExitVehicle(veh: Vehicle, ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Determines whether or not a given player player can enter the given vehicle. `Player:EnterVehicle` will still call this hook.
    --- Called just before `GM:PlayerEnteredVehicle`. See also `GM:CanExitVehicle`.
    --- @param player The player that wants to enter a vehicle.
    --- @param vehicle The vehicle in question.
    --- @param role The seat number.
    --- @return boolean `false` if the player is not allowed to enter the vehicle.
    @side(server)
    method CanPlayerEnterVehicle(player: Player, vehicle: Vehicle, role: number): boolean | nil
    --- Determines if the player can kill themselves using the `kill` or `explode` console commands.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @return boolean `true` if the player should be allowed to suicide, `false` if not.
    @side(server)
    method CanPlayerSuicide(player: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Determines if the player can unfreeze the entity.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @param entity The entity
    --- @param phys The physics object of the entity
    --- @return boolean True if they can unfreeze.
    @side(server)
    method CanPlayerUnfreeze(player: Player, entity: Entity, phys: PhysObj): boolean | nil
    --- Controls if a `property` can be used or not.
    --- @param ply Player, that tried to use the property
    --- @param property Class of the property that is tried to use, for example - bonemanipulate This is not guaranteed to be the internal property name used in `properties.Add`!
    --- @param ent The entity, on which property is tried to be used on
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow using that property
    @side(shared)
    method CanProperty(ply: Player, property: string, ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called whenever a players tries to undo.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to undo something.
    --- @param undo The undo table as a Structures/Undo.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow the undo.
    @side(server)
    method CanUndo(ply: Player, undo: Undo): boolean | nil
    --- Called each frame to record demos to video using `IVideoWriter`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called every frame regardless of whether or not a demo is being recorded
    @side(client)
    method CaptureVideo(): any
    --- Called when a message is printed to the chat box. Note, that this isn't working with player messages even though there are arguments for it.
    --- For player messages see `GM:PlayerSay` and `GM:OnPlayerChat`
    --- @param index The index of the player.
    --- @param name The name of the player.
    --- @param text The text that is being sent.
    --- @param type Chat filter type. Possible values are: * `joinleave` - Player join and leave messages * `namechange` - Player name change messages * `servermsg` - Server messages such as convar changes * `teamchange` - Team changes? * `chat` - (Obsolete?) Player chat? Seems to trigger when server console uses the `say` command * `none` - A fallback value
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress the chat message.
    @side(client)
    method ChatText(index: number, name: string, text: string, type: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called whenever the content of the user's chat input box is changed.
    --- @param text The new contents of the input box
    @side(client)
    method ChatTextChanged(text: string): any
    --- Called when a **non local player** connects to allow the Lua system to check the password.
    --- The default behaviour in the base gamemodes emulates what would normally happen. If `sv_password` is set and its value matches the password passed in by the client (via `password` concommand) - then they are allowed to join. If `sv_password` isn't set it lets them in too.
    --- @param steamID64 The 64bit Steam ID of the joining player, use util.SteamIDFrom64 to convert it to a `STEAM_0:` one.
    --- @param ipAddress The IP of the connecting client
    --- @param svPassword The current value of sv_password (the password set by the server)
    --- @param clPassword The password provided by the client
    --- @param name The name of the joining player
    --- @return boolean If the hook returns `false` then the player is disconnected
    --- @return string If returning false in the first argument, then this should be the disconnect message. This will default to `#GameUI_ServerRejectBadPassword`, which is `Bad Password.` translated to the client's language.
    @side(server)
    method CheckPassword(steamID64: string, ipAddress: string, svPassword: string, clPassword: string, name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player's sign on state changes.
    --- You cannot get a valid player object from the userID at any point during this hook.
    --- @param userID The userID of the player whose sign on state has changed.
    --- @param oldState The previous sign on state. See Enums/SIGNONSTATE enums.
    --- @param newState The new/current sign on state. See Enums/SIGNONSTATE enums.
    @side(shared)
    method ClientSignOnStateChanged(userID: number, oldState: number, newState: number): any
    --- Called when derma menus are closed with `Global.CloseDermaMenus`.
    @side(client)
    method CloseDermaMenus(): any
    --- Called whenever an entity becomes a clientside ragdoll.
    --- See `GM:CreateEntityRagdoll` for serverside ragdolls.
    --- @param entity The Entity that created the ragdoll
    --- @param ragdoll The ragdoll being created.
    @side(client)
    method CreateClientsideRagdoll(entity: Entity, ragdoll: Entity): any
    --- Called when a serverside ragdoll of an entity has been created.
    --- See `GM:CreateClientsideRagdoll` for clientside ragdolls.
    --- @param owner Entity that owns the ragdoll
    --- @param ragdoll The ragdoll entity
    @side(server)
    method CreateEntityRagdoll(owner: Entity, ragdoll: Entity): any
    --- Allows you to change the players movements before they're sent to the server.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- **NOTE**: Due to this hook being clientside only, it could be overridden by the user allowing them to completely skip your logic, it is recommended to use `GM:StartCommand` in a shared file instead.
    --- @param cmd The User Command data
    --- @return boolean Return true to: * Disable Sandbox C menu "screen clicking" * Disable Teammate nocollide (verification required) * Prevent calling of C_BaseHLPlayer::CreateMove & subsequently C_BasePlayer::CreateMove
    @side(client)
    method CreateMove(cmd: CUserCmd): boolean | nil
    --- Teams are created within this hook using `team.SetUp`.
    --- This hook is called before `GM:PreGamemodeLoaded`.
    @side(shared)
    method CreateTeams(): any
    --- Called upon an animation event, this is the ideal place to call player animation functions such as `Player:AddVCDSequenceToGestureSlot`, `Player:AnimRestartGesture` and so on.
    --- @param ply Player who is being animated
    --- @param event Animation event. See Enums/PLAYERANIMEVENT
    --- @param data The data for the event. This is interpreted as an Enums/ACT by `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM` and `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM_GESTURE`, or a sequence by `PLAYERANIMEVENT_CUSTOM_SEQUENCE`.
    --- @return number The translated activity to send to the weapon. See Enums/ACT. Return `ACT_INVALID` if you don't want to send an activity.
    @side(shared)
    method DoAnimationEvent(ply: Player, event: number, data: number | nil): number | nil
    --- Handles the player's death.
    --- This hook is **not** called if the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`. See `GM:PlayerSilentDeath` for that.
    --- * `GM:PlayerDeath` is called after this hook
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called after that
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param attacker The entity that killed the player
    --- @param dmg Damage info
    @side(server)
    method DoPlayerDeath(ply: Player, attacker: Entity, dmg: CTakeDamageInfo): any
    --- This hook is called every frame to draw all of the current death notices.
    --- @param x X position to draw death notices as a ratio
    --- @param y Y position to draw death notices as a ratio
    @side(client)
    method DrawDeathNotice(x: number, y: number): any
    --- Called every frame before drawing the in-game monitors ( Breencast, in-game TVs, etc ), but doesn't seem to be doing anything, trying to render 2D or 3D elements fail.
    @side(client)
    method DrawMonitors(): any
    --- Called after all other 2D draw hooks are called. Draws over all VGUI Panels and HUDs.
    --- Unlike `GM:HUDPaint`, this hook is called with the game paused and while the Camera SWEP is equipped.
    --- Does not get called when `r_drawvgui` is disabled.
    @side(client)
    method DrawOverlay(): any
    --- Allows you to override physgun effects rendering.
    --- **NOTE**: This is still called when `physgun_drawbeams` is set to `0`, because this hook is also capable of overriding physgun sprite effects, while the convar does not.
    --- @param ply Physgun owner
    --- @param physgun The physgun
    --- @param enabled Is the beam enabled
    --- @param target Entity we are grabbing. This will be NULL if nothing is being held
    --- @param physBone ID of the physics bone (PhysObj) we are grabbing at. Use Entity:TranslatePhysBoneToBone to translate to an actual bone.
    --- @param hitPos Beam hit position relative to the physics bone (PhysObj) we are grabbing.
    --- @return boolean Return false to hide default effects
    @side(client)
    method DrawPhysgunBeam(ply: Player, physgun: Weapon, enabled: boolean, target: Entity, physBone: number, hitPos: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Called right before an entity stops driving. Overriding this hook will cause it to not call `drive.End` and the player will not stop driving.
    --- @param ent The entity being driven
    --- @param ply The player driving the entity
    @side(shared)
    method EndEntityDriving(ent: Entity, ply: Player): any
    --- Called whenever a sound has been played. This will not be called clientside if the server played the sound without the client also calling `Entity:EmitSound`.
    --- @param data Information about the played sound. Changes done to this table can be applied by returning `true` from this hook. See Structures/EmitSoundInfo.
    --- @return boolean * Return `true` to apply all changes done to the data table. * Return `false` to prevent the sound from playing. * Return `nil` or nothing to play the sound without altering it.
    @side(shared)
    method EntityEmitSound(data: { [any]: any }): boolean | nil
    --- Called every time a bullet is about to be fired from an entity, which allows to completely modify the bullet structure before the bullet is actually fired.
    --- See `GM:PostEntityFireBullets` if you wish to hook the final bullet values, such as the aim direction post spread calculations.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called directly from `Entity:FireBullets`. Due to this, you cannot call `Entity:FireBullets` inside this hook or an infinite loop will occur crashing the game.
    --- @param entity The entity that fired the bullet
    --- @param data The bullet data. See Structures/Bullet.
    --- @return boolean * Return `true` to apply all changes done to the bullet table. * Return `false` to suppress the bullet.
    @side(shared)
    method EntityFireBullets(entity: Entity, data: Bullet): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a key-value pair is set on an entity on map spawn. Is **not** called by `Entity:SetKeyValue`.
    --- See `ENTITY:KeyValue` for a `scripted entities` hook, and its scripted weapon alternative: `WEAPON:KeyValue`.
    --- @param ent Entity that the keyvalue is being set on
    --- @param key Key of the key/value pair
    --- @param value Value of the key/value pair
    --- @return string If set, the value of the key-value pair will be overridden by this string.
    @side(shared)
    method EntityKeyValue(ent: Entity, key: string, value: string): string | nil
    --- Called when an NW2Var is changed.
    --- If a NW2Var is set on an entity that is based on a Lua Entity could result in the NW2Var being mixed up with other ones and being updated multiple times.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is fired before the client value is actually changed. Calling the GetNW2 function for the specified variable name within this hook will return the old value, not the current/updated one.
    --- This hook gets called for all NW2Vars on all Entities in a full update. The old value will be nil in this case.
    --- If this hook seems to be called for no apparent reason, check if it's caused by a full update.
    --- @param ent The owner entity of the changed NW2Var
    --- @param name The name of the changed NW2Var
    --- @param oldval The old value of the NW2Var
    --- @param newval The new value of the NW2Var
    @side(shared)
    method EntityNetworkedVarChanged(ent: Entity, name: string, oldval: any, newval: any): any
    --- Called right before removal of an entity.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called clientside during full updates due to how networking works in the Source Engine.
    --- This can happen when the client briefly loses connection to the server, and can be simulated via `cl_fullupdate` for testing purposes.
    --- @param ent Entity being removed
    --- @param fullUpdate Whether the removal is happening due to a full update clientside. The entity may or **may not** be recreated immediately after, depending on whether it is in the local player's [PVS](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). (See Entity:IsDormant)
    @side(shared)
    method EntityRemoved(ent: Entity, fullUpdate: boolean): any
    --- Called when an entity is about to take damage. You can modify all parts of the damage info in this hook or completely block the damage event.
    --- See `GM:PostEntityTakeDamage` if you wish to hook the final damage event.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the entity taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param target The entity taking damage
    --- @param dmg Detailed information about the damage event. When you retrieve "the attacker" the player's angle and position will be incorrect.
    --- @return boolean Return true to completely block the damage event
    @side(server)
    method EntityTakeDamage(target: Entity, dmg: CTakeDamageInfo): boolean | nil
    --- This hook polls the entity the player use action should be applied to.
    --- **NOTE**: The default behavior of this hook is in [CBasePlayer::FindUseEntity](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/0d8dceea4310fde5706b3ce1c70609d72a38efdf/mp/src/game/shared/baseplayer_shared.cpp#L1068-L1270). Despite CBasePlayer::FindUseEntity being defined shared, it is only called serverside in practice, so this hook will be only called serverside, as well. It is possible for modules to call it clientside, so the Lua code should still be treated as shared.
    --- @param ply The player who initiated the use action.
    --- @param defaultEnt The entity that was chosen by the engine.
    --- @return Entity The entity to use instead of default entity
    @side(shared)
    method FindUseEntity(ply: Player, defaultEnt: Entity): Entity | nil
    --- Runs when user cancels/finishes typing.
    @side(client)
    method FinishChat(): any
    --- Called after `GM:Move`, applies all the changes from the `CMoveData` to the player.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply Player
    --- @param mv Movement data
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default engine behavior, i.e. declare that you have already moved the player according to the move data in a custom way.
    @side(shared)
    method FinishMove(ply: Player, mv: CMoveData): boolean | nil
    --- Called to allow override of the default Derma skin for all panels.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is only called on Lua start up, changing its value (or adding new hooks) after it has been already called will not have any effect.
    --- **NOTE**: You can `Panel:SetSkin` "Default" (or other skins) on the frame/base panel and they will still take priority
    --- @return string A **case sensitive** Derma skin name to be used as default, registered previously via derma.DefineSkin. Returning nothing, nil or invalid name will make it fallback to the "Default" skin.
    @side(client)
    method ForceDermaSkin(): string | nil
    --- Called when game content has been changed, for example an addon or a mountable game was (un)mounted.
    @side(shared)
    method GameContentChanged(): any
    --- An internal function used to get an untranslated string to show in the kill feed as the entity's name. See `GM:SendDeathNotice`
    --- @param name The name of the entity.
    --- @return string The untranslated name for given NPC. The translation/localization would happen on the client.
    @side(server)
    method GetDeathNoticeEntityName(name: string | Entity): string | nil
    --- Called when a player takes damage from falling, allows to override the damage.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param speed The fall speed
    --- @return number New fall damage
    @side(server)
    method GetFallDamage(ply: Player, speed: number): number | nil
    --- Called when the game(server) needs to update the text shown in the server browser as the gamemode. Runs at a ~2s interval, runs even when the server is hibernating. This hook doesn't run when `hide_server 1` is set.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook (and the `sv_gamename_override` command) may not work on some popular gamemodes like DarkRP or Trouble Terrorist Town. This is not a bug, it's just how it works. See [here](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/4637#issuecomment-677884989) for more information.
    --- Also, it **only** works on dedicated servers and is called at regular intervals (about one second) **even** if the server has no players and the hibernation function is enabled.
    --- @return string The text to be shown in the server browser as the gamemode.
    @side(shared)
    method GetGameDescription(): string | nil
    --- Allows you to modify the Source Engine's motion blur shaders.
    --- @param horizontal The amount of horizontal blur.
    --- @param vertical The amount of vertical  blur.
    --- @param forward The amount of forward/radial blur.
    --- @param rotational The amount of rotational blur.
    --- @return number New amount of horizontal blur.
    --- @return number New amount of vertical blur.
    --- @return number New amount of forward/radial blur.
    --- @return number New amount of rotational blur.
    @side(client)
    method GetMotionBlurValues(horizontal: number, vertical: number, forward: number, rotational: number): number | nil
    --- Called to determine preferred carry angles for the entity. It works for both, +use pickup and gravity gun pickup.
    --- **WARNING**: Due to nature of the gravity gun coding in multiplayer, this hook **MAY** seem to not work ( but rest assured it does ), due to clientside prediction not knowing the carry angles. The +use pickup doesn't present this issue as it doesn't predict the player carrying the object clientside ( as you may notice by the prop lagging behind in multiplayer )
    --- **NOTE**: This hook can **not** override preferred carry angles of props such as the sawblade and the harpoon.
    --- @param ent The entity to generate carry angles for
    --- @param ply The player who is holding the object
    --- @return Angle The preferred carry angles for the entity.
    @side(server)
    method GetPreferredCarryAngles(ent: Entity, ply: Player): Angle | nil
    --- Returns the color for the given entity's team. This is used in chat and deathnotice text.
    --- @param ent Entity
    --- @return Color Team Color
    @side(client)
    method GetTeamColor(ent: Entity): Color | nil
    --- Returns the team color for the given team index.
    --- @param team Team index
    --- @return Color Team Color
    @side(client)
    method GetTeamNumColor(team: number): Color | nil
    --- Override this hook to disable/change ear-grabbing in your gamemode. By default, it is not called anywhere on the server.
    --- @param ply Player
    @side(shared)
    method GrabEarAnimation(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when an entity is released by a gravity gun.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunDrop` for the Physics Gun drop variant.
    --- @param ply Player who is wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity that has been dropped
    @side(server)
    method GravGunOnDropped(ply: Player, ent: Entity): any
    --- Called when an entity is picked up by a gravity gun.
    --- See `GM:OnPlayerPhysicsPickup` for the player `+use` pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity that has been picked up by the gravity gun
    @side(server)
    method GravGunOnPickedUp(ply: Player, ent: Entity): any
    --- Called every tick to poll whether a player is allowed to pick up an entity with the gravity gun or not.
    --- See `GM:AllowPlayerPickup` for the +USE pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:PhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- Calls `ENTITY:GravGunPickupAllowed` on the entity being hovered every frame in Sandbox-derived gamemodes.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity the player is attempting to pick up
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow entity pick up
    @side(server)
    method GravGunPickupAllowed(ply: Player, ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called when an entity is about to be punted with the gravity gun (primary fire).
    --- By default this function makes `ENTITY:GravGunPunt` work in Sandbox derived gamemodes.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the gravity gun
    --- @param ent The entity the player is attempting to punt
    --- @return boolean Return true to allow and false to disallow.
    @side(shared)
    method GravGunPunt(ply: Player, ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the mouse has been double clicked on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- By default this hook calls `GM:GUIMousePressed`.
    --- @param mouseCode The code of the mouse button pressed, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @param aimVector A normalized vector pointing in the direction the client has clicked
    @side(client)
    method GUIMouseDoublePressed(mouseCode: number, aimVector: Vector): any
    --- Called whenever a players presses a mouse key on the context menu in Sandbox or on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- See `GM:VGUIMousePressed` for a hook that is called on all VGUI elements.
    --- @param mouseCode The key that the player pressed using Enums/MOUSE.
    --- @param aimVector A normalized direction vector local to the camera. Internally, this is  gui.ScreenToVector( gui.MousePos() ).
    @side(client)
    method GUIMousePressed(mouseCode: number, aimVector: Vector): any
    --- Called whenever a players releases a mouse key on the context menu in Sandbox or on any panel derived from CGModBase, such as the panel used by `gui.EnableScreenClicker` and the panel used by `Panel:ParentToHUD`.
    --- @param mouseCode The key the player released, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @param aimVector A normalized direction vector local to the camera. Internally this is  gui.ScreenToVector( gui.MousePos() ).
    @side(client)
    method GUIMouseReleased(mouseCode: number, aimVector: Vector): any
    --- Called to handle player armor reduction, when player receives damage.
    --- Clarify hook order with other damage hooks.
    --- @param ply The player that took damage.
    --- @param dmginfo The taken damage.
    @side(server)
    method HandlePlayerArmorReduction(ply: Player, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo): any
    --- Allows to override player driving animations.
    --- @param ply Player to process
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerDriving(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Allows to override player crouch animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerDucking(ply: Player, velocity: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Called every frame by the player model animation system. Allows to override player jumping animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerJumping(ply: Player, velocity: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Called every frame by the player model animation system. Allows to override player landing animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @param onGround Was the player on ground?
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerLanding(ply: Player, velocity: Vector, onGround: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Allows to override player noclip animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerNoClipping(ply: Player, velocity: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Allows to override player swimming animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerSwimming(ply: Player, velocity: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Allows to override player flying ( in mid-air, not noclipping ) animations.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param velocity Players velocity
    --- @return boolean Return true if we've changed/set the animation, false otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method HandlePlayerVaulting(ply: Player, velocity: Vector): boolean | nil
    --- Hides the team selection panel.
    @side(client)
    method HideTeam(): any
    --- Called when the client has picked up ammo. Override to disable default HUD notification.
    --- @param itemName Name of the item (ammo) picked up
    --- @param amount Amount of the item (ammo) picked up
    @side(client)
    method HUDAmmoPickedUp(itemName: string, amount: number): any
    --- Renders the HUD pick-up history. Override to hide default or draw your own HUD.
    @side(client)
    method HUDDrawPickupHistory(): any
    --- Called every frame to render the scoreboard.
    --- It is recommended to use Derma and VGUI for this job instead of this hook. Called right after `GM:HUDPaint`.
    @side(client)
    method HUDDrawScoreBoard(): any
    --- Called from `GM:HUDPaint` to draw player info when you hover over a player with your crosshair or mouse.
    --- @return boolean Should the player info be drawn.
    @side(client)
    method HUDDrawTargetID(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when an item has been picked up. Override to disable the default HUD notification.
    --- @param itemName Name of the picked up item
    @side(client)
    method HUDItemPickedUp(itemName: string): any
    --- Called whenever the HUD should be drawn.
    --- This is the ideal place to draw custom HUD elements.
    --- To prevent the default game HUD from drawing, use `GM:HUDShouldDraw`.
    --- This hook does **not** get called when the Camera SWEP is held, or when the esc menu is open.
    --- If you need to draw in those situations, use `GM:DrawOverlay` instead.
    @side(client)
    method HUDPaint(): any
    --- Called before `GM:HUDPaint` when the HUD background is being drawn.
    --- Just like `GM:HUDPaint`, this hook will not be called when the main menu is visible. `GM:PostDrawHUD` does not have this behavior.
    --- Things rendered in this hook will **always** appear behind things rendered in `GM:HUDPaint`.
    @side(client)
    method HUDPaintBackground(): any
    --- Called when the Gamemode is about to draw a given element on the client's HUD (heads-up display).
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called HUNDREDS of times per second (more than 5 times per frame on average). You shouldn't be performing any computationally intensive operations. For Weapons you SHOULD use `WEAPON:HUDShouldDraw` instead.
    --- @param name The name of the HUD element. You can find a full list of HUD elements for this hook HUD_Element_List.
    --- @return boolean Return false to prevent the given element from being drawn on the client's screen.
    @side(client)
    method HUDShouldDraw(name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a weapon has been picked up. Override to disable the default HUD notification.
    --- @param weapon The picked up weapon
    @side(client)
    method HUDWeaponPickedUp(weapon: Weapon): any
    --- Called after the gamemode loads and starts.
    --- No entities would be present at the time this hook is called, please see `GM:InitPostEntity` for a one time fire hook after all map entities have been initialized.
    @side(shared)
    method Initialize(): any
    --- Called after all the entities are initialized. Starting from this hook `Global.LocalPlayer` will return valid object.
    --- **NOTE**: At this point the client only knows about the entities that are within the spawnpoints' [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). For instance, if the server sends an entity that is not within this PVS, the client will receive it as NULL entity.
    @side(shared)
    method InitPostEntity(): any
    --- Allows you to modify the supplied User Command with mouse input. This could be used to make moving the mouse do funky things to view angles.
    --- @param cmd User command.
    --- @param x The amount of mouse movement across the X axis this frame.
    --- @param y The amount of mouse movement across the Y axis this frame.
    --- @param ang The current view angle.
    --- @return boolean Return true if we modified something.
    @side(client)
    method InputMouseApply(cmd: CUserCmd, x: number, y: number, ang: Angle): boolean | nil
    --- Check if a player can spawn at a certain spawnpoint.
    --- @param ply The player who is spawned
    --- @param spawnpoint The spawnpoint entity (on the map).
    --- @param makeSuitable If this is true, it'll kill any players blocking the spawnpoint.
    --- @return boolean Return true to indicate that the spawnpoint is suitable (Allow for the player to spawn here), false to prevent spawning.
    @side(server)
    method IsSpawnpointSuitable(ply: Player, spawnpoint: Entity, makeSuitable: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called whenever a player pressed a key included within the IN keys.
    --- For a more general purpose function that handles all kinds of input, see `GM:PlayerButtonDown`.
    --- See `GM:KeyRelease` for the key release event.
    --- Despite being a predicted hook, it will still be called in singleplayer for your convenience.
    --- **WARNING**: Due to this being a predicted hook, `Global.ParticleEffect`s created only serverside from this hook will not be networked to the client, so make sure to do that on both realms.
    --- @param ply The player pressing the key. If running client-side, this will always be Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param key The key that the player pressed using Enums/IN.
    @side(shared)
    method KeyPress(ply: Player, key: number): any
    --- Runs when a IN key was released by a player.
    --- For a more general purpose function that handles all kinds of input, see `GM:PlayerButtonUp`.
    --- See `GM:KeyPress` for the key press event.
    --- Despite being a predicted hook, it will still be called in singleplayer for your convenience.
    --- @param ply The player releasing the key. If running client-side, this will always be Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param key The key that the player released using Enums/IN.
    @side(shared)
    method KeyRelease(ply: Player, key: number): any
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called from `gm_load` when the game should load a map.
    --- @param data Compressed save data
    --- @param map The name of the map the save was created on
    --- @param timestamp The time the save was created on. Will always be 0.
    @side(server)
    method LoadGModSave(data: string, map: string, timestamp: number): any
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is downloading. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param reason Failure Reason.
    --- @param workshopid the workshop ID of the missing map (if found). Can be an empty string
    @side(client)
    method LoadGModSaveFailed(reason: string, workshopid: string): any
    --- Called when `menu.lua` has finished loading.
    @side(client)
    method MenuStart(): any
    --- Override this gamemode function to disable mouth movement when talking on voice chat. By default, it is not called anywhere on the server.
    --- @param ply Player in question
    @side(shared)
    method MouthMoveAnimation(ply: Player): any
    --- The Move hook is called for you to manipulate the player's MoveData.
    --- You shouldn't adjust the player's position in any way in the move hook. This is because due to prediction errors, the netcode might run the move hook multiple times as packets arrive late. Therefore you should only adjust the movedata construct in this hook.
    --- Generally you shouldn't have to use this hook - if you want to make a custom move type you should look at the drive system.
    --- This hook is called after `GM:PlayerTick`.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply Player
    --- @param mv Movement information
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default engine action.
    @side(shared)
    method Move(ply: Player, mv: CMoveData): boolean | nil
    --- Returning true in this hook will cause it to render depth buffers defined with `render.GetResolvedFullFrameDepth`.
    --- @return boolean Render depth buffer
    @side(client)
    method NeedsDepthPass(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when an entity has been created over the network.
    --- @param ent Created entity
    @side(client)
    method NetworkEntityCreated(ent: Entity): any
    --- Called when a player's SteamID has been validated by Steam.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerAuthed` and `Player:IsFullyAuthenticated`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook doesn't work intentionally in singleplayer [because the SteamID is not validated](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/4906#issuecomment-819337130) in that case. This also applies to `sv_lan 1` servers for every duplicate `-multirun` client.
    --- @param name Player name
    --- @param steamID Player SteamID
    --- @param ownerID SteamID64 of the game license owner, in case Family Sharing is used. See also Player:OwnerSteamID64
    @side(server)
    method NetworkIDValidated(name: string, steamID: string, ownerID: string): any
    --- Called whenever this entity changes its transmission state for this `Global.LocalPlayer`, such as exiting or re entering the [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community").
    --- **NOTE**: This is the best place to handle the reset of `Entity:SetPredictable`, as this would be usually called when the player lags and requests a full packet update.
    --- When the entity stops transmitting, `Entity:IsDormant` will only return true **after** this hook.
    --- @param entity The entity that changed its transmission state.
    --- @param shouldtransmit `True` if we started transmitting to this client and `false` if we stopped.
    @side(client)
    method NotifyShouldTransmit(entity: Entity, shouldtransmit: boolean): any
    --- Called when a player has achieved an achievement. You can get the name and other information from an achievement ID with the `achievements` library.
    --- @param ply The player that earned the achievement
    --- @param achievement The index of the achievement
    @side(client)
    method OnAchievementAchieved(ply: Player, achievement: number): any
    --- Called when the local player presses TAB while having their chatbox opened.
    --- **WARNING**: This function now uses `player.Iterator`. This means it can't run all the time, as an error in the `GM:OnEntityCreated` or `GM:EntityRemoved` hooks is likely to interrupt it. Make sure that no addon causes an error in these hooks.
    --- @param text The currently typed into chatbox text
    --- @return string What should be placed into the chatbox instead of what currently is when player presses tab
    @side(client)
    method OnChatTab(text: string): string | nil
    --- Called when the player cleans up something.
    --- @param name The name of the cleanup type
    --- @return boolean Return false to suppress the cleanup notification.
    @side(client)
    method OnCleanup(name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called on the server when a Lua error occurs on a client and is sent to the server.
    --- This hook allows server-side code to detect and log client-side errors.
    --- See `GM:OnLuaError` for a hook that captures Lua errors directly within its `realm`.
    --- **WARNING**: Note that the stack argument can contain a table with 0 values.
    --- **NOTE**: Warning: the hook "protects" against lua error spam. If it has 5 errors in less than 1 second, the hook will not receive any of these 4 errors.
    --- @param error The error that occurred. As well as the path and line of the error. Example: `addons/test/lua/autorun/client/test_error.lua:4: 'then' expected near ''`
    --- @param ply The player whose client caused the error.
    --- @param stack The Lua error stack trace
    --- @param name Title of the addon that is creating the Lua errors, or "ERROR" if addon is not found.
    @side(server)
    method OnClientLuaError(error: string, ply: Player, stack: { [any]: any }, name: string): any
    --- Called when a caption/subtitle has been emitted to the closed caption box.
    --- @param soundScript The name of the soundscript, or `customLuaToken` if it's from gui.AddCaption
    --- @param duration How long the caption should stay for
    --- @param fromPlayer Is this caption coming from the player?
    --- @param fullText The caption. Can be nil if its token is not registered
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent the caption from appearing
    @side(client)
    method OnCloseCaptionEmit(soundScript: string, duration: number, fromPlayer: boolean, fullText: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the context menu keybind (+menu_context) is released, which by default is C.
    --- This hook will not run if `input.IsKeyTrapping` returns true.
    --- See also `GM:OnContextMenuOpen`.
    @side(client)
    method OnContextMenuClose(): any
    --- Called when the context menu keybind (`+menu_context`) is pressed, which by default is C.
    --- See also `GM:OnContextMenuClose`.
    @side(client)
    method OnContextMenuOpen(): any
    --- Called when the crazy physics detection detects an entity with crazy physics, i.e. position being far outside of the map, velocities being near or at infinity, etc. The primary reason for this system is to prevent program crashes in physics engine.
    --- @param ent The entity that was detected as crazy
    --- @param physobj The physics object that is going crazy
    @side(shared)
    method OnCrazyPhysics(ent: Entity, physobj: PhysObj): any
    --- Called when a player has been hurt by an explosion. Override to disable default sound effect.
    --- @param ply Player who has been hurt
    --- @param dmginfo Damage info from explosion
    @side(server)
    method OnDamagedByExplosion(ply: Player, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo): any
    --- Called as soon as the entity is created. Very little of the entity's properties will be initialized at this stage. (keyvalues, classname, flags, anything), especially on the serverside.
    --- **WARNING**: Removing the created entity during this event can lead to unexpected problems. Use `Global.SafeRemoveEntityDelayed`( entity, 0 ) to safely remove the entity.
    --- @param entity The entity
    @side(shared)
    method OnEntityCreated(entity: Entity): any
    --- Called when the `Entity:WaterLevel` of an entity is changed.
    --- 0 - The entity isn't in water.
    --- 1 - Slightly submerged (at least to the feet).
    --- 2 - The majority of the entity is submerged (at least to the waist).
    --- 3 - Completely submerged.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook can be considered a physics callback, so changing collision rules (`Entity:SetSolidFlags`) in it may lead to a crash!
    --- @param entity The entity.
    --- @param old Previous water level.
    --- @param new_ The new water level.
    @side(server)
    method OnEntityWaterLevelChanged(entity: Entity, old: number, new_: number): any
    --- Called when the gamemode is loaded. `gmod.GetGamemode` will be functional at this point.
    --- `Global.LocalPlayer`() returns NULL at the time this is run.
    @side(shared)
    method OnGamemodeLoaded(): any
    --- Called when a Lua error occurs.
    --- If you want to retrieve client errors on the server side, you can use this hook: `GM:OnClientLuaError`
    --- **NOTE**: On the `server realm`, this hook will only account for server-side errors, not client-side ones.
    --- @param error The error that occurred.
    --- @param realm Where the Lua error took place, "client", or "server"
    --- @param stack The Lua error stack trace
    --- @param name Title of the addon that is creating the Lua errors, or nil if addon is not found.
    --- @param id Steam Workshop ID of the addon creating Lua errors, if it is an addon.
    @side(shared)
    method OnLuaError(error: string, realm: string, stack: { [any]: any }, name: string, id: string): any
    --- Called when a Addon Conflict occurs, only works in the Menu realm.
    --- @param addon1 The first Addon
    --- @param addon2 The second Addon
    --- @param fileName The File the Conflict occurred in.
    @side(client)
    method OnNotifyAddonConflict(addon1: string, addon2: string, fileName: string): any
    --- Called whenever an NPC drops an item upon its death, such as health kits, armor batteries, etc.
    --- It will NOT be called for dropped weapons, with exception of Half-Life: Source NPCs, since they don't use actual weapon entities and create a weapon entity on death.
    --- `GM:PlayerDroppedWeapon` works for NPC weapon drops already. (Yes, it's not a typo)
    --- It will also not be called for live grenades spawned by Zombine.
    --- @param npc The killed NPC
    --- @param item The item that got dropped by the NPC.
    @side(server)
    method OnNPCDropItem(npc: NPC, item: Entity): any
    --- Called whenever an NPC is killed.
    --- @param npc The killed NPC
    --- @param attacker The NPCs attacker, the entity that gets the kill credit, for example a player or an NPC.
    --- @param inflictor Death inflictor. The entity that did the killing. Not necessarily a weapon.
    @side(server)
    method OnNPCKilled(npc: NPC, attacker: Entity, inflictor: Entity): any
    --- Called when the main menu has been blocked by `GM:OnPauseMenuShow` four times in a small interval. This is used internally to explain to the user that they can hold SHIFT to force open the main menu.
    @side(client)
    method OnPauseMenuBlockedTooManyTimes(): any
    --- Called when the pause menu is attempting to be opened. Allows you to prevent the main menu from being opened that time.
    --- The user can hold SHIFT to not call this hook. If the main menu is blocked multiple times in short succession, a warning will be displayed to the end user on how to bypass the hook.
    --- @return boolean Should the menu be allowed to open?
    @side(client)
    method OnPauseMenuShow(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a permission gets Granted or Revoked.
    @side(client)
    method OnPermissionsChanged(): any
    --- Called when a player freezes an entity with the physgun.
    --- @param weapon The weapon that was used to freeze the entity.
    --- @param physobj Physics object of the entity.
    --- @param ent The target entity.
    --- @param ply The player who tried to freeze the entity.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to block the unfreeze. The unfreezing is handled by the base gamemode hook. This hook has no return value, returning any value will prevent the gamemode hook from running, which is true for every hook.
    @side(server)
    method OnPhysgunFreeze(weapon: Entity, physobj: PhysObj, ent: Entity, ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called to when a player has successfully picked up an entity with their Physics Gun.
    --- Not to be confused with `GM:PhysgunPickup` which is called to ask if the player should be able to pick up an entity.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnPickedUp` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPlayerPhysicsPickup` for the player `+use` pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player that has picked up something using the physics gun.
    --- @param ent The entity that was picked up.
    @side(server)
    method OnPhysgunPickup(ply: Player, ent: Entity): any
    --- Called when a player reloads with the physgun. Override this to disable default unfreezing behavior.
    --- Regardless of whether or not you return true or false, it will disable reloading. Only returning nil/nothing will allow reloading. The intended behavior should be that returning false disables reloading.
    --- @param physgun The physgun in question.
    --- @param ply The player wielding the physgun.
    --- @return boolean Whether the player can reload with the physgun or not/
    @side(server)
    method OnPhysgunReload(physgun: Weapon, ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player has changed team using `GM:PlayerJoinTeam`.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not work with `hook.Add` and it is only called manually from `GM:PlayerJoinTeam` by the base gamemode
    --- @param ply Player who has changed team
    --- @param oldTeam Index of the team the player was originally in
    --- @param newTeam Index of the team the player has changed to
    --- @deprecated Use GM:PlayerChangedTeam instead, which works for every Player:SetTeam call.
    @side(server)
    method OnPlayerChangedTeam(ply: Player, oldTeam: number, newTeam: number): any
    --- Called whenever a player sends a chat message. For the serverside equivalent, see `GM:PlayerSay`.
    --- **NOTE**: The input (or suppression) of this hook is based on the output from `GM:PlayerSay`. Chat events suppressed serverside do not call this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param text The message's text
    --- @param teamChat Is the player typing in team chat?
    --- @param isDead Is the player dead?
    --- @return boolean Should the message be suppressed?
    @side(client)
    method OnPlayerChat(ply: Player, text: string, teamChat: boolean, isDead: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player makes contact with the ground after a jump or a fall.
    --- @param player Player
    --- @param inWater Did the player land in water?
    --- @param onFloater Did the player land on an object floating in the water?
    --- @param speed The speed at which the player hit the ground
    --- @return boolean Return true to suppress default action
    @side(shared)
    method OnPlayerHitGround(player: Entity, inWater: boolean, onFloater: boolean, speed: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player jumps.
    --- @param player Player
    --- @param speed The velocity/impulse of the jump
    @side(shared)
    method OnPlayerJump(player: Entity, speed: number): any
    --- Called when a player +use drops an entity.
    --- @param ply The player that dropped the object
    --- @param ent The object that was dropped.
    --- @param thrown Whether the object was throw or simply let go of.
    @side(server)
    method OnPlayerPhysicsDrop(ply: Player, ent: Entity, thrown: boolean): any
    --- Called when a player +use pickups up an entity. This will be called after the entity passes though `GM:AllowPlayerPickup`.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnPickedUp` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for the Physics Gun pickup variant.
    --- @param ply The player that picked up the object
    --- @param ent The object that was picked up.
    @side(server)
    method OnPlayerPhysicsPickup(ply: Player, ent: Entity): any
    --- Called when gamemode has been reloaded by auto refresh.
    --- **NOTE**: It seems that this event can be triggered more than once for a single refresh event.
    @side(shared)
    method OnReloaded(): any
    --- Called when the player's screen resolution of the game changes. This also called when changing MSAA settings.
    --- `Global.ScrW` and `Global.ScrH` will return the new values when this hook is called.
    --- @param oldWidth The previous width of the game's window.
    --- @param oldHeight The previous height of the game's window.
    --- @param newWidth The new/current width of the game's window.
    --- @param newHeight The new/current height of the game's window.
    @side(client)
    method OnScreenSizeChanged(oldWidth: number, oldHeight: number, newWidth: number, newHeight: number): any
    --- Called when a player releases the `+menu` bind on their keyboard, which is bound to Q by default.
    @side(client)
    method OnSpawnMenuClose(): any
    --- Called when a player presses the `+menu` bind on their keyboard, which is bound to Q by default.
    @side(client)
    method OnSpawnMenuOpen(): any
    --- Called when a `DTextEntry` gets focus.
    --- This hook is run from `DTextEntry:OnGetFocus` and `PANEL:OnMousePressed` of `DTextEntry`.
    --- @param panel The panel that got focus
    @side(client)
    method OnTextEntryGetFocus(panel: Panel): any
    --- Called when a `DTextEntry` loses focus.
    --- @param panel The panel that lost focus
    @side(client)
    method OnTextEntryLoseFocus(panel: Panel): any
    --- Called when the player undoes something.
    --- @param name The name of the undo action
    --- @param customText The custom text for the undo, set by undo.SetCustomUndoText
    --- @return boolean Return false to suppress the undo notification.
    @side(client)
    method OnUndo(name: string, customText: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the player changes their weapon to another one - and their viewmodel model changes.
    --- This is not always called clientside.
    --- @param viewmodel The viewmodel that is changing
    --- @param oldModel The old model
    --- @param newModel The new model
    @side(shared)
    method OnViewModelChanged(viewmodel: Entity, oldModel: string, newModel: string): any
    --- Called when a player drops an entity with the Physgun.
    --- See `GM:GravGunOnDropped` for the Gravity Gun drop variant.
    --- @param player The player who dropped an entity
    --- @param entity The dropped entity
    @side(shared)
    method PhysgunDrop(player: Player, entity: Entity): any
    --- Called to determine if a player should be able to pick up an entity with the Physics Gun.
    --- See `GM:OnPhysgunPickup` for a hook which is called when a player has successfully picked up an entity.
    --- See `GM:GravGunPickupAllowed` for the Gravity Gun pickup variant.
    --- See `GM:AllowPlayerPickup` for the `+USE` pickup variant.
    --- @param player The player that is picking up using the Physics Gun.
    --- @param entity The entity that is being picked up.
    --- @return boolean Returns whether the player can pick up the entity or not.
    @side(shared)
    method PhysgunPickup(player: Player, entity: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called after player's reserve ammo count changes.
    --- @param ply The player whose ammo is being affected.
    --- @param ammoID The ammo type ID.
    --- @param oldCount The old ammo count.
    --- @param newCount The new ammo count.
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerAmmoChanged(ply: Player, ammoID: number, oldCount: number, newCount: number): any
    --- Called after the player gets their `Player:UniqueID` set for the first time. This hook will also be called in singleplayer.
    --- See `GM:NetworkIDValidated` for a hook that is called with the player's SteamID is validated by Steam.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param steamid The player's SteamID. This will always be an empty string `""` in singleplayer.
    --- @param uniqueid The player's UniqueID. This will always be `"1"` in singleplayer.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerAuthed(ply: Player, steamid: string, uniqueid: string): any
    --- Runs when a bind has been pressed. Allows to block commands.
    --- **NOTE**: By using the "alias" console command, this hook can be effectively circumvented. To prevent this use `input.TranslateAlias`.
    --- To stop the user from using `+attack`, `+left` and any other movement commands of the sort, please look into using `GM:StartCommand` instead.
    --- The third argument will always be true.
    --- This does not run for function keys binds (F1-F12).
    --- @param ply The player who used the command; this will always be equal to Global.LocalPlayer.
    --- @param bind The bind command.
    --- @param pressed If the bind was activated or deactivated.
    --- @param code The button code. See Enums/BUTTON_CODE Enums.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent the bind.
    @side(client)
    method PlayerBindPress(ply: Player, bind: string, pressed: boolean, code: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player presses a button.
    --- This will not be called if player has a panel opened with keyboard input enabled, use `PANEL:OnKeyCodePressed` instead.
    --- See `GM:KeyPress` for an alternative that uses `Enums/IN`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerButtonUp` for the "key release" event.
    --- @param ply Player who pressed the button
    --- @param button The button, see Enums/BUTTON_CODE
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerButtonDown(ply: Player, button: number): any
    --- Called when a player releases a button.
    --- This will not be called if player has a panel opened with keyboard input enabled, use `PANEL:OnKeyCodeReleased` instead.
    --- See `GM:KeyRelease` for an alternative that uses `Enums/IN`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerButtonDown` for the "key press" event.
    --- @param ply Player who released the button
    --- @param button The button, see Enums/BUTTON_CODE
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerButtonUp(ply: Player, button: number): any
    --- Decides whether a player can hear another player using voice chat.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called **players count * speaking players count** times every 0.3 seconds if at least 1 player is talking or every 5 seconds if no one is talking.
    --- You should ensure that your code is efficient, or this will definitely influence performance.
    --- @param listener The listening player.
    --- @param talker The talking player.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` if the listener should hear the talker, `false` if they shouldn't.
    --- @return boolean 3D sound. If set to `true`, will fade out the sound the further away listener is from the  talker, the voice will also be in stereo, and not mono.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerCanHearPlayersVoice(listener: Player, talker: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to join a team
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not work with `hook.Add` and it is only called manually from `GM:PlayerJoinTeam` by the base gamemode
    --- @param ply Player attempting to switch teams
    --- @param team Index of the team
    --- @return boolean Allowed to switch
    @side(server)
    method PlayerCanJoinTeam(ply: Player, team: number): boolean | nil
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to pick an item up. (ammo, health, armor)
    --- This will typically only work for base game entities, unless mod authors that implement similar entities also manually call this hook.
    --- See `GM:PlayerCanPickupWeapon` for a hook that controls weapon pickups.
    --- @param ply Player attempting to pick up
    --- @param item The item the player is attempting to pick up
    --- @return boolean Allow pick up
    @side(server)
    method PlayerCanPickupItem(ply: Player, item: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Returns whether or not a player is allowed to pick up a weapon.
    --- If this returns `false`, `Player:Give` won't work.
    --- See `GM:PlayerCanPickupItem` for a hook that affects things like health kits, armor batteries and ammo entities.
    --- See `GM:WeaponEquip` for a hook that is called when a player successfully picks up a weapon after passing this hook.
    --- @param ply The player attempting to pick up the weapon.
    --- @param weapon The weapon entity in question.
    --- @return boolean `false` to disallow pickup.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerCanPickupWeapon(ply: Player, weapon: Weapon): boolean | nil
    --- Returns whether or not the player can see the other player's chat.
    --- **NOTE**: The **speaker** parameter does not have to be a valid `Player` object which happens when console messages are displayed for example.
    --- @param text The chat text
    --- @param teamOnly If the message is team-only
    --- @param listener The player receiving the message
    --- @param speaker The player sending the message.
    --- @return boolean Can see other player's chat
    @side(server)
    method PlayerCanSeePlayersChat(text: string, teamOnly: boolean, listener: Player, speaker: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player has changed team using `Player:SetTeam`.
    --- **WARNING**: Avoid calling `Player:SetTeam` in this hook as it may cause an infinite loop!
    --- **WARNING**: `Player:Team` inside this hook will return `oldTeam`.
    --- @param ply Player whose team has changed.
    --- @param oldTeam Index of the team the player was originally in. See team.GetName and the team library.
    --- @param newTeam Index of the team the player has changed to.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerChangedTeam(ply: Player, oldTeam: number, newTeam: number): any
    --- Called whenever a player is about to spawn something to see if they hit a limit for whatever they are spawning.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook will not be called in singleplayer, as singleplayer does not have limits.
    --- @param ply The player who is trying to spawn something.
    --- @param limitName The limit's name.
    --- @param current The amount of whatever player is trying to spawn that the player already has spawned.
    --- @param defaultMax The default maximum count, as dictated by the `sbox_max` convar on the server. This is the amount that will be used if nothing is returned from this hook.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to indicate the limit was hit, or nothing otherwise
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerCheckLimit(ply: Player, limitName: string, current: number, defaultMax: number): boolean | nil
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called whenever a player's class is changed on the server-side with `player_manager.SetPlayerClass`.
    --- @param ply The player whose class has been changed.
    --- @param newID The network ID of the player class's name string, or `0` if we are clearing a player class from the player. Pass this into util.NetworkIDToString to retrieve the proper name of the player class.
    @side(client)
    method PlayerClassChanged(ply: Player, newID: number): any
    --- Executes when a player connects to the server. Called before the player has been assigned a `UserID` and entity. See the `player_connect` gameevent for a version of this hook called after the player entity has been created.
    --- **NOTE**: This is only called clientside for listen server hosts.
    --- **NOTE**: This is not called clientside for the local player.
    --- @param name The player's name.
    --- @param ip The player's IP address. Will be "none" for bots. This argument will only be passed serverside.
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerConnect(name: string, ip: string): any
    --- Called when a player is killed by `Player:Kill` or any other normal means.
    --- This hook is **not** called if the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`. See `GM:PlayerSilentDeath` for that.
    --- * `GM:DoPlayerDeath` is called **before** this hook.
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called **after** this hook.
    --- See `Player:LastHitGroup` if you need to get the last hit hitgroup of the player.
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param victim The player who died
    --- @param inflictor Item used to kill the victim
    --- @param attacker Player or entity that killed the victim
    @side(server)
    method PlayerDeath(victim: Player, inflictor: Entity, attacker: Entity): any
    --- Returns whether or not the default death sound should be muted.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return boolean Mute death sound
    @side(server)
    method PlayerDeathSound(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called every think while the player is dead. The return value will determine if the player respawns.
    --- Overwriting this function will prevent players from respawning by pressing space or clicking.
    --- This hook is not called for players with the `FL_FROZEN` flag applied.
    --- @param ply The player affected in the hook.
    --- @return boolean This hook does not define a return value. The description below just describes how the hook library works in general. Return a non-nil value to prevent the current gamemode from handling this event. In the `base` gamemode, the gamemode handles player respawning in this hook. So blocking the gamemode hook will prevent player from respawning, in this specific case.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerDeathThink(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player leaves the server. See the `player_disconnect gameevent` for a shared version of this hook that includes the disconnect reason too.
    --- This is not called in single-player or listen servers for the host.
    --- @param ply the player
    @side(server)
    method PlayerDisconnected(ply: Player): any
    --- Called to update the player's animation during a drive.
    --- @param ply The driving player
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerDriveAnimate(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when a weapon is dropped by a player via `Player:DropWeapon`. Despite its name, this hook is also called for NPC weapon drops.
    --- Also called when a weapon is removed from a player via `Player:StripWeapon`.
    --- See also `GM:WeaponEquip` for a hook when a player picks up a weapon.
    --- The weapon's `Entity:GetOwner` will be NULL at the time this hook is called.
    --- `WEAPON:OnDrop` will be called before this hook is.
    --- @param owner The player or NPC who owned this weapon before it was dropped.
    --- @param wep The weapon that was dropped.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerDroppedWeapon(owner: Player | NPC, wep: Weapon): any
    --- Called when player stops using voice chat.
    --- See `GM:PlayerStartVoice` for the opposite hook.
    --- @param ply Player who stopped talking. Can be NULL when player entity is outside of the PVS. Use the player index.
    --- @param plyIndex The Entity:EntIndex of the talking player.
    @side(client)
    method PlayerEndVoice(ply: Player, plyIndex: number): any
    --- Called when a player enters a vehicle.
    --- Called just after `GM:CanPlayerEnterVehicle`.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerLeaveVehicle`.
    --- @param ply Player who entered vehicle.
    --- @param veh Vehicle the player entered.
    --- @param role The seat number.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerEnteredVehicle(ply: Player, veh: Vehicle, role: number): any
    --- Called before firing clientside animation events on a player model.
    --- See `GM:PlayerHandleAnimEvent` for the serverside version.
    --- @param ply The player who has triggered the event.
    --- @param pos Position of the effect
    --- @param ang Angle of the effect
    --- @param event The event ID of happened even. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events).
    --- @param name Name of the event
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable the effect
    @side(client)
    method PlayerFireAnimationEvent(ply: Player, pos: Vector, ang: Angle, event: number, name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called whenever a player steps. Return true to mute the normal sound.
    --- See `GM:PlayerStepSoundTime` for a related hook about footstep frequency.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called on all clients.
    --- @param ply The stepping player
    --- @param pos The position of the step
    --- @param foot Foot that is stepped. 0 for left, 1 for right
    --- @param sound Sound that is going to play
    --- @param volume Volume of the footstep
    --- @param filter The Recipient filter of players who can hear the footstep
    --- @return boolean Prevent default step sound
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerFootstep(ply: Player, pos: Vector, foot: number, sound: string, volume: number, filter: CRecipientFilter): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player freezes an object.
    --- @param ply Player who has frozen an object
    --- @param ent The frozen object
    --- @param physobj The frozen physics object of the frozen entity ( For ragdolls )
    @side(server)
    method PlayerFrozeObject(ply: Player, ent: Entity, physobj: PhysObj): any
    --- Called before firing serverside animation events on the player models.
    --- See `GM:PlayerFireAnimationEvent` for the clientside version.
    --- @param ply The player who has triggered the event.
    --- @param event The event ID of happened even. See [this page](http://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Animation_Events).
    --- @param eventTime The absolute time this event occurred using Global.CurTime.
    --- @param cycle The frame this event occurred as a number between 0 and 1.
    --- @param type Event type. See [the Source SDK](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/master/src/game/shared/eventlist.h#L14-L23).
    --- @param options Name or options of this event.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerHandleAnimEvent(ply: Player, event: number, eventTime: number, cycle: number, type: number, options: string): any
    --- Called when a player gets hurt.
    --- @param victim Victim
    --- @param attacker Attacker Entity
    --- @param healthRemaining Remaining Health
    --- @param damageTaken Damage Taken
    @side(server)
    method PlayerHurt(victim: Player, attacker: Entity, healthRemaining: number, damageTaken: number): any
    --- Called when the player spawns for the first time.
    --- See `GM:PlayerSpawn` for a hook called every player spawn.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called before the player has fully loaded, when the player is still in seeing the `Starting Lua` screen. For example, trying to use the `Entity:GetModel` function will return the default model (`models/player.mdl`).
    --- **WARNING**: Sending `net` messages to the spawned player in this hook may cause them to be received before the player finishes loading, for example `Global.LocalPlayer` might return NULL since `GM:InitPostEntity` may have not been called yet clientside though the net message **won't** be lost and the client still should receive it (more information here: https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-requests/issues/718).
    --- Workaround without networking:
    --- ```
    --- local load_queue = {}
    --- hook.Add( "PlayerInitialSpawn", "myAddonName/Load", function( ply )
    --- load_queue[ ply ] = true
    --- end )
    --- hook.Add( "StartCommand", "myAddonName/Load", function( ply, cmd )
    --- if load_queue[ ply ] and not cmd:IsForced() then
    --- load_queue[ ply ] = nil
    --- -- Send what you need here if it requires the client to be fully loaded!
    --- end
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- With networking:
    --- ```
    --- -- CLIENT
    --- hook.Add( "InitPostEntity", "Ready", function()
    --- net.Start( "cool_addon_client_ready" )
    --- net.SendToServer()
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- ```
    --- -- SERVER
    --- util.AddNetworkString( "cool_addon_client_ready" )
    --- net.Receive( "cool_addon_client_ready", function( len, ply )
    --- -- Send what you need here!
    --- end )
    --- ```
    --- @param player The player who spawned.
    --- @param transition If `true`, the player just spawned from a map transition.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerInitialSpawn(player: Player, transition: boolean): any
    --- Makes the player join a specified team. This is a convenience function that calls `Player:SetTeam` and runs the `GM:OnPlayerChangedTeam` hook.
    --- @param ply Player to force
    --- @param team The team to put player into
    @side(server)
    method PlayerJoinTeam(ply: Player, team: number): any
    --- Called when a player leaves a vehicle for any reason, including `Player:ExitVehicle`.
    --- See `GM:PlayerEnteredVehicle` for the opposite hook.
    --- **NOTE**: For vehicles with exit animations, this will be called **at the end** of the animation, **not at the start**!
    --- @param ply Player who left a vehicle.
    --- @param veh Vehicle the player left.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerLeaveVehicle(ply: Player, veh: Vehicle): any
    --- Called to give players the default set of weapons.
    --- **NOTE**: This function may not work in your custom gamemode if you have overridden your `GM:PlayerSpawn` and you do not use self.BaseClass.PlayerSpawn or `hook.Call`.
    --- @param ply Player to give weapons to.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerLoadout(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when a player tries to switch noclip mode.
    --- `MOVETYPE_NOCLIP` can be used to determine if a player is currently in noclip mode.
    --- @param ply The person who entered/exited noclip
    --- @param desiredState Represents the noclip state (on/off) the user will enter if this hook allows them to.
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow the switch.
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerNoClip(ply: Player, desiredState: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called after the player's think, just after `GM:FinishMove`.
    --- **NOTE**: On the client side, it is only called for the local player.
    --- @param ply The player
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerPostThink(ply: Player): any
    --- Request a player to join the team. This function will check if the team is available to join or not.
    --- This hook is called when the player runs "changeteam" in the console.
    --- To prevent the player from changing teams, see `GM:PlayerCanJoinTeam`
    --- @param ply The player to try to put into a team
    --- @param team Team to put the player into if the checks succeeded
    @side(server)
    method PlayerRequestTeam(ply: Player, team: number): any
    --- Called when a player dispatched a chat message. For the clientside equivalent, see `GM:OnPlayerChat`.
    --- **NOTE**: It may be more reliable to use `gameevent/player_say` to read messages serverside because addons commonly return values in this hook to change chat messages.
    --- @param sender The player which sent the message.
    --- @param text The message's content.
    --- @param teamChat Return false when the message is for everyone, true when the message is for the sender's team.
    --- @return string What to show instead of original text. Set to `""` to stop the message from displaying.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSay(sender: Player, text: string, teamChat: boolean): string | nil
    --- Called to determine a spawn point for a player to spawn at.
    --- **NOTE**: The spawn point entity will also impact the player's eye angle. For example, if the entity is upside down, the player's view will be as well.
    --- @param ply The player who needs a spawn point
    --- @param transition If true, the player just spawned from a map transition (`trigger_changelevel`). You probably want to not return an entity for that case to not override player's position.
    --- @return Entity The spawn point entity to spawn the player at
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSelectSpawn(ply: Player, transition: boolean): Entity | nil
    --- Find a team spawn point entity for this player.
    --- @param team Players team
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @return Entity The entity to use as a spawn point.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSelectTeamSpawn(team: number, ply: Player): Entity | nil
    --- Called whenever view model hands needs setting a model. By default this calls `PLAYER:GetHandsModel` and if that fails, sets the hands model according to his player model.
    --- @param ply The player whose hands needs a model set
    --- @param ent The hands to set model of
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSetHandsModel(ply: Player, ent: Entity): any
    --- Called whenever a player spawns and must choose a model. A good place to assign a model to a player.
    --- **NOTE**: This function may not work in your custom gamemode if you have overridden your `GM:PlayerSpawn` and you do not use `self.BaseClass.PlayerSpawn` in it, or `hook.Call` this hook from `GM:PlayerSpawn`.
    --- @param ply The player being chosen
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSetModel(ply: Player): any
    --- Returns true if the player should take damage from the given attacker.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the player taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param attacker The attacker
    --- @return boolean Allow damage
    @side(server)
    method PlayerShouldTakeDamage(ply: Player, attacker: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Allows to suppress player taunts.
    --- @param ply Player who tried to taunt
    --- @param act Act ID of the taunt player tries to do, see Enums/ACT
    --- @return boolean Return false to disallow player taunting
    @side(server)
    method PlayerShouldTaunt(ply: Player, act: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called when the player is killed by `Player:KillSilent`.
    --- The player is already considered dead when this hook is called.
    --- * See `GM:PlayerDeath` for a hook which handles all other death causes.
    --- * `GM:PostPlayerDeath` is called **after** this hook.
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return true in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player who was killed
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSilentDeath(ply: Player): any
    --- Called whenever a player spawns, including respawns.
    --- See `GM:PlayerInitialSpawn` for a hook called only the first time a player spawns.
    --- See the `player_spawn gameevent` for a shared version of this hook.
    --- **WARNING**: By default, in "base" derived gamemodes, this hook will also call `GM:PlayerLoadout` and `GM:PlayerSetModel`, which may override your `Entity:SetModel` and `Player:Give` calls. Consider using the other hooks or a 0-second timer.
    --- @param player The player who spawned.
    --- @param transition If true, the player just spawned from a map transition. You probably want to not touch player's weapons or position if this is set to `true`.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSpawn(player: Player, transition: boolean): any
    --- Called to spawn the player as a spectator.
    --- @param ply The player to spawn as a spectator
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSpawnAsSpectator(ply: Player): any
    --- Determines if the player can spray using the `impulse 201` console command.
    --- @param sprayer The player.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to allow spraying, return `true` to prevent spraying.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSpray(sprayer: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when player starts taunting.
    --- @param ply The player who is taunting
    --- @param act The sequence ID of the taunt
    --- @param length Length of the taunt
    @side(server)
    method PlayerStartTaunt(ply: Player, act: number, length: number): any
    --- Called when a player starts using voice chat.
    --- See `GM:PlayerEndVoice` for the hook when the player stops talking.
    --- **NOTE**: Set `mp_show_voice_icons` to 0, if you want disable voice chat icons above player heads.
    --- @param ply Player who started using voice chat. Can be NULL when player entity is outside of the PVS. Use the player index.
    --- @param plyIndex The Entity:EntIndex. Only appears when non-local player speaks for the first time. After August 2026 - always provided.
    @side(client)
    method PlayerStartVoice(ply: Player, plyIndex: number | nil): any
    --- Allows you to override the time between footsteps.
    --- See `GM:PlayerFootstep` for a related hook about footstep sounds themselves.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called on all clients.
    --- @param ply Player who is walking
    --- @param type The type of footsteps, see Enums/STEPSOUNDTIME
    --- @param walking Is the player walking or not ( +walk? )
    --- @return number Time between footsteps, in ms
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerStepSoundTime(ply: Player, type: number, walking: boolean): number | nil
    --- Called whenever a player attempts to either turn on or off their flashlight, returning false will deny the change.
    --- **NOTE**: Also gets called when using `Player:Flashlight`.
    --- @param ply The player who attempts to change their flashlight state.
    --- @param enabled The new state the player requested, true for on, false for off.
    --- @return boolean Can toggle the flashlight or not
    @side(server)
    method PlayerSwitchFlashlight(ply: Player, enabled: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player attempts to switch their weapon.
    --- Primary usage of this hook is to prevent/allow weapon switching, **not** to detect weapon switching. It will not be called for `Player:SetActiveWeapon`.
    --- @param player The player switching weapons.
    --- @param oldWeapon The previous weapon. Will be `NULL` if the previous weapon was removed or the player is switching from nothing.
    --- @param newWeapon The weapon the player switched to. Will be `NULL` if the player is switching to nothing. This can be `NULL` on the client if the weapon hasn't been created over the network yet.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent weapon switch.
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerSwitchWeapon(player: Player, oldWeapon: Weapon, newWeapon: Weapon): boolean | nil
    --- The Move hook is called for you to manipulate the player's `CMoveData`. This hook is called moments before `GM:Move` and `GM:PlayerNoClip`.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook will not run when inside a vehicle. `GM:VehicleMove` will be called instead.
    --- @param player The player
    --- @param mv The current movedata for the player.
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerTick(player: Player, mv: CMoveData): any
    --- Called when a player has been hit by a trace and damaged (such as from a bullet). Returning true overrides the damage handling and prevents `GM:ScalePlayerDamage` from being called.
    --- @param ply The player that has been hit
    --- @param dmginfo The damage info of the bullet
    --- @param dir Normalized vector direction of the bullet's path
    --- @param trace The trace of the bullet's path, see Structures/TraceResult
    --- @return boolean Override engine handling
    @side(shared)
    method PlayerTraceAttack(ply: Player, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo, dir: Vector, trace: TraceResult): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player unfreezes an object.
    --- @param ply Player who has unfrozen an object
    --- @param ent The unfrozen object
    --- @param physobj The frozen physics object of the unfrozen entity ( For ragdolls )
    @side(server)
    method PlayerUnfrozeObject(ply: Player, ent: Entity, physobj: PhysObj): any
    --- Triggered when the player presses use on an object. Continuously runs until USE is released but will not activate other Entities until the USE key is released; dependent on activation type of the Entity.
    --- @param ply The player pressing the "use" key.
    --- @param ent The entity which the player is looking at / activating USE on.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` if the player is not allowed to USE the entity. Do not return `true` if using a hook, otherwise other mods may not get a chance to block a player's use.
    @side(server)
    method PlayerUse(ply: Player, ent: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called when it's time to populate the context menu menu bar at the top.
    --- @param menubar The DMenuBar itself.
    @side(client)
    method PopulateMenuBar(menubar: Panel): any
    --- Called right after the map has cleaned up (usually because `game.CleanUpMap` was called)
    --- See also `GM:PreCleanupMap`.
    @side(shared)
    method PostCleanupMap(): any
    --- Called right after the 2D skybox has been drawn - allowing you to draw over it.
    @side(client)
    method PostDraw2DSkyBox(): any
    --- Called after rendering effects. This is where halos are drawn. Called just before `GM:PreDrawHUD` (The two hooks are basically identical).
    --- See `GM:PreDrawEffects` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawEffects(): any
    --- Called after `GM:PreDrawHUD`,  `GM:HUDPaintBackground` and `GM:HUDPaint` but before  `GM:DrawOverlay`.
    --- Unlike `GM:HUDPaint`(`Background`) hooks, this will still be called when the main menu is visible. And so will be `GM:PreDrawHUD`
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawHUD(): any
    --- Called after drawing opaque entities.
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawTranslucentRenderables` and `GM:PreDrawOpaqueRenderables`.
    --- @param bDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param bDrawingSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawOpaqueRenderables(bDrawingDepth: boolean, bDrawingSkybox: boolean, isDraw3DSkybox: boolean): any
    --- Called after the player hands are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for the view model alternative.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawPlayerHands` for a hook that is called just before view model hands are drawn.
    --- @param hands This is the gmod_hands entity.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity.
    --- @param ply The the owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawPlayerHands(hands: Entity, vm: Entity, ply: Player, weapon: Weapon, flags: number): any
    --- Called after drawing the 3D skybox. This will not be called if skybox rendering was prevented via the `GM:PreDrawSkyBox` hook.
    --- See also `GM:PostDraw2DSkyBox`.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawSkyBox(): any
    --- Called after all translucent entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawOpaqueRenderables` and  `GM:PreDrawTranslucentRenderables`.
    --- This is still called when r_drawentities or r_drawopaquerenderables is disabled.
    --- This is not called when r_drawtranslucentworld is disabled.
    --- @param bDrawingDepth Whether the current call is writing depth.
    --- @param bDrawingSkybox Whether the current call is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current call is drawing the 3D skybox.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawTranslucentRenderables(bDrawingDepth: boolean, bDrawingSkybox: boolean, isDraw3DSkybox: boolean): any
    --- Called after view model is drawn.
    --- The render FOV in this hook is different from the main view, as view models are usually rendered with a different FOV. Every render operation will only be accurate with the view model entity.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` for a hook that is called just before a view model is drawn.
    --- For view model hands alternative, see `GM:PostDrawPlayerHands`.
    --- @param viewmodel Players view model
    --- @param player The owner of the weapon/view model
    --- @param weapon The weapon the player is currently holding
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    method PostDrawViewModel(viewmodel: Entity, player: Player, weapon: Weapon, flags: number): any
    --- Called every time a bullet pellet (i.e. this hook is called multiple times for a shotgun shot) is fired from an entity. Notably this hook will have the final damage and aim direction for the bullet pellet.
    --- See `GM:EntityFireBullets` if you wish to modify the bullets before they are fired.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called directly from `Entity:FireBullets`. Due to this, you cannot call `Entity:FireBullets` inside this hook or an infinite loop will occur crashing the game.
    --- @param entity The entity that fired the bullet
    --- @param data A table of data about the bullet that was fired. See Structures/FiredBullet.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to suppress the bullet.
    @side(shared)
    method PostEntityFireBullets(entity: Entity, data: FiredBullet): boolean | nil
    --- Called when an entity receives a damage event, after passing damage filters, etc.
    --- See `GM:EntityTakeDamage` if you wish to prevent damage events, or otherwise alter them.
    --- **WARNING**: Applying damage from this hook to the entity taking damage will lead to infinite loop/crash.
    --- @param ent The entity that took the damage.
    --- @param dmginfo Detailed information about the damage event. When you retrieve "the attacker" the player's angle and position will be incorrect.
    --- @param wasDamageTaken Whether the entity actually took the damage. (For example, shooting a Strider will generate this event, but it won't take bullet damage).
    @side(server)
    method PostEntityTakeDamage(ent: Entity, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo, wasDamageTaken: boolean): any
    --- Called after the gamemode has loaded.
    @side(shared)
    method PostGamemodeLoaded(): any
    --- Called right after `GM:DoPlayerDeath`, `GM:PlayerDeath` and `GM:PlayerSilentDeath`.
    --- This hook will be called for all deaths, including `Player:KillSilent`
    --- **NOTE**: `Player:Alive` will return false in this hook.
    --- @param ply The player
    @side(server)
    method PostPlayerDeath(ply: Player): any
    --- Called after a given player in your [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community") was drawn.
    --- This hook will not be called if player was prevented from being drawn via `GM:PrePlayerDraw`.
    --- @param ply The player that was drawn.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    @side(client)
    method PostPlayerDraw(ply: Player, flags: number): any
    --- Allows you to suppress post processing effect drawing.
    --- @param effect_name The classname of Post Processing effect
    --- @return boolean Return true/false depending on whether this post process should be allowed
    @side(client)
    method PostProcessPermitted(effect_name: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called after the frame has been rendered. Will not be called if `GM:PreRender` returned `true`, disabling all further rendering operations for the current frame.
    @side(client)
    method PostRender(): any
    --- Called after the VGUI has been drawn.
    @side(client)
    method PostRenderVGUI(): any
    --- Called just after performing an undo.
    --- @param undo The undo table. See Structures/Undo struct.
    --- @param count The amount of props/actions undone. This will be `0` for undos that are skipped in cases where for example the entity that is meant to be undone is already deleted.
    @side(server)
    method PostUndo(undo: { [any]: any }, count: number): any
    --- Called right before the map cleans up (usually because `game.CleanUpMap` was called)
    --- See also `GM:PostCleanupMap`.
    @side(shared)
    method PreCleanupMap(): any
    --- Called just after `GM:PreDrawViewModel` and can technically be considered as a "PostDrawAllViewModels".
    --- See `GM:PostDrawEffects` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawEffects(): any
    --- Called before rendering the halos. This is the place to call `halo.Add`. This hook is actually running inside of `GM:PostDrawEffects`.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawHalos(): any
    --- Called just after `GM:PostDrawEffects` (duplicate of it). Drawing anything in it seems to work incorrectly.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawHUD` for the associated hook.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawHUD(): any
    --- Called before all opaque entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PreDrawTranslucentRenderables` and  `GM:PostDrawOpaqueRenderables`.
    --- @param isDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param isDrawSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent opaque renderables from drawing.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawOpaqueRenderables(isDrawingDepth: boolean, isDrawSkybox: boolean, isDraw3DSkybox: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called before the player hands are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` for the view model alternative.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawPlayerHands` for a hook that is called just before view model hands are drawn.
    --- @param hands This is the gmod_hands entity before it is drawn.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity before it is drawn.
    --- @param ply The the owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent the viewmodel hands from rendering
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawPlayerHands(hands: Entity, vm: Entity, ply: Player, weapon: Weapon, flags: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called before the 3D sky box is drawn. This will not be called for maps with no 3D skybox, or when the 3d skybox is disabled. (`r_3dsky 0`)
    --- See also `GM:PostDrawSkyBox`
    --- @return boolean Return true to disable skybox drawing (both 2D and 3D skybox)
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawSkyBox(): boolean | nil
    --- Called before all the translucent entities are drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PreDrawOpaqueRenderables` and  `GM:PostDrawTranslucentRenderables`.
    --- This is still called when r_drawentities or r_drawopaquerenderables is disabled.
    --- This is not called when r_drawtranslucentworld is disabled.
    --- @param isDrawingDepth Whether the current draw is writing depth.
    --- @param isDrawSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D or 2D skybox. In case of 2D skyboxes it is possible for this hook to always be called with this parameter set to `true`.
    --- @param isDraw3DSkybox Whether the current draw is drawing the 3D.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent translucent renderables from drawing.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawTranslucentRenderables(isDrawingDepth: boolean, isDrawSkybox: boolean, isDraw3DSkybox: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Called before the view model has been drawn.
    --- By default this hook also calls `WEAPON:PreDrawViewModel`, so you can use that if developing a scripted weapon.
    --- See `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for a hook that runs immediately after rendering a view model.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModels` for a hook that runs before **all** view models are drawn within a frame.
    --- For view model hands, see `GM:PreDrawPlayerHands`.
    --- @param vm This is the view model entity before it is drawn. On server-side, this entity is the predicted view model.
    --- @param ply The owner of the view model.
    --- @param weapon This is the weapon that is from the view model.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent the default view model rendering. This also affects GM:PostDrawViewModel.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawViewModel(vm: Entity, ply: Player, weapon: Weapon, flags: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called just before all view models (there are 3 per player, see `Player:GetViewModel`) and entities with `RENDERGROUP_VIEWMODEL` are drawn.
    --- See `GM:PreDrawViewModel` and `GM:PostDrawViewModel` for hooks that run for specific view models.
    --- You can use `GM:PreDrawEffects` as a "`PostDrawViewModels`" hook as it is called just after the all the view model(s) are drawn.
    @side(client)
    method PreDrawViewModels(): any
    --- Called before the gamemode is loaded.
    @side(shared)
    method PreGamemodeLoaded(): any
    --- Called before the player is drawn.
    --- See also `GM:PostPlayerDraw`.
    --- @param player The player that is about to be drawn.
    --- @param flags The Enums/STUDIO flags for this render operation.
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to prevent default player rendering, which hides the player.
    @side(client)
    method PrePlayerDraw(player: Player, flags: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called by `scripted_ents.Register`.
    --- @param ent The entity table to be registered.
    --- @param class_ The class name to be assigned.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the entity from being registered. Returning any other value has no effect.
    @side(shared)
    method PreRegisterSENT(ent: { [any]: any }, class_: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a Scripted Weapon (SWEP) is about to be registered, allowing addons to alter the weapon's SWEP table with custom data for later usage. Called internally from `weapons.Register`.
    --- @param swep The SWEP table to be registered.
    --- @param class_ The class name to be assigned.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to prevent the weapon from being registered. Returning any other value has no effect.
    @side(shared)
    method PreRegisterSWEP(swep: { [any]: any }, class_: string): boolean | nil
    --- Called before the renderer is about to start rendering the next frame.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent all rendering. This can make the whole game stop rendering anything.
    @side(client)
    method PreRender(): boolean | nil
    --- Called just before performing an undo.
    --- @param undo The undo table. See Structures/Undo struct.
    --- @return boolean Return `false` to disallow the undo.
    @side(server)
    method PreUndo(undo: { [any]: any }): boolean | nil
    --- This will prevent IN_ATTACK from sending to server when player tries to shoot from C menu.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent screen clicks.
    @side(client)
    method PreventScreenClicks(): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a prop has been destroyed.
    --- @param attacker The person who broke the prop. This can be a NULL entity for cases where the prop was not broken by a player.
    --- @param prop The entity that has been broken by the attacker.
    @side(shared)
    method PropBreak(attacker: Player, prop: Entity): any
    --- Render the scene. Used by the `Stereoscopy` post-processing effect.
    --- **NOTE**: Materials rendered in this hook require `$ignorez` parameter to draw properly.
    --- @param origin View origin
    --- @param angles View angles
    --- @param fov View FOV
    --- @return boolean Return `true` to override drawing the scene.
    @side(client)
    method RenderScene(origin: Vector, angles: Angle, fov: number): boolean | nil
    --- Used to render post processing effects.
    @side(client)
    method RenderScreenspaceEffects(): any
    --- Called when the game is reloaded from a Source Engine save system ( not the Sandbox saves or dupes ).
    --- See `GM:Saved` for a hook that is called when such a save file is created.
    @side(shared)
    method Restored(): any
    --- Called when the game is saved using the Source Engine save system (not the Sandbox saves or dupes).
    --- See `GM:Restored` for a hook that is called when such a save file is loaded.
    --- See also the `saverestore` for relevant functions.
    @side(shared)
    method Saved(): any
    --- Called when an NPC takes damage.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is called only when a specific hit group of the NPC is hit. In cases where the hitgroup doesn't matter, you should use `GM:EntityTakeDamage` instead!
    --- @param npc The NPC that takes damage
    --- @param hitgroup The hitgroup (hitbox) enum where the NPC took damage. See Enums/HITGROUP
    --- @param dmginfo Damage info
    @side(server)
    method ScaleNPCDamage(npc: NPC, hitgroup: number, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo): any
    --- This hook allows you to change how much damage a player receives when one takes damage to a specific body part.
    --- **NOTE**: This is called only for bullet damage a player receives, you should use `GM:EntityTakeDamage` instead if you need to detect **ALL** damage.
    --- @param ply The player taking damage.
    --- @param hitgroup The hitgroup where the player took damage. See Enums/HITGROUP
    --- @param dmginfo The damage info.
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent damage that this hook is called for, stop blood particle effects and blood decals. It is possible to return true only on client ( This will work **only in multiplayer** ) to stop the effects but still take damage.
    @side(shared)
    method ScalePlayerDamage(ply: Player, hitgroup: number, dmginfo: CTakeDamageInfo): boolean | nil
    --- Called when player released the scoreboard button (TAB by default).
    @side(client)
    method ScoreboardHide(): any
    --- Called when player presses the scoreboard button (TAB by default).
    --- @return boolean Return true to prevent default scoreboard from showing.
    @side(client)
    method ScoreboardShow(): boolean | nil
    --- An internal function used to send a death notice event to all clients.
    --- @param attacker The entity that caused the death.
    --- @param inflictor The attacker's weapon class name or the attacker itself if no weapon was equipped.
    --- @param victim The entity that died.
    --- @param flags Death notice flags. 1 = Friendly victim (to the player), 2 = friendly attacker (to the player)
    @side(server)
    method SendDeathNotice(attacker: Entity | string | nil, inflictor: string, victim: Entity | string, flags: number): any
    --- Sets player run and sprint speeds.
    --- Using a speed of `0` can lead to prediction errors, and can cause players to move at `sv_maxvelocity`
    --- **WARNING**: This is not a hook. Treat this as a utility function to set the player's speed.
    --- @param ply The player to set the speed of.
    --- @param walkSpeed The walk speed.
    --- @param runSpeed The run speed.
    @side(shared)
    method SetPlayerSpeed(ply: Player, walkSpeed: number, runSpeed: number): any
    --- SetupMove is called before the engine process movements. This allows us to override the players movement.
    --- See `Game Movement` for an explanation on the move system.
    --- @param ply The player whose movement we are about to process
    --- @param mv The move data to override/use
    --- @param cmd The command data
    @side(shared)
    method SetupMove(ply: Player, mv: CMoveData, cmd: CUserCmd): any
    --- Allows you to add extra positions to the player's [PVS (Potential Visibility Set)](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/PVS "PVS - Valve Developer Community"). This is the place to call `Global.AddOriginToPVS`.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param viewEntity Players Player:GetViewEntity
    @side(server)
    method SetupPlayerVisibility(ply: Player, viewEntity: Entity): any
    --- Allows you to use render.Fog* functions to manipulate skybox fog.
    --- This will not be called for maps with no 3D skybox, or when the 3d skybox is disabled. (`r_3dsky 0`)
    --- @param scale The scale of 3D skybox
    --- @return boolean Return true to tell the engine that fog is set up
    @side(client)
    method SetupSkyboxFog(scale: number): boolean | nil
    --- Allows you to use render.Fog* functions to manipulate world fog.
    --- @return boolean Return true to tell the engine that fog is set up
    @side(client)
    method SetupWorldFog(): boolean | nil
    --- Called to decide whether a pair of entities should collide with each other. This is only called if `Entity:SetCustomCollisionCheck` was used on one or both entities.
    --- Where applicable, consider using `constraint.NoCollide` or a [logic_collision_pair](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Logic_collision_pair) entity instead - they are considerably easier to use and may be more appropriate in some situations.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook **must** return the same value consistently for the same pair of entities.
    --- If an entity changed in such a way that its collision rules change, you **must** call `Entity:CollisionRulesChanged` on that entity immediately - **not in this hook and not in physics callbacks.**
    --- As long as you religiously follow the rules set by the examples this hook will work reliably without breaking, even a small mistake might break physics.
    --- This hook can cause all physics to break under certain conditions.
    --- @param ent1 The first entity in the collision poll.
    --- @param ent2 The second entity in the collision poll.
    --- @return boolean Whether the entities should collide.
    @side(shared)
    method ShouldCollide(ent1: Entity, ent2: Entity): boolean | nil
    --- Called to determine if the `Global.LocalPlayer` should be drawn.
    --- If you're using this hook to draw a player for a `GM:CalcView` hook, then you may want to consider using the `drawviewer` variable you can use in your `Structures/CamData` table instead.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook has an internal cache that is reset at the start of every frame. This will prevent this hook from running in certain cases. This cache is reset in `cam.Start` and in a future update in `render.RenderView` when rendering extra views.
    --- @param ply The player.
    --- @return boolean `true` to draw the player, `false` to hide.
    @side(client)
    method ShouldDrawLocalPlayer(ply: Player): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showhelp` console command. (Default bind is F1)
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command
    @side(server)
    method ShowHelp(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showspare1` console command ( Default bind is F3 ).
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command.
    @side(server)
    method ShowSpare1(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showspare2` console command ( Default bind is F4 ).
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command.
    @side(server)
    method ShowSpare2(ply: Player): any
    --- Called when a player executes `gm_showteam` console command. ( Default bind is F2 )
    --- @param ply Player who executed the command
    @side(server)
    method ShowTeam(ply: Player): any
    --- Called whenever the Lua environment is about to be shut down, for example on map change, or when the server is going to shut down.
    @side(shared)
    method ShutDown(): any
    --- Called when spawn icon is generated.
    --- @param lastmodel File path of previously generated model.
    --- @param imagename File path of the generated icon.
    --- @param modelsleft Amount of models left to generate.
    @side(client)
    method SpawniconGenerated(lastmodel: string, imagename: string, modelsleft: number): any
    --- Called when the Spawnmenu is Created.
    @side(client)
    method SpawnMenuCreated(): any
    --- Runs when the user tries to open the chat box.
    --- **WARNING**: Returning `true` won't stop the chatbox from taking VGUI focus. `chat.Close` may be of use to mitigate that, or usage of `GM:PlayerBindPress`.
    --- @param isTeamChat Whether the message was sent through team chat.
    --- @return boolean Return true to hide the default chat box.
    @side(client)
    method StartChat(isTeamChat: boolean): boolean | nil
    --- Allows you to change the players inputs before they are processed by the server. This function is also called for bots, making it the best solution to control them.
    --- This is basically a shared version of `GM:CreateMove`.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook is predicted, but not by usual means, it is called when a `CUserCmd` is generated on the client, and on the server when it is received, so it is necessary for this hook to be called clientside even on singleplayer
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param ucmd The usercommand
    @side(shared)
    method StartCommand(ply: Player, ucmd: CUserCmd): any
    --- Called right before an entity starts driving. Overriding this hook will cause it to not call `drive.Start` and the player will not begin driving the entity.
    --- @param ent The entity that is going to be driven
    --- @param ply The player that is going to drive the entity
    @side(shared)
    method StartEntityDriving(ent: Entity, ply: Player): any
    --- Called when you start a new game via the menu.
    @side(client)
    method StartGame(): any
    --- Called every rendered frame on client, except when the game is paused.
    --- Called every game tick on the server. This will be the same as `GM:Tick` on the server when there is no lag, but will only be called once every processed server frame during lag.
    --- `Global.CurTime` is guaranteed to be different with each call to this hook on the server.
    --- See `GM:Tick` for a hook that runs every tick on both the client and server.
    --- **NOTE**: On server, this hook **WILL NOT** run if the server is empty, unless you set the `ConVar` `sv_hibernate_think` to `1`.
    @side(shared)
    method Think(): any
    --- Called every game tick. `engine.TickCount` is guaranteed to be different between each call.
    --- Server side, this is similar to `GM:Think` (See that page for details).
    --- The default tickrate is `66.6666` (15 millisecond intervals). It can be changed via the `-tickrate` `command line option`.
    --- See `engine.TickInterval` for a function to retrieve this data at runtime.
    --- **NOTE**: This hook **WILL NOT** run if the server is empty, unless you set the `ConVar` `sv_hibernate_think` to 1
    @side(shared)
    method Tick(): any
    --- **NOTE**: Isn't called when CalcMainActivity returns a valid override sequence id
    --- Allows you to translate player activities.
    --- @param ply The player
    --- @param act The activity. See Enums/ACT
    --- @return number The new, translated activity
    @side(shared)
    method TranslateActivity(ply: Player, act: number): number | nil
    --- Animation updates (pose params etc) should be done here.
    --- @param ply The player to update the animation info for.
    --- @param velocity The player's velocity.
    --- @param maxSeqGroundSpeed Speed of the animation - used for playback rate scaling.
    @side(shared)
    method UpdateAnimation(ply: Player, velocity: Vector, maxSeqGroundSpeed: number): any
    --- Called when a variable is edited on an Entity (called by Edit Properties... menu). See `Editable Entities` for more information.
    --- **WARNING**: This hook is called to change a variable and not after a variable was changed
    --- @param ent The entity being edited
    --- @param ply The player doing the editing
    --- @param key The name of the variable
    --- @param val The new value, as a string which will later be converted to its appropriate type
    --- @param editor The edit table defined in Entity:NetworkVar
    @side(server)
    method VariableEdited(ent: Entity, ply: Player, key: string, val: string, editor: { [any]: any }): any
    --- Called when you are driving a vehicle. This hook works just like `GM:Move`.
    --- This hook is called before `GM:Move` and will be called when `GM:PlayerTick` is not.
    --- @param ply Player who is driving the vehicle
    --- @param veh The vehicle being driven
    --- @param mv Move data
    @side(shared)
    method VehicleMove(ply: Player, veh: Vehicle, mv: CMoveData): any
    --- Called when user clicks on a VGUI panel.
    --- @param button The button that was pressed, see Enums/MOUSE
    --- @return boolean Return true if the mouse click should be ignored or not.
    @side(client)
    method VGUIMousePressAllowed(button: number): boolean | nil
    --- Called when a mouse button is pressed on a VGUI element or menu.
    --- @param pnl Panel that currently has focus.
    --- @param mouseCode The key that the player pressed using Enums/MOUSE.
    @side(client)
    method VGUIMousePressed(pnl: Panel, mouseCode: number): any
    --- Called as a weapon entity is picked up by a player. (Including `Player:Give`)
    --- Contrary to the name of the hook, it is **not called** when the player switches their active weapon to another.
    --- See also `GM:PlayerDroppedWeapon` and `GM:PlayerCanPickupWeapon`.
    --- **NOTE**: At the time when this hook is called `Entity:GetOwner` will return `NULL`. The owner is set on the next frame.
    --- **NOTE**: This will not be called when picking up a weapon you already have as the weapon will be removed and `WEAPON:EquipAmmo` will be called instead.
    --- @param weapon The equipped weapon.
    --- @param owner The player that is picking up the weapon.
    @side(server)
    method WeaponEquip(weapon: Weapon, owner: Player): any
    --- Called when an addon from the Steam workshop finishes downloading. Used by default to update details on the workshop downloading panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopDownloadedFile(id: number, title: string): any
    --- Called when an addon from the Steam workshop begins downloading. Used by default to place details on the workshop downloading panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param imageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param size File size of addon in bytes.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopDownloadFile(id: number, imageID: number, title: string, size: number): any
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is downloading. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param imageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param downloaded Current bytes of addon downloaded.
    --- @param expected Expected file size of addon in bytes.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopDownloadProgress(id: number, imageID: number, title: string, downloaded: number, expected: number): any
    --- Called after `GM:WorkshopStart`.
    --- @param remain Remaining addons to download
    --- @param total Total addons needing to be downloaded
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopDownloadTotals(remain: number, total: number): any
    --- Called when downloading content from Steam workshop ends. Used by default to hide fancy workshop downloading panel.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopEnd(): any
    --- Called while an addon from the Steam workshop is extracting. Used by default to update details on the fancy workshop download panel.
    --- @param id Workshop ID of addon.
    --- @param ImageID ID of addon's preview image. For example, for **Extended Spawnmenu** addon, the image URL is ``` http://cloud-4.steamusercontent.com/ugc/702859018846106764/9E7E1946296240314751192DA0AD15B6567FF92D/ ``` So, the value of this argument would be **702859018846106764**.
    --- @param title Name of addon.
    --- @param percent Current bytes of addon extracted.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopExtractProgress(id: number, ImageID: number, title: string, percent: number): any
    --- Called when downloading content from Steam workshop begins. Used by default to show fancy workshop downloading panel.
    --- The order of Workshop hooks is this:
    --- * WorkshopStart
    --- * WorkshopDownloadTotals
    --- * * These are called for each new item:
    --- * WorkshopDownloadFile
    --- * WorkshopDownloadProgress - This is called until the file is finished
    --- * WorkshopDownloadedFile
    --- * WorkshopEnd (this ones called once)
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopStart(): any
    --- Called when UGC subscription status changes.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopSubscriptionsChanged(): any
    --- Called when a Workshop Message is received?. Currently, it seems like the message will be **#ugc.mounting** every time.
    --- When does this exactly get called?. If an addon is subscribed, unsubscribed, error occurs or on any event?
    --- @param message The Message from the Workshop. Will be a phrase that needs to be translated.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopSubscriptionsMessage(message: string): any
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- Called by the engine when the game initially fetches subscriptions to be displayed on the bottom of the main menu screen.
    --- @param num Amount of subscribed addons that have info retrieved.
    --- @param max Total amount of subscribed addons that need their info retrieved.
    @side(client)
    method WorkshopSubscriptionsProgress(num: number, max: number): any
    --- **INTERNAL**: This is used internally - although you're able to use it you probably shouldn't.
    --- This hook is used to add default categories to spawnmenu tool tabs.
