--- Don't move
declare MOVETYPE_NONE: number
--- For players, in TF2 commander view, etc
declare MOVETYPE_ISOMETRIC: number
--- Player only, moving on the ground
declare MOVETYPE_WALK: number
--- Monster/NPC movement
declare MOVETYPE_STEP: number
--- Fly, no gravity
declare MOVETYPE_FLY: number
--- Fly, with gravity
declare MOVETYPE_FLYGRAVITY: number
--- Physics movetype
declare MOVETYPE_VPHYSICS: number
--- Doesn't collide with the world, but does push and crush entities. This is what is used by the engine for elevators, trains, doors, moving water, etc. In order to work properly, the entity needs to have specific Save Values/Internal Variables set which tell it how long it should be moving for. **Note:** This same process can be done for both position and angle. 1. You'll need to `Get an existing Save Value` called `ltime` 2. Calculate how long (in seconds) the entity will be moving before it reaches its destination. As a simple example, this can be done via `duration = distance / speed` 3. `Set the Save Value` for `m_flMoveDoneTime` to the value you retrieved for `ltime` plus the duration calculated in step 2. Put more simply: `m_flMoveDoneTime = ltime + duration` 4. Set the entity's velocity to move it to the destination at the speed used in step 2. Once the duration of the move has elapsed, the entity will stop moving.  If you have done your calculations correctly, it should stop exactly at the desired destination. **NOTE**: MOVETYPE_PUSH entities only move during `Entity:Think` so if you want smooth movement, you need to set `Entity:NextThink` to `Global.CurTime`, which instructs the entity to execute `Entity:Think` as quickly as possible.
declare MOVETYPE_PUSH: number
--- Noclip
declare MOVETYPE_NOCLIP: number
--- For players, when moving on a ladder
declare MOVETYPE_LADDER: number
--- Spectator movetype. DO **NOT** use this to make player spectate
declare MOVETYPE_OBSERVER: number
--- Custom movetype, can be applied to the player to prevent the default movement code from running, while still calling the related hooks
declare MOVETYPE_CUSTOM: number
--- Error condition.
declare NAV_NONE: number
--- walk/run
declare NAV_GROUND: number
--- jump/leap
declare NAV_JUMP: number
--- can fly, move all around
declare NAV_FLY: number
--- climb ladders
declare NAV_CLIMB: number
--- The nav area is invalid.
declare NAV_MESH_INVALID: number
--- Must crouch to use this node/area
declare NAV_MESH_CROUCH: number
--- Must jump to traverse this area (only used during generation)
declare NAV_MESH_JUMP: number
--- Do not adjust for obstacles, just move along area
declare NAV_MESH_PRECISE: number
--- Inhibit discontinuity jumping
declare NAV_MESH_NO_JUMP: number
--- Must stop when entering this area
declare NAV_MESH_STOP: number
--- Must run to traverse this area
declare NAV_MESH_RUN: number
--- Must walk to traverse this area
declare NAV_MESH_WALK: number
--- Avoid this area unless alternatives are too dangerous
declare NAV_MESH_AVOID: number
--- Area may become blocked, and should be periodically checked
declare NAV_MESH_TRANSIENT: number
--- Area should not be considered for hiding spot generation
declare NAV_MESH_DONT_HIDE: number
--- Bots hiding in this area should stand
declare NAV_MESH_STAND: number
--- Hostages shouldn't use this area
declare NAV_MESH_NO_HOSTAGES: number
--- This area represents stairs, do not attempt to climb or jump them - just walk up
declare NAV_MESH_STAIRS: number
--- Don't merge this area with adjacent areas
declare NAV_MESH_NO_MERGE: number
--- This nav area is the climb point on the tip of an obstacle
declare NAV_MESH_OBSTACLE_TOP: number
--- This nav area is adjacent to a drop of at least `CliffHeight` (300 hammer units). Unused by base game.
declare NAV_MESH_CLIFF: number
--- Whether the area is blocked via `CNavArea:MarkAsBlocked`.
declare NAV_MESH_BLOCKED_LUA: number
--- Whether the area has a `prop_door_rotating` that is blocking it (because the door is closed)
declare NAV_MESH_BLOCKED_PROPDOOR: number
--- Area has designer specified cost controlled by `func_nav_cost` entities
declare NAV_MESH_FUNC_COST: number
--- Area is in an elevator's path
declare NAV_MESH_HAS_ELEVATOR: number
--- Whether the area is blocked by a `func_nav_blocker` entity and is impassible.
declare NAV_MESH_NAV_BLOCKER: number
